been doing since Second Edition.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-06-25T08:22:42-07:00","id":1320757,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1293395-ex-3-lunars-glorious-argent-beastiary-a-lunar-s-character-thread?p=1320756#post1320756\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In other words, doing what the Karmeus Bird has been doing since Second Edition.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, yeah, but y'know as a PC tactic with all the mechanics?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8959-prototype00","name":"prototype00","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8959_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"964"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-06-25T09:20:13-07:00","id":1320767,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1293395-ex-3-lunars-glorious-argent-beastiary-a-lunar-s-character-thread?p=1320756#post1320756\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">the Karmeus Bird</div> </div> </div> </div>What's that?<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-06-25T12:35:44-07:00","id":1320813,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1293395-ex-3-lunars-glorious-argent-beastiary-a-lunar-s-character-thread?p=1320767#post1320767\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What's that?</div> </div> </div> </div>It's a hideous, Wyld-mutated bird found in Nexus. They have a penchant for seizing prey, taking it up somewhere high, and dropping it onto a hard surface.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-06-28T23:35:11-07:00","id":1321467,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"font-size:14px\"><b>Aguile Ofidian</b></span><br /> <br /> <img src=\"https://www.dropbox.com/s/xg5072sy7xibkp8/db048kq-0d3c3a6f-4871-41a0-a522-de6f2efa9a8b.jpg?raw=1\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/><br /> <br /> Source: <a href=\"https://www.deviantart.com/kiguri/art/Iroun-dracotaur-665325674\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.deviantart.com/kiguri/ar...taur-665325674</a> (Please commission this individual to do Lunars Companion art!)<br /> <br /> So let me tell you about a build that uses the strongest power in Exalted.<br /> <br /> No, its not the Incarnae, nor the Primordial Wyld nor even the Charms of the Solar Exalted.<br /> <br /> Its <b>GRAVITY</b>. For your reference I append the falling environmental rules here:<br /> <br /> <u>Fall Distance, Levels, Damage Dice</u><br /> Close None None<br /> Short 3B 5B<br /> Medium 4L 7B<br /> Long 5-7L 8-12L<br /> Extreme 7-10L 10-14L<br /> <br /> So for example if you fall from Medium distance and don't have any way to halt your fall: Parachute, lucky branch, charms e.t.c., you will take 4L LEVELS of damage. That's 4 health boxes, no argument. And on top of that 7B dice of damage that IGNORE HARDNESS. Its around 7 HL basically guaranteed. Its insane.<br /> <br /> Now normally, you only get this in a fight if you push someone off a cliff or something, but what if I was to tell you that you could expose enemies to this environmental hazard at least every other round? Here are the key moving parts:<br /> <br /> 1. The Wings Mutation (so that you can take to the sky)<br /> 2. The Constrictor Mutation (so that instead of the pricey Restrain/Drag grapple maneuver, which costs two rounds of control and your action, you can just drag when you want with your reflexive move action for one round of control and save your action for like, say, Throw/Slam)<br /> <br /> Here are the Nice to Haves:<br /> <br /> 1. Legendary Size (No contest control rolls in grapple mean lots of rounds of control)<br /> 2. Grapple Enhancers<br /> 3. Some grapple enhancing Martial Arts (Falcon is the most synergistic)<br /> <br /> So without further ado, my build:<br /> <br /> <u>Aguile Ofidiano</u><br /> <br /> Caste: Full Moon<br /> Spirit Shape: Eagle/ Giant Constrictor<br /> Tell: Wings OOOOO<br /> <br /> <b>Attributes</b><br /> <br /> Physical: Primary<br /> Strength OOOOO (Favored)<br /> Dex OO<br /> Stamina OOOOO (Favored)<br /> <br /> Social: Tertiary<br /> Charisma OOOOO (Favored)<br /> Manipulation O<br /> Appearance OO<br /> <br /> Mental: Secondary<br /> Intelligence OO<br /> Wits OOOOO<br /> Perception OOO (Favored)<br /> <br /> <b>Abilities </b>(4 BP spent)<br /> <br /> Martial Arts (Falcon Style) OOOOO<br /> Athletics OOO<br /> Join Battle OOO<br /> Brawl O<br /> <br /> Anything else is more or less free choice. You have 18 dots to customize your character however you want.<br /> <br /> <b>Merits </b>(4 BP spent)<br /> <br /> Martial Arts OOOO<br /> Wings OOOOO<br /> Artifact (Moonsilver Chain Shirt) OOO<br /> Hearthstone (Sphere of the Revolutionary Dog) OO<br /> <br /> <b>Charms</b><br /> <br /> Excellencies:<br /> <br /> Strength<br /> Dexterity<br /> Stamina<br /> Charisma<br /> Appearance<br /> Perception<br /> Wits<br /> <br /> Universal:<br /> <br /> Hybrid Body Transformation: This is a key charms because it provides you access to all the mutations you need/want to become a whirlwind of grappling and slamming.<br /> <br /> Chimera Soul Expression: Just to add more mutation points to the mix. I'll now provide a list of mutations that I chose from the 12 point pool.<br /> <br /> - Constrictor OOO (As mentioned, key to moving straight up for a cheaper cost in control rounds, also allows you to move without first spending an action, this is key as we will see)<br /> - Claws OOOO (Are useful for their increased damage when you need to hit as well as the +1 defense you get as a Medium Weapon. This becomes the only medium weapon we can use with a later strength charm as we will see)<br /> - Extra Limbs / Centaur OOOOO (Against non-mounted/non heavy weapon using enemies, this is +1 to hit and + 1 to defense, all the time basically)<br /> Alternatively<br /> - Unusual Hide OOOOO (the most cost effective soak in the game)<br /> <br /> Note: I'm sure some of you are asking: Why not Beast-mode? (shapeshift into a Tyrant Lizard and be a grapple master) The simple reason is that you need a range of mutations that none of the canonical animal shapes will provide you (Until Legendary Sized beasties comes out with both Wings and Constrictor, I suppose)<br /> <br /> Strength:<br /> <br /> Deadly Claw Blow: Allows use to use our Strength for our Attack calculations for our Natural Weapons and our Unarmed strike (instead of Dex), the best thing here is that you can parry with your claws (+1 defence) and attack with your Unarmed Strike (+4 accuracy) for the best of both worlds if needed.<br /> <br /> Grizzly Bear Embrace: The first in a line of many &quot;Grapple Good&quot; Charms.<br /> <br /> Towering Beast Form: Is nice for the Tyrant Lizard form, which is a legit combat form for us, but is better because it is a pre-req for...<br /> <br /> Mountainous Spirit Expression: Essence 2 but we can pick it thanks to the Glory Sphere. This is our panic button, we basically become an unstoppable behemoth that can grapple most everything and take less damage and no onslaught from everyone at this point.<br /> <br /> Stamina:<br /> <br /> Steel Paw Style: Allows you to use Stamina instead of Dex (since we are not focusing Dex thanks to Deadly Claw Blow) for Parry Calculations, I'll do a quick rundown of total resting parry later, its quite good.<br /> <br /> Ox Body Technique: With 5 Stamina, this is as good as it's ever going to be.<br /> <br /> Appearance:<br /> <br /> Subtle Silver Declaration: Allows you to Hide your Tell, perfectly, generally useful indeed.<br /> <br /> Moon's Hidden Face: This is key. Normally HBT is a pain in the ass to activate in combat because Simple activation. But with this you can declare all your mutations Subtle for a cheap 2m and walk around with them all the time. Then, you can drop commitment reflexively on your turn in combat and guess what, Monster mode!<br /> <br /> Wits:<br /> <br /> Desert Basilisc Diadem: Just a handy, dandy socket for my Sphere of the Revolutionary Dog<br /> <br /> Radiant Basilisc Jewel: A whole raft of benefits, 4 extra mote drip per hour outside combat (useful if you want to spend all day as a giant) and a Greater Hearthstone that can't be removed. I pick the Glory Sphere, to represent our ever-upward reaching nature. This allows us to pick 1 Essence 2 charm.<br /> <br /> Dexterity:<br /> <br /> Sinuous Striking Grace: This a great charm, it gives you a virtual +5 to init each round so that basically means you can pick if you want to go first. You don't even need a high Dex to benefit from it! (Either Wits or Dex, and we have High Wits for Join Battle)<br /> <br /> Agile Beast Defense: A good workhorse charm to boost our defense.<br /> <br /> Falcon Style:<br /> <br /> Swift Talon Strike: A nice workhorse charm that gives a success to attack for 2m (pays for itself) and lets you reroll 1s on the damage roll/grapple control roll until they disappear. If you come down from a range band up to attack (this is important) you reroll 1s and 2s until they disappear. You will more or less always get the reroll 1s and 2s for reasons I will enumerate.<br /> <br /> <b>Nuts and Bolts:</b><br /> <br /> - So as you can see I left 7 BP to play around with, you could buy up more merits (like whichever of Centaur or Unusual Hide you didn't have) or max Perception or all kinds of fun stuff.<br /> <br /> - The basic (ish) scheme of combat is this:<br /> <br /> 1. You grapple someone (hopefully in Legendary Size but for weaker enemies it's not a massive deal)<br /> 2. You move up Reflexively with your move action, and your foe follows due to Constrictor. And spend 1 round of control.<br /> 3. You use the Throw/Slam action in grapple (which you can do once you've established your grapple) to decisively/witheringly throw your foe straight at the ground. Foe takes your your decisive/withering damage (depends if you want to keep your Init high) from the throw/slam and a bit of Mustard on the side in the form of 3 Bashing LEVELS of health and 5B dice of damage that ignore hardness.<br /> 4. Next turn you fly down to them and land and attack and activate Swift Talon Strike from Falcon Style for all the rerolls.<br /> 5. Repeat step 1-4.<br /> <br /> Note: If needed, as long as you have rounds of control remaining, you can keep flying up and up and access the higher ranks of falling damage, the example I provided here gives a nice 3B/5B bonus on top of your own throw/slam in the same round that the grapple is initiated, so I appreciate the efficiency.<br /> <br /> - Parry is quite good if you are a 'taur at (5 Stamina + 5 MA + 1 Specialty (Falcon Style) + 2 (Stunt Dice))/2 = 7 + 1 (Medium Weapon: Claw) + 1 (Centaur) = 9 Parry DV before even a single point of essence is spent.<br /> <br /> I'll come and put in any refinements later - charms that need to be/are nice to take are obvious in Str/Sta and Falcon Style.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":8959,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8959-prototype00","user":"prototype00","date":". 06-29-2019, 08:57 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8959-prototype00","name":"prototype00","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8959_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"964"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-06-29T02:20:36-07:00","id":1321482,"title":"","content":"Awesome build. I think you could get away without using Legendary form most of the time, but it\u2019s certainly handy to have available.<br /> <br /> Can I just say that it is Wild that a Lunar in an Ape form is totally unable to use any Martial Arts but HBTing into a Winged Centaur causes no imprediment whatsoever?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1247-maseiken","name":"Maseiken","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1247_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"170"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-06-29T02:48:30-07:00","id":1321488,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Maseiken</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1293395-ex-3-lunars-glorious-argent-beastiary-a-lunar-s-character-thread?p=1321482#post1321482\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Awesome build. I think you could get away without using Legendary form most of the time, but it\u2019s certainly handy to have available.</div> </div> </div> </div>Completely agree, this is for when Deebs want to 3v1 you or some other such numerical nonsense or you are actually fighting another Legendary Sized Creature.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Can I just say that it is Wild that a Lunar in an Ape form is totally unable to use any Martial Arts but HBTing into a Winged Centaur causes no imprediment whatsoever? </div> </div> </div>It was, a bit, I was actually thinking (based on the illustration up there) &quot;Okay... but what is she actually Lucha Libre-ing with....?&quot; <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> By the by just in case anyone was wondering about the Wings -3 to all combat actions, let me just state that you do most of your fighting/grabbing on the ground, then you go up into the air. Ironically, since no actions are rolled for throw/slam (its just a straight Init roll) you take no penalties for doing it while flying as far as I understand.<br /> <br /> prototype00","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8959-prototype00","name":"prototype00","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8959_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"964"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-06-29T07:19:37-07:00","id":1321506,"title":"","content":"It's a good tactic in white rooms where there's nothing with which to interact, but since the falling rules <i>also </i>encourage allowing a character with a good stunt to mitigate a fall with a roll, I'd argue it's hardly &quot;the strongest power in Exalted.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-06-29T07:28:11-07:00","id":1321507,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1293395-ex-3-lunars-glorious-argent-beastiary-a-lunar-s-character-thread?p=1321506#post1321506\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's a good tactic in white rooms where there's nothing with which to interact, but since the falling rules <i>also </i>encourage allowing a character with a good stunt to mitigate a fall with a roll, I'd argue it's hardly &quot;the strongest power in Exalted.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>I mean, all the mitigation seems to rely on things being there to catch you or a soft landing being available.<br /> <br /> I'm sure there will be some give and take between Storyteller and Player, but it is also well within the player's with this character's purview to say as a stunt &quot;With my Hawk-like vision, I scope out a particularly inhospitable piece of ground with no convenient outs to pancake this guy.&quot; The rules also, bless them, provide for throwing your foe into a pile of rusty knives.<br /> <br /> Another arrow in the quiver of tactics with really minimal investment over a regular Lunar Falcon Style grappler is probably no bad thing.<br /> <br /> Edit: Though just like all things, there are adverserial Storytellers ( I saw a couple on Discord) who will go out of their way to discount a combat tactic that is too out of the box for them.<br /> <br /> If so, if every locale bristles with convenient handholds to catch yourself for no good reason, I fully recommend not playing this character.<br /> <br /> Edit, second of his name: I would assume that even if they caught themselves, they would mitigate the fall damage, but not the throw/slam damage as there is nothing in the rules providing for the reduction of damage from decisive attacks short of specific charm effects. (Presumably they still land heavily enough to take that damage)<br /> <br /> Edit, the third: If it wasn't clear from the delivery, I was exaggerating the power of this tactic for comedic/entertainment value. I think it is good enough to deserve a build, to be sure, but I'm pretty sure it is just about as valid as all the other tactics in Exalted, like swording an enemy to death.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":8959,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8959-prototype00","user":"prototype00","date":". 06-29-2019, 11:16 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8959-prototype00","name":"prototype00","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8959_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"964"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-06-29T20:20:00-07:00","id":1321573,"title":"","content":"Hmm, just wondering if it would be worthwhile to splash Tiger Style OOO for Striking Fury Claws to help shore up Aguile\u2019s admittedly not the best Withering Damage...<br /> <br /> Also, what would be the best Ess 3 Charm to cheat out at the start of Ess2 with the Glory Sphere...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":8959,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8959-prototype00","user":"prototype00","date":". 06-29-2019, 11:25 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8959-prototype00","name":"prototype00","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8959_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"964"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-01T23:19:55-07:00","id":1321837,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>prototype00</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1293395-ex-3-lunars-glorious-argent-beastiary-a-lunar-s-character-thread?p=1321507#post1321507\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> If so, if every locale bristles with convenient handholds to catch yourself for no good reason, I fully recommend not playing this character.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Maybe something like:<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlie and the Great Glass Elevator</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">'Madam,' said Mr Wonka, 'it is not a lift any longer. Lifts only go up and down inside buildings. But now that it has taken us up into the sky, it has become an ELEVATOR. It is THE GREAT GLASS ELEVATOR.'<br /> 'And what keeps it up?' said Grandma Josephine. 'Skyhooks,' said Mr Wonka.</div> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1247-maseiken","name":"Maseiken","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1247_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"170"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-02T00:34:20-07:00","id":1321848,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Maseiken</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1293395-ex-3-lunars-glorious-argent-beastiary-a-lunar-s-character-thread?p=1321837#post1321837\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Maybe something like:</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, the Great Celestial Skyhook working... totally legit....<br /> <br /> Next up Tiger Tiger stylist...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8959-prototype00","name":"prototype00","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8959_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"964"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-05T11:42:09-07:00","id":1322469,"title":"","content":"BTW has any of you ever tried to actually build a Lunar that does try to make fighting in animal shapes her shtick? <br /> Because the whole attack pool thing in animal shapes, with a maximum of their pool + 1 if your stats are decent, and using the same pool for withering and decisive attacks just makes the entire endeavor seem really hamstrung to me..?<br /> Did I overlook something? Are there like a ton of animals out there with good accuracy? Did I overlook a charm that actually lets you beef up your accuracy properly, and cheaply?<br /> Admittedly, I've read Lunars only once, but still, figured someone's tried harder than me, and might be willing to share..?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/903-cheshire-cat","name":"Cheshire Cat","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar903_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"502"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-05T13:14:10-07:00","id":1322481,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cheshire Cat</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1293395-ex-3-lunars-glorious-argent-beastiary-a-lunar-s-character-thread?p=1322469#post1322469\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Because the whole attack pool thing in animal shapes, with a maximum of their pool + 1 if your stats are decent, and using the same pool for withering and decisive attacks just makes the entire endeavor seem really hamstrung to me..?</div> </div> </div> </div>It's your pool with +1 accuracy (+2 with Claws of the Silver Moon), not the animals pool. Animal pools are never a cap.<br /> <br /> With that said.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cheshire Cat</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1293395-ex-3-lunars-glorious-argent-beastiary-a-lunar-s-character-thread?p=1322469#post1322469\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">BTW has any of you ever tried to actually build a Lunar that does try to make fighting in animal shapes her shtick?</div> </div> </div> </div><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1289923-mortal-kombat-wombat-wherein-prototype00-thinks-about-lunar-animal-forms\">Yes.</a> The stuff you get access to for 2 BP of hearts blood and 4m commited is kind of ridiculous.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2579,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2579-limaxophobiac","user":"limaxophobiac","date":". 07-05-2019, 04:31 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2579-limaxophobiac","name":"limaxophobiac","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"294"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-05T13:30:12-07:00","id":1322484,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>limaxophobiac</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1293395-ex-3-lunars-glorious-argent-beastiary-a-lunar-s-character-thread?p=1322481#post1322481\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It's your pool with +1 accuracy (+2 with Claws of the Silver Moon), not the animals pool. Animal pools are never a cap.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ah lol it's my pool? That explains that. <br /> <br /> Are we sure about that, though?<br /> The book says:<br /> &quot;If her (Dexterity + Brawl) pool is higher than the attack pool for a natural weapon, her withering attacks with it gain +1 Accuracy.&quot;<br /> Kind of sounds like &quot;it&quot; could be either my attacks with my brawl pool, or with the attack pool of the natural weapon..?<br /> And still means meh accuracy with withering attacks, though admittedly much better than what I thought.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/903-cheshire-cat","name":"Cheshire Cat","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar903_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"502"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-05T17:29:49-07:00","id":1322535,"title":"","content":"Before that under the general rules for actions in animal form (which apply since attacks are actions the animal has a dice pool for) it says<br /> <br /> &quot;When she takes an action the animal has a listed dice pool for, she may use its dice pool. Any dice over her own base (Attribute + Ability) pool count as Charm dice and are subject to her dice cap (p. XX), potentially preventing her from using a form\u2019s full dice pool. <b>If the animal\u2019s pool is lower than hers, or it has no listed pool, </b><b>she may use her own dice pool</b>, although the Storyteller may assess penalties if her shape is ill-suited to that action.&quot;<br /> <br /> so you can clearly use your attribute + ability pool for them, almost certainly without penalties since saying an animals shape is ill-suitted for its own natural attacks is just weird.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2579,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2579-limaxophobiac","user":"limaxophobiac","date":". 07-05-2019, 08:32 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2579-limaxophobiac","name":"limaxophobiac","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"294"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-05T19:22:53-07:00","id":1322547,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cheshire Cat</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1293395-ex-3-lunars-glorious-argent-beastiary-a-lunar-s-character-thread?p=1322469#post1322469\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">BTW has any of you ever tried to actually build a Lunar that does try to make fighting in animal shapes her shtick?<br /> Because the whole attack pool thing in animal shapes, with a maximum of their pool + 1 if your stats are decent, and using the same pool for withering and decisive attacks just makes the entire endeavor seem really hamstrung to me..?<br /> Did I overlook something? Are there like a ton of animals out there with good accuracy? Did I overlook a charm that actually lets you beef up your accuracy properly, and cheaply?<br /> Admittedly, I've read Lunars only once, but still, figured someone's tried harder than me, and might be willing to share..?</div> </div> </div> </div>So in general analysis now that we've established that you can use either your pool or the animal's, whichever's better (and if yours is better to attack, you get +1 accuracy):<br /> <br /> 1. If you are using your own pool:<br /> - Hippo is probably the scariest opponent damage-wise for non Legendary sized shapes. Also, stupid soak for such a damaging form.<br /> - Pestletail if you want the best soak (actually has a pretty damaging attack as well)<br /> - Death Kitty, due to latents (you need 2 of them) has the best Evasion and accuracy of the strict combat forms.<br /> <br /> 2. If you are not using your own pool:<br /> - You want to aim for some accurate animal like great cat for your day-to-day<br /> - Tyrant Lizard has pools that are bigger than any possible human combination if you need a panic button and is an all round stellar shape.<br /> <br /> Other animals have more specific uses (like flight and whatnot).<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8959-prototype00","name":"prototype00","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8959_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"964"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-05T21:33:14-07:00","id":1322555,"title":"","content":"Being a cat, especially when you buy the Underfoot Menace and Stalking Shadow Hunter latent abilities, is actually hilariously powerful.<br /> <br /> For 4m committed:<ul><li>Your attack bonus, provided your dex+brawl is higher than a cat's, is 1+3 (always on Ambush Hunter)= 4, which is equal to a mortal light weapon.</li> <li>Your damage bonus is +12 for your bite, which is equal to a medium artifact weapon.</li> <li>Your evasion is increased by 2.</li> <li>If you want to hide during combat, enemies subtract 2 successes from rolls to notice you</li> <li>You Double 9s on hearing rolls to notice hidden enemies.</li> </ul><br /> However this isn't the end of the benefits you get from being a cat. Lunar charms often have Protean effects, and cats are both Tiny and have the Ambush hunter traits.<br /> <br /> Being Tiny allows the Lunar to activate a lot of defensive Dexterity charms after the opponent has rolled instead of before, which greatly increases mote efficiently. If you are hit by an attack, you activate charms until in no longer hits you.<br /> <br /> The Lunar Stealth charms in Dexterity, especially those based around Stealth in combat, have protean effects based on Tiny size or Ambush Hunter.<br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/458-indivisible","name":"Indivisible","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"41"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-05T21:46:39-07:00","id":1322556,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Indivisible</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1293395-ex-3-lunars-glorious-argent-beastiary-a-lunar-s-character-thread?p=1322555#post1322555\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Being a cat, especially when you buy the Underfoot Menace and Stalking Shadow Hunter latent abilities, is actually hilariously powerful.<br /> <br /> For 4m committed:<ul><li>Your attack bonus, provided your dex+brawl is higher than a cat's, is 1+3 (always on Ambush Hunter)= 4, which is equal to a mortal light weapon.</li> <li>Your damage bonus is +12 for your bite, which is equal to a medium artifact weapon.</li> <li>Your evasion is increased by 2.</li> <li>If you want to hide during combat, enemies subtract 2 successes from rolls to notice you</li> <li>You Double 9s on hearing rolls to notice hidden enemies.</li> </ul>However this isn't the end of the benefits you get from being a cat. Lunar charms often have Protean effects, and cats are both Tiny and have the Ambush hunter traits.<br /> <br /> Being Tiny allows the Lunar to activate a lot of defensive Dexterity charms after the opponent has rolled instead of before, which greatly increases mote efficiently. If you are hit by an attack, you activate charms until in no longer hits you.<br /> <br /> The Lunar Stealth charms in Dexterity, especially those based around Stealth in combat, have protean effects based on Tiny size or Ambush Hunter.<br /> <br /></div> </div> </div> </div>People always laugh when I tell them about Death Kitty. Who\u2019s laughing now?<br /> <br /> Edit: Tho, the damage bonus in kitty form isn\u2019t affected by strength, so it\u2019s 12 period. Like a Strength 5 Martial Artist using Unarmed. Damage is not a strong point (though a Full Moon could go 5 Str and just boost it with the Excellency).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":8959,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8959-prototype00","user":"prototype00","date":". 07-06-2019, 12:52 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8959-prototype00","name":"prototype00","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8959_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"964"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-06T03:55:07-07:00","id":1322585,"title":"","content":"Thank you guys for the answers, my confusion 90% stemmed from me reading the description in the Lunar book as them being able to use rolled actions other than attacks with their own pools, and then reading that as the +1 from having a higher pool applying to the animal's listed accuracy pool, not the Lunar's. The way you guys read it makes a lot of animal shapes very, very scary.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/903-cheshire-cat","name":"Cheshire Cat","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar903_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"502"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-07T06:26:20-07:00","id":1322769,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cheshire Cat</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1293395-ex-3-lunars-glorious-argent-beastiary-a-lunar-s-character-thread?p=1322585#post1322585\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Thank you guys for the answers, my confusion 90% stemmed from me reading the description in the Lunar book as them being able to use rolled actions other than attacks with their own pools, and then reading that as the +1 from having a higher pool applying to the animal's listed accuracy pool, not the Lunar's. The way you guys read it makes a lot of animal shapes very, very scary.</div> </div> </div> </div>Actually, this conversation has got me off my keister to work on Death Kitty (or a version there of). Changing moon (I wonder if Full Moon would be better, but TBH, fighting in animal form isn't super Attribute intensive) Ninja/Spy/Thief. Inspiration here:<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><br /> <br /> <img src=\"https://cafart.r.worldssl.net/images/Category_345/subcat_35967/J6LSXuKI_1704161948061gpadd.jpg\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/></div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Because of course, who else could it be?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8959-prototype00","name":"prototype00","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8959_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"964"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-07T06:53:17-07:00","id":1322773,"title":"","content":"Kitty is such a good stealth fighter (and just great at stealth in general) I think Changing Moons non-charm stealth dice will come in handy.<br /> <br /> For animal-form combatants No-moon also has one advantage over full-moon in that it can get back the WP for taking legendary size with its anima power once per day so can maintain it indefinitely (as long as you've got that Basilisc Jewel) without giving up daily WP regen. It's why my fabulous and extremely intimidating tyrant-lizard peacock chimera is a no-moon.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2579,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2579-limaxophobiac","user":"limaxophobiac","date":". 07-07-2019, 10:01 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2579-limaxophobiac","name":"limaxophobiac","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"294"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-07T07:08:46-07:00","id":1322776,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>limaxophobiac</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1293395-ex-3-lunars-glorious-argent-beastiary-a-lunar-s-character-thread?p=1322773#post1322773\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Kitty is such a good stealth fighter (and just great at stealth in general) I think Changing Moons non-charm stealth dice will come in handy.<br /> <br /> For animal-form combatants No-moon also has one advantage over full-moon in that it can get back the WP for taking legendary size with its anima power once per day so can maintain it indefinitely (as long as you've got that Basilisc Jewel) without giving up daily WP regen. It's why my fabulous and extremely intimidating tyrant-lizard peacock chimera is a no-moon.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm maxing Brawl (for the +1 accuracy) and Dodge (for all the evasion) but with the two latents (6bp!) thats basically all my BP. I'm going to have to build conservatively for the Attributes, methinks, and unfortunately Stealth stays at 3 (though with a belt/collar of Shadow Walking, I'm sure it's fine).<br /> <br /> But at least making an effort towards a Str excellency (for damage, +16 base isn't bad with a 3 Str only 2 off the QC Earth Deeb) and Sta Excellency (for soak, just in case, this might be a lost cause though).<br /> <br /> Edit: Ooh, point Kitty Cat, the Ambush Hunter Merit (+3 dice to attacks from stealth) should also equally apply to Decisive attacks, unlike the straight accuracy boost of normal light weapons.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":8959,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8959-prototype00","user":"prototype00","date":". 07-07-2019, 12:09 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8959-prototype00","name":"prototype00","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8959_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"964"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-07T11:22:48-07:00","id":1322813,"title":"","content":"Yah, free dice to all attacks is sweet.<br /> It might make sense to not buy latents until after character creation - they're a fairly poor bp:xp ratio.<br /> Strength-kitty can do some fun things with Last Warrior's Unity - good strength and an artifact weapon can far outpace a cat's damage, overwhelming is good, and combining a light or medium artifact weapon with ambush hunter is a lot of baseline accuracy. Plus, evocations.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23597-autxauty","name":"autXautY","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"286"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-07T17:46:59-07:00","id":1322859,"title":"","content":"Str Kitty is interesting but somewhat less Streamlined I feel, you have to be a Dawn probably to have high Str/Dex (still need Evasion!) and Sta (because everyone needs Also, you can\u2019t hide (or so I understand) tail-blade.<br /> <br /> Still, the increased Overwhelming would be nice and Claws of the Silver Moon is in Str, so good build as well.<br /> <br /> About the BP:XP split, I\u2019m going to build this character with say, 12 Lunar XP and 10 XP and ease the go burden on myself sonewhat.<br /> <br /> Where oh where to get overwhelming on this character...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":8959,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8959-prototype00","user":"prototype00","date":". 07-07-2019, 08:58 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8959-prototype00","name":"prototype00","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8959_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"964"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-07T20:30:04-07:00","id":1322878,"title":"","content":"Hmm, as always the answer is Sorcery: Wood Dragon\u2019s Claw if you know you are going to be roughing it up.<br /> <br /> Edit: Actually, just realized the answer isn\u2019t that easy, darnnit.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":8959,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8959-prototype00","user":"prototype00","date":". 07-08-2019, 12:31 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8959-prototype00","name":"prototype00","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8959_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"964"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-08T08:42:24-07:00","id":1322974,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"font-size:16px\"><b>Kylina Sele</b> <span style=\"font-size:12px\">(Note: Kylina is built with 3 sessions under her belt of shadow walking, and so she spent the 12 Lunar XP on getting one of the two latents she needs and one extra Charm)</span><br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\">Spirit Shape: Cat<br /> Tell: Silent Movement OOO</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\">Come Back Adam Warren! There's more Lunars Art to be done!</span><div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><br /> <br /> <img src=\"https://images-wixmp-ed30a86b8c4ca887773594c2.wixmp.com/f/578c2dd8-67cd-4b4e-9911-27ee707bcc19/d3gk4o8-7b7228c1-80fc-4770-b3de-de1cd242d2e9.jpg/v1/fill/w_1080,h_740,q_70,strp/exalted_s_anja_silverclaws_by_adamwarren_d3gk4o8-pre.jpg?token=eyJ0eXAiOiJKV1QiLCJhbGciOiJIUzI1NiJ9..EmOEzLhqYURGSJzaSay20LizWN2NURou5EhAnUscEMY\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/></div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\"><b>Attributes</b><br /> <br /> Physical (Secondary) (3bp spent)</span></span><br /> <br /> Strength OOO<br /> Dex OOOOO (Favored)<br /> Sta OOO<br /> <br /> Social (Primary)<br /> <br /> Charisma OO<br /> Manipulation OOOOO (Favored)<br /> Appearance OOOOO (Favored)<br /> <br /> Mental (Tertiary)<br /> <br /> Perception OO<br /> Intelligence OOO<br /> Wits OOO (Favored)<br /> <br /> <b>Abilities (8bp spent)</b><br /> <br /> Athletics OO<br /> Awareness OOO<br /> Brawl OOOOO (Specialty: Bite)<br /> Dodge OOOOO (Specialty: Small Forms)<br /> Integrity O<br /> Larceny OOO<br /> Linguistics O<br /> Occult OOO<br /> Presence OOO<br /> Socialize OOO (Specialty: Cat Got your Tongue?)<br /> Stealth OOO (Specialty: Small Forms)<br /> <br /> <b>Merits (4 bp spent)</b><br /> <br /> Artifact (Belt of Shadow Walking) OOO<br /> Heart's Blood OO<br /> Stolen Faces OO<br /> Silent Movement OOO<br /> Backing: Silver Pact O<br /> Latent: Stalking Shadow Hunter<br /> Latent: Underfoot Menace<br /> <br /> <b>Charms</b><br /> <br /> Excellencies: (Yes, she has Excellencies in all attributes. She is literally omni-capable. No, it wasn't easy, as you'll soon see)<br /> <br /> Strength<br /> Dexterity<br /> Stamina<br /> Charisma<br /> Manipulation<br /> Appearance<br /> Perception<br /> Intelligence<br /> Wits<br /> <br /> Universal:<br /> <br /> Quicksilver Second Face: Never be left without your battle form.<br /> <br /> Strength:<br /> <br /> Ferocious Biting Tooth: Eventually this will be our main source of Overwhelming, for now its merely decent, but it also gives us our Str Excellency, which we can stunt for +4 damage.<br /> <br /> Divine Predator Strike: This is <i>basically</i> also Overwhelming, and these two charms go well together to boost our damage a long with the Strength Excellency.<br /> <br /> Stamina:<br /> <br /> Impenetrable Beast Armor/Durant Quicksilver Adaptation: The wonder combination is the basis of Lunar Soak. In this case, we are hoping we don't get hit (9-10 Evasion), but if we do, this should take some of the edge off.<br /> <br /> Dexterity:<br /> <br /> Nest Raiding Slyness: What Master Thief would pass up this Heart's Blood/Stolen Faces source? Its basically what you were going to do anyway.<br /> <br /> Emerald Grasshopper Form: The Ultimate infiltration method. Enemies have a -3 success to see her at all when she uses this.<br /> <br /> Sinuous Striking Grace: One of the top tier Dex Offense Charms as go first and free dice is always nice.<br /> <br /> Agile Beast Defense: Our 1m workhorse will always give us +1 to Evasion and we can apply it after we see what our foe rolls (if it isn't 9, don't bother)<br /> <br /> Bending Before the Storm: Our Onslaught Negator.<br /> <br /> Charisma:<br /> <br /> Argent Songbird Voice: Our omni-applicable success-on-social actions generator.<br /> <br /> Debt of Borrowed Skin: Our altruistic method of stealing other people's faces. A thief with a heart of gold, indeed.<br /> <br /> Perception:<br /> <br /> Perceiving the Hidden World: Not only does this let us see immaterial, as a Cat we auto-detect out to Long Range!<br /> <br /> Spirit Rending Fury: For 1 mote per attack, this lets us attack with impunity with the Belt of Shadow Walking if the enemy can't strike Immaterial.<br /> <br /> Intelligence:<br /> <br /> Memory Drinking Meditation: If you ever replace someone and don't want their spouse to suspect, accept no substitutes. Also super good at collecting information on others (just steal the faces of those around them and reap the intel).<br /> <br /> Terrestrial Circle Sorcery: No need to belabour the usefulness here. I chose Mists of Eventide as a Control Spell as it will serve you well in stealthy infiltrations if you can put people to sleep and they can't see where it is coming from.<br /> <br /> <b>Finale:</b><br /> <br /> So there you have it, Kylina is more or less done. She is great at basically everything (thanks Excellencies) and superlative in a few areas:<br /> <br /> - Stealth: With her 14 pool (5 Dex + 3 Stealth + 1 Specialty + 3 Belt of Shadow Walking + 2 Stunt) and her ability to eat 2 successes from enemies trying to detect her (4 if they are trying to do it by hearing!) without spending a single mote, Kylina is an infiltrator of the highest calibre (she eats 3 successes if she wants to go tiny)<br /> <br /> - Fighting - As stated before, she has the highest accuracy and highest Evasion of any animal form thanks to merits and latents. Damage is a bit lackluster, but hopefully the strength Excellency (+16 damage with that, which is considerable) and the Strength Charms cover for her a bit. Her Soak is always going to be bad, but I did not know of a way to fix that. *sigh* glass cannon it is then.<br /> <br /> - Femme-fataling. Look at that Manipulation and Appearance, look at it! I wasn't even able to get Charms in these two attributes, but they are favored anyway. Just go out there and make men and women melt.<br /> <br /> I'm sure there are lots of ways I could have built her better, why not take the time to tell me? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> Always welcome comments!<br /> <br /> Edit: For all that effort, she has basically the same Defense as Aguile one page prior. Full Moons, man, Full Moons.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":8959,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8959-prototype00","user":"prototype00","date":". 07-08-2019, 11:59 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8959-prototype00","name":"prototype00","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8959_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"964"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-08T14:36:48-07:00","id":1323056,"title":"","content":"Thoughts<br /> Very nice omni-capability.<br /> I think last warrior's unity might be good for a cat even without high strength - for Kylina, an artifact light weapon gives +4 accuracy, +1 damage, +2 overwhelming, and potentially a tag (smashing might be the best, for delicious 21 dice no-mote smashing attacks)<br /> Artifact moonsilver armor can boost your soak, though you need light armor to avoid penalties to evasion.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23597-autxauty","name":"autXautY","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"286"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-08T16:42:23-07:00","id":1323075,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>autXautY</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1293395-ex-3-lunars-glorious-argent-beastiary-a-lunar-s-character-thread?p=1323056#post1323056\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Thoughts<br /> Very nice omni-capability.<br /> I think last warrior's unity might be good for a cat even without high strength - for Kylina, an artifact light weapon gives +4 accuracy, +1 damage, +2 overwhelming, and potentially a tag (smashing might be the best, for delicious 21 dice no-mote smashing attacks)<br /> Artifact moonsilver armor can boost your soak, though you need light armor to avoid penalties to evasion.</div> </div> </div> </div>Hmm, actually I was just thinking about the artifact weapon with Wood Dragon's Claw, lot more versatile tag wise and it's not like someone is going to notice if you are going all ninja-kitty. You couldn't use your hands for stuff anyway as a cat. And it would stack with the bonus from Underfoot Menace, and you get to cut one latent, which is huge. I'll think about it.<br /> <br /> So 5 Dex + 5 Brawl + 1 Specialty + 3 Ambush Hunter/Underfoot Menace + 4 Accuracy + 2 Stunt = 20 dice to withering attacks without even having to spend a mote and 13 damage (raising to 17 with Str Excellency) *sigh* you are right, its better than the bite.<br /> <br /> Can you use Wood Dragon's Claw as a cat?<br /> <br /> Artifact Moonsilver Armor<br /> <br /> This on the other hand I was grappling with, it just seems too obvious with not a good way to remove it if needed (Wood dragon's Claw you can just dismiss and re-summon) as a cat. I dunno. Would having a resting EV of 9, raising to 12 with mote expenditure be enough to avoid most damage?<br /> <br /> prototype00","signature":"","edited":{"userid":8959,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8959-prototype00","user":"prototype00","date":". 07-08-2019, 08:28 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8959-prototype00","name":"prototype00","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8959_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"964"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-08T17:47:17-07:00","id":1323086,"title":"","content":"Wood Dragon's Claw is a reasonable replacement for an artifact weapon, I think. I don't see why you couldn't use it as a cat. And has +5 accuracy, not +4.<br /> Actually, the overwhelming might be almost a bigger boost than the damage - one of the scariest things for this build is someone with 15+soak, because gaining initiative will take you forever, and one hit loses it all.<br /> <br /> Yah, armor does have sneakiness issues. Potentially you could get an evocation to hide/disguise it? Many Pockets Meditation + Quicksilver Armor Approach can don hidden armor in a turn, but several charms and motes is a bit expensive.<br /> <br /> Alternatively, at Essence 2: Perfect Hybrid Interaction (Unusual Hide). Or find a mutated cat and eat it. Or find a cat, mutate it with Sharing Luna's Gifts, and steal it's food while taunting it.<br /> Or, if you're going for sorcery: Invulnerable Skin of Bronze: +6 soak, and an extra +essence if you aren't wearing armor.<br /> <br /> EV is mostly good enough, but someone if an enemy solar throws 28 dice at you, or an enemy sidereal throws 21 dice with TN 4 at you, you'll want soak. Even if they just send 16 dice at you, you'd rather not choose between a slight chance of taking 10+ dice of withering damage, or spending 6m straight to prevent the hit.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23597-autxauty","name":"autXautY","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"286"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-08T21:05:56-07:00","id":1323118,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>autXautY</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1293395-ex-3-lunars-glorious-argent-beastiary-a-lunar-s-character-thread?p=1323086#post1323086\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Wood Dragon's Claw is a reasonable replacement for an artifact weapon, I think. I don't see why you couldn't use it as a cat. And has +5 accuracy, not +4.<br /> Actually, the overwhelming might be almost a bigger boost than the damage - one of the scariest things for this build is someone with 15+soak, because gaining initiative will take you forever, and one hit loses it all.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, true and I\u2019ve got both Str charms and an arifact weapon to grant overwhelming.<br /> <br /> Hopefully, being scarily accurate (20 Resting Accuracy!!!) is enough to bridge the gap.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Yah, armor does have sneakiness issues. Potentially you could get an evocation to hide/disguise it? Many Pockets Meditation + Quicksilver Armor Approach can don hidden armor in a turn, but several charms and motes is a bit expensive.<br /> <br /> Alternatively, at Essence 2: Perfect Hybrid Interaction (Unusual Hide). Or find a mutated cat and eat it. Or find a cat, mutate it with Sharing Luna's Gifts, and steal it's food while taunting it. </div> </div> </div>Unusual Hide OOOOO is certainly a possible purchase/Tell mutation. Less Ninja potential but certainly better survivability (so 8 base, then up to 4 more so 12 in total) and with Moon\u2019s Hidden Face, also not noticeable.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Or, if you're going for sorcery: Invulnerable Skin of Bronze: +6 soak, and an extra +essence if you aren't wearing armor. </div> </div> </div>I though of this, but the Medium armour status gave me pause.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> EV is mostly good enough, but someone if an enemy solar throws 28 dice at you, or an enemy sidereal throws 21 dice with TN 4 at you, you'll want soak. Even if they just send 16 dice at you, you'd rather not choose between a slight chance of taking 10+ dice of withering damage, or spending 6m straight to prevent the hit. </div> </div> </div>Was mostly using Deebs as a baseline, but you are right.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8959-prototype00","name":"prototype00","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8959_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"964"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-09T05:07:46-07:00","id":1323170,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>prototype00</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1293395-ex-3-lunars-glorious-argent-beastiary-a-lunar-s-character-thread?p=1323118#post1323118\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I though of this, but the Medium armour status gave me pause.</div> </div> </div> </div>Any particular thing you worry about? I don't think this build uses martial arts, and I don't recall any charms besides stamina ones that forbid wearing armor.<br /> ISoB explicitly doesn't impair mobility 'normally', just for martial arts and similar effects<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>prototype00</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1293395-ex-3-lunars-glorious-argent-beastiary-a-lunar-s-character-thread?p=1323118#post1323118\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\">Was mostly using Deebs as a baseline, but you are right.</span></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Right, DBs are going to have a lot less ability to overpower high defense. Maxing 24 dice and a success (11+2stunt+5 weapon+6motes+wp), but if they have anything other than a light weapon their pool gets below what can frequently hit you.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23597-autxauty","name":"autXautY","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"286"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-09T05:33:11-07:00","id":1323177,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>autXautY</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1293395-ex-3-lunars-glorious-argent-beastiary-a-lunar-s-character-thread?p=1323170#post1323170\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Any particular thing you worry about? I don't think this build uses martial arts, and I don't recall any charms besides stamina ones that forbid wearing armor.<br /> ISoB explicitly doesn't impair mobility 'normally', just for martial arts and similar effects</div> </div> </div> </div>Does it not penalize your evasion? If not thats cool, might be something I pick up.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Right, DBs are going to have a lot less ability to overpower high defense. Maxing 24 dice and a success (11+2stunt+5 weapon+6motes+wp), but if they have anything other than a light weapon their pool gets below what can frequently hit you. </div> </div> </div>Yeah, but it isn't overly onerous to give this character decent soak.<br /> <br /> Just noticed that I miscounted accuracy, its actually resting accuracy 21, isn't it? (5 Dex + 5 Brawl + 1 Specialty + 2 Stunt + 5 Artifact + 3 Ambush Hunter), goodness, thats rather mote efficient.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":8959,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8959-prototype00","user":"prototype00","date":". 07-09-2019, 08:42 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8959-prototype00","name":"prototype00","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8959_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"964"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-09T07:50:06-07:00","id":1323196,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"font-size:16px\"><b>Kylina Sele</b> (Take 2) <span style=\"font-size:12px\">Okay, lets try this again, I've managed to trim a bit so that I can fit it all in at character creation...</span><br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\">Spirit Shape: Cat<br /> Tell: Unusual Hide OOOOO</span> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><br /> <br /> <img src=\"https://images-wixmp-ed30a86b8c4ca887773594c2.wixmp.com/f/ba8d6b24-8e5f-4939-a4bf-0752491f50c0/dcq2urv-96e45b48-b9e0-47ed-b3bd-c02b8afcf7e3.png?token=eyJ0eXAiOiJKV1QiLCJhbGciOiJIUzI1NiJ9..lt_o7oiD5dOpoAtn2U0maioYfnLD8r4C1yT8RIP7xxU\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/></div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\"><b>Attributes</b><br /> <br /> Physical (Secondary) (3bp spent)</span></span><br /> <br /> Strength OOO<br /> Dex OOOOO (Favored)<br /> Sta OOO<br /> <br /> Social (Primary)<br /> <br /> Charisma OO<br /> Manipulation OOOOO (Favored)<br /> Appearance OOOOO (Favored)<br /> <br /> Mental (Tertiary)<br /> <br /> Perception OO<br /> Intelligence OOO<br /> Wits OOO (Favored)<br /> <br /> <b>Abilities (8bp spent)</b><br /> <br /> Athletics OO<br /> Awareness OOO<br /> Brawl OOOOO (Specialty: Bite)<br /> Dodge OOOOO (Specialty: Small Forms)<br /> Integrity O<br /> Larceny OOO<br /> Linguistics O<br /> Occult OOO<br /> Presence OOO<br /> Socialize OOO (Specialty: Cat Got your Tongue?)<br /> Stealth OOO (Specialty: Small Forms)<br /> <br /> <b>Merits (4 bp spent)</b><br /> <br /> Artifact (Belt of Shadow Walking) OOO<br /> Heart's Blood O<br /> Stolen Faces OO<br /> Unusual Hide (Tell) OOOOO<br /> Latent: Underfoot Menace<br /> <br /> <b>Charms</b><br /> <br /> Excellencies: (Yes, she has Excellencies in all attributes. She is literally omni-capable. No, it wasn't easy, as you'll soon see)<br /> <br /> Strength<br /> Dexterity<br /> Stamina<br /> Charisma<br /> Manipulation<br /> Appearance<br /> Perception<br /> Intelligence<br /> Wits<br /> <br /> Universal:<br /> <br /> Quicksilver Second Face: Never be left without your battle form.<br /> <br /> Strength:<br /> <br /> Ferocious Biting Tooth: Eventually this will be our main source of Overwhelming, for now its merely decent, but it also gives us our Str Excellency, which we can stunt for +4 damage.<br /> <br /> Divine Predator Strike: This is <i>basically</i> also Overwhelming, and these two charms go well together to boost our damage a long with the Strength Excellency.<br /> <br /> Stamina:<br /> <br /> Impenetrable Beast Armor/Durant Quicksilver Adaptation: The wonder combination is the basis of Lunar Soak. In this case, we are hoping we don't get hit (9-10 Evasion), but if we do, this should take some of the edge off. (Soak is 8 normally, can be raised up to 12 for 4 motes, once this character has some Lunar XP under her belt, she can pick up Invulnerable Skin of Bronze for those really dangerous days for 14 soak resting which can be raised to 18 with the Excellency)<br /> <br /> Dexterity:<br /> <br /> Agile Beast Defense: Our 1m workhorse will always give us +1 to Evasion and we can apply it after we see what our foe rolls (if it isn't 9, don't bother)<br /> <br /> Bending Before the Storm: Our Onslaught Negator.<br /> <br /> Charisma:<br /> <br /> Argent Songbird Voice: Our omni-applicable success-on-social actions generator.<br /> <br /> Debt of Borrowed Skin: Our altruistic method of stealing other people's faces. A thief with a heart of gold, indeed.<br /> <br /> Perception:<br /> <br /> Perceiving the Hidden World: Not only does this let us see immaterial, as a Cat we auto-detect out to Long Range!<br /> <br /> Spirit Rending Fury: For 1 mote per attack, this lets us attack with impunity with the Belt of Shadow Walking if the enemy can't strike Immaterial.<br /> <br /> Intelligence:<br /> <br /> Memory Drinking Meditation: If you ever replace someone and don't want their spouse to suspect, accept no substitutes. Also super good at collecting information on others (just steal the faces of those around them and reap the intel).<br /> <br /> Terrestrial Circle Sorcery: No need to belabour the usefulness here. I chose Mists of Eventide as a Control Spell as it will serve you well in stealthy infiltrations if you can put people to sleep and they can't see where it is coming from.<br /> <br /> Wood Dragon's Claw: A really key part of our combat - an artifact weapon on demand allows us to attack at a resting Withering Accuracy of 21 (!!!) (Dex 5 + Brawl 5 + Specialty 1 + Ambush Hunter 3 + Accuracy 5 + Stunt 2).<br /> <br /> Combined with Divine Predator Strike and Ferocious Biting Tooth, you are basically always adding 3 dice to your post-soak damage (you'll get 2 10s on 21 dice most of the time, statistically) and your overwhelming is going to be at least 4 so that's a 7 dice overwhelming damage even if their soak eats everything, which is nice.<br /> <br /> Appearance:<br /> <br /> Subtle Silver Declaration / Moons Hidden Face: Since our Tell is now obvious, these are necessary investments to not reveal ourselves. Generally useful too.<br /> <br /> Edit: Good call <b>autXautY </b>on Wood Dragon's Claw/Artifact weapon. Stacking that and Ambush Hunter is really quite stellar (best resting accuracy in the game...?)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":8959,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8959-prototype00","user":"prototype00","date":". 07-09-2019, 11:45 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8959-prototype00","name":"prototype00","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8959_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"964"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-09T13:04:12-07:00","id":1323262,"title":"","content":"I generally like what you've done with the character (though, the name is pretty groan-worthy). However, I have reservations about the Tell (in both the most recent iteration and the first).<br /> <br /> For the most recent, were I the Storyteller, I would want some sort of justification as to why you would have Unusual Hide at rank 5. The most I would allow for a cat totem would be rank 2 without some other justification. Is this Wyld-mutated cat that is your spirit shape? Man, what even are the rules for taking such animals as spirit shapes and taking those mutations as your Tell? Normally, taking such forms requires the Lunar to commit extra motes when changing into those shapes. Does taking them as your Tell absolve you from having to commit those motes? Anyway, I believe the inconsistency between cats and Unusual Hide 5 was why autXautY was suggesting anything and everything that could get you that Merit except taking it as a Tell (though, correct me if I am wrong about that, aut).<br /> <br /> For the first iteration (and this is just me being curious more than anything), what sort of physical manifestation were you thinking that Silent Movement would take?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":24959,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24959-mynorin","user":"Mynorin","date":". 07-09-2019, 04:28 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24959-mynorin","name":"Mynorin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24959_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"60"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-09T14:30:52-07:00","id":1323283,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mynorin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1293395-ex-3-lunars-glorious-argent-beastiary-a-lunar-s-character-thread?p=1323262#post1323262\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I generally like what you've done with the character (though, the name is pretty groan-worthy). However, I have reservations about the Tell (in both the most recent iteration and the first).<br /> <br /> For the most recent, were I the Storyteller, I would want some sort of justification as to why you would have Unusual Hide at rank 5. The most I would allow for a cat totem would be rank 2 without some other justification. Is this Wyld-mutated cat that is your spirit shape? Man, what even are the rules for taking such animals as spirit shapes and taking those mutations as your Tell? Normally, taking such forms requires the Lunar to commit extra motes when changing into those shapes. Does taking them as your Tell absolve you from having to commit those motes? Anyway, I believe the inconsistency between cats and Unusual Hide 5 was why autXautY was suggesting anything and everything that could get you that Merit except taking it as a Tell (though, correct me if I am wrong about that, aut).<br /> <br /> For the first iteration (and this is just me being curious more than anything), what sort of physical manifestation were you thinking that Silent Movement would take?</div> </div> </div> </div>I'd agree that unusual hide is an odd tell for a cat-totem. I guess you could explain it as one of the non-totem tells - hide covered in scar tissue maybe?<br /> My impression is you don't spend extra motes for keeping your tell when you shapeshifter - you've more or less bought it using merits points instead of motes. I think there's an ask in the ask the devs thread about it.<br /> That, plus the already existing tell in the first write-up, plus the option to turn it on and off were why I suggested alternate means. Also, I enjoy the idea of mutating an animal, then stealing it's shape.<br /> I'd imagine cat-like feet would be the manifestation of silent movement.<br /> <br /> Do people interpret a tell as opening up protean charms? What about turning into a mutated animal?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23597-autxauty","name":"autXautY","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"286"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-09T15:35:22-07:00","id":1323295,"title":"","content":"If you're hell-bent on unusual hide, why not be a chimera, and be a cat-armadillo chimera, and get unusual hide OOOOO via the armadillo for your chimera spirit shape and use the cat stats as a base line to cheese that in? Even leaves you with one mutation point.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/903-cheshire-cat","name":"Cheshire Cat","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar903_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"502"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-09T16:49:41-07:00","id":1323311,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cheshire Cat</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1293395-ex-3-lunars-glorious-argent-beastiary-a-lunar-s-character-thread?p=1323295#post1323295\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If you're hell-bent on unusual hide, why not be a chimera, and be a cat-armadillo chimera, and get unusual hide OOOOO via the armadillo for your chimera spirit shape and use the cat stats as a base line to cheese that in? Even leaves you with one mutation point.</div> </div> </div> </div>I do believe the Chimera Charm is only applicable in HBT (As per my reading of Chimera Soul Expression), when you turn into an animal, you turn into that animal, in this case, a cat, barring Tell shennanigans. Chimeras are for wolf-man form.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I generally like what you've done with the character (though, the name is pretty groan-worthy). However, I have reservations about the Tell (in both the most recent iteration and the first). </div> </div> </div>Heh, you're the first person to comment on the name. I'm quite proud that I spent less than no time thinking it up. ;P<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> For the most recent, were I the Storyteller, I would want some sort of justification as to why you would have Unusual Hide at rank 5. The most I would allow for a cat totem would be rank 2 without some other justification. Is this Wyld-mutated cat that is your spirit shape? Man, what even are the rules for taking such animals as spirit shapes and taking those mutations as your Tell? Normally, taking such forms requires the Lunar to commit extra motes when changing into those shapes. Does taking them as your Tell absolve you from having to commit those motes? Anyway, I believe the inconsistency between cats and Unusual Hide 5 was why autXautY was suggesting anything and everything that could get you that Merit except taking it as a Tell (though, correct me if I am wrong about that, aut). </div> </div> </div>See, the thing is the Tell is special, and here are a couple of things that have already been discussed but I will re-post here:<br /> <br /> 1. The Tell doesn't have to have any relation to your Spirit Shape. It can be any odd thing (like a Shadow that moves independently of you, is given as one of the examples). So if you wanted a Tell (My skin is made of Black Onyx) as long as you bought it with merit dots, thats fine.<br /> <br /> 2. The Tell is (As auXautY said) always in all your shapes and thus if you choose it as something that does something (like a mutation, unusual hide) its basically your always on Superpower and doesn't cost extra motes.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> For the first iteration (and this is just me being curious more than anything), what sort of physical manifestation were you thinking that Silent Movement would take? </div> </div> </div>Hmm, I was thinking those cute cat-pads on the bottom of her feet, personally. The silent movement mutation is not one that is called out as obvious like Quills or Unusual Hide, so it should be possible not to flaunt it if you don't need to (hence why I didn't buy the mutation hiding charm).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Do people interpret a tell as opening up protean charms? What about turning into a mutated animal? </div> </div> </div>I believe it's been asked, neither the Tell, nor a mutated animal qualifies you for Protean benefits, it has to be something the actual animal itself has.<br /> <br /> Edit: Let me lay out the ways to mitigate Soak Woes as I see them:<br /> <br /> 1. Moonsilver Armor: The drawback here is it\u2019s obvious and you don\u2019t have any way to remove it (except more Ess2 Charms) as a cat.<br /> <br /> 2. Unusual Hide (Tell): You can make it subtle via a pair of charms that also disguised your Tell, might have some flavour concerns (though The Black (Onyx) cat does have some charm).<br /> <br /> 3: Invulnerable Skin of Bronze: The drawback here is that it is obvious and you are heavy (not good for sneaking on a beam). However you can dismiss it and resume it as a cat, but not instantly. This is always an option as you can just pick up the spell with Lunar XP.<br /> <br /> What would y\u2019all recommend?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":8959,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8959-prototype00","user":"prototype00","date":". 07-09-2019, 08:56 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8959-prototype00","name":"prototype00","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8959_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"964"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-09T18:25:57-07:00","id":1323330,"title":"","content":"Hmm, besides Lore 3 for introducing facts, any other ability minimums for doing stuff (not crafting) for Kylina, since she is Omni-Excellency?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8959-prototype00","name":"prototype00","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8959_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"964"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-09T18:31:07-07:00","id":1323331,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>prototype00</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1293395-ex-3-lunars-glorious-argent-beastiary-a-lunar-s-character-thread?p=1323311#post1323311\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I do believe the Chimera Charm is only applicable in HBT (As per my reading of Chimera Soul Expression), when you turn into an animal, you turn into that animal, in this case, a cat, barring Tell shennanigans. Chimeras are for wolf-man form.</div> </div> </div> </div>My impression is it also applies to your spirit shape, but not to any other shapes.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>prototype00</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1293395-ex-3-lunars-glorious-argent-beastiary-a-lunar-s-character-thread?p=1323311#post1323311\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Edit: Let me lay out the ways to mitigate Soak Woes as I see them:<br /> <br /> 1. Moonsilver Armor: The drawback here is it\u2019s obvious and you don\u2019t have any way to remove it (except more Ess2 Charms) as a cat.<br /> <br /> 2. Unusual Hide (Tell): You can make it subtle via a pair of charms that also disguised your Tell, might have some flavour concerns (though The Black (Onyx) cat does have some charm).<br /> <br /> 3: Invulnerable Skin of Bronze: The drawback here is that it is obvious and you are heavy (not good for sneaking on a beam). However you can dismiss it and resume it as a cat, but not instantly. This is always an option as you can just pick up the spell with Lunar XP.<br /> <br /> What would y\u2019all recommend?</div> </div> </div> </div>In the long run, I'd say all 3. Or, get a suit of moonsilver armor, learn invulnerable skin of bronze, and get some access to unusual hide (Tell/chimera on spirit shape/PHI/alternate form/whatever random lunar charms help). None of them are that expensive, and you can pick and choose what to use when - if you've abandoned subtlety as you march to glorious battle, put on the armor, turn your hide into iron, then turn it into bronze. (Iron which has been turned into bronze is twice as hard as regular iron or bronze) If you need to sneak into a warren of thin, fragile beams watched by eagle-eyed guardians who would never suspect an ordinary cat, yet instantly tell the difference between an ordinary cat and one with mutations, leave them all off as you turn into a totally ordinary cat, and maybe add unusual hide if a fight starts and it doesn't cost an action.<br /> I think there's a few hearthstones that add long-duration soak, but also require committing motes (in Arms of the Chosen, the bamboo one and one of the stone ones with evocations)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23597-autxauty","name":"autXautY","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"286"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-09T18:56:46-07:00","id":1323335,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>autXautY</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1293395-ex-3-lunars-glorious-argent-beastiary-a-lunar-s-character-thread?p=1323331#post1323331\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My impression is it also applies to your spirit shape, but not to any other shapes.</div> </div> </div> </div>You are absolutely correct, so something something Unusual Hide as a Kitty that I can keep hidden with Moons Hidden Face (so that she looks like an ordinary kitty), then I can also purchase the Silent Movement as my Tell anyway.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> In the long run, I'd say all 3. Or, get a suit of moonsilver armor, learn invulnerable skin of bronze, and get some access to unusual hide (Tell/chimera on spirit shape/PHI/alternate form/whatever random lunar charms help). None of them are that expensive, and you can pick and choose what to use when - if you've abandoned subtlety as you march to glorious battle, put on the armor, turn your hide into iron, then turn it into bronze. (Iron which has been turned into bronze is twice as hard as regular iron or bronze) If you need to sneak into a warren of thin, fragile beams watched by eagle-eyed guardians who would never suspect an ordinary cat, yet instantly tell the difference between an ordinary cat and one with mutations, leave them all off as you turn into a totally ordinary cat, and maybe add unusual hide if a fight starts and it doesn't cost an action.<br /> I think there's a few hearthstones that add long-duration soak, but also require committing motes (in Arms of the Chosen, the bamboo one and one of the stone ones with evocations) </div> </div> </div>The Hearthstone is a good idea but ST fiat to make it stable I guess. With the Desert Basilisc series of charms, socketing is not an issue, so great idea!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":8959,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8959-prototype00","user":"prototype00","date":". 07-09-2019, 10:11 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8959-prototype00","name":"prototype00","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8959_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"964"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-09T19:57:29-07:00","id":1323345,"title":"","content":"A few thoughts on the cat woman build:<ul><li>If you're using Wood Dragon's Claws, your Brawl specialty should probably be WDC instead of Bite</li> <li>For a few specialties, they should be Tiny form, not Small form</li> <li>If you want Unusual Hide for your tell, you should choose a different form for your totem and say that you got cat through the Heart's Blood merit. None of your plan requires a Cat Totem.</li> <li>You need 4 mental attribute charms to buy Sorcery and you only have 3.</li> </ul><br /> <br /> I have to say, being able to use Wood Dragon's Claws in cat form makes Death Kitty a lot more powerful.<br /> <br /> Moon's Hidden Face could have interesting interactions with Wood Dragon's Claws, especially if you make it your control spell and add evocations. Actually, wouldn't it also hide Invulnerable Skin of Bronze?<br /> <br /> Graceful Crane Stance would be a must if you want to sneak while Bronze.<br /> <br /> For Soak:<br /> <br /> Stamina 3: 3<br /> Unusual Hide 5: 5<br /> Light Armor: 5<br /> Invulnerable Skin of Bronze: 6<br /> <br /> Resting Soak 19 + another 4 that can be added after a hit<br /> Hardness 6<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/458-indivisible","name":"Indivisible","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"41"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-09T22:24:43-07:00","id":1323378,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Indivisible</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1293395-ex-3-lunars-glorious-argent-beastiary-a-lunar-s-character-thread?p=1323345#post1323345\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A few thoughts on the cat woman build:<ul><li>If you're using Wood Dragon's Claws, your Brawl specialty should probably be WDC instead of Bite</li> <li>For a few specialties, they should be Tiny form, not Small form</li> <li>If you want Unusual Hide for your tell, you should choose a different form for your totem and say that you got cat through the Heart's Blood merit. None of your plan requires a Cat Totem.</li> <li>You need 4 mental attribute charms to buy Sorcery and you only have 3.</li> </ul></div> </div> </div> </div>Will respond in order:<br /> <br /> 1. Yep, need to change that to Specialty: Claw or something. Shame, lots of animal shapes have great bites.<br /> <br /> 2. I was going for the more general meaning of \u201cSmall\u201d but I take your point. Most other Tiny Creatures don\u2019t have the advantages of cats though.<br /> <br /> 3. But the styling, it\u2019s got to be an elegant character... It\u2019s okay Chimera form into Unusual Hide is better, so I get to keep my kitty Spirit Shape. I wonder what to chimera with that would be thematic and believable? Some kind of insect maybe? A Black Widow? Then I can take Silent Movement as my Tell.<br /> <br /> 4. Totally correct, I\u2019m playing around in my head to make Physical Primary and Max Str OOOOO, so I can move Charms around. Also a 15 base damage - 20 with the Excellency is so tempting with that 21 Accuracy...<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I have to say, being able to use Wood Dragon's Claws in cat form makes Death Kitty a lot more powerful. </div> </div> </div>Isn\u2019t it? Man, you can just coast on that 21 dice accuracy and put all motes into damage vs 99% of foes.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Moon's Hidden Face could have interesting interactions with Wood Dragon's Claws, especially if you make it your control spell and add evocations. Actually, wouldn't it also hide Invulnerable Skin of Bronze? </div> </div> </div>This I\u2019m not so sure of, it specifically says mutations, so magic effects are probably not covered.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Graceful Crane Stance would be a must if you want to sneak while Bronze. </div> </div> </div>First thing I was thinking of, really.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> For Soak:<br /> <br /> Stamina 3: 3<br /> Unusual Hide 5: 5<br /> Light Armor: 5<br /> Invulnerable Skin of Bronze: 6<br /> <br /> Resting Soak 19 + another 4 that can be added after a hit<br /> Hardness 6 </div> </div> </div>I\u2019m still leery about Moonsilver armour, but the rest of the stuff (Unusual Hide/ISOB) is definitely stuff you can run around with that still gives you respectable Soak. But that\u2019s just me.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":8959,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8959-prototype00","user":"prototype00","date":". 07-10-2019, 01:29 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8959-prototype00","name":"prototype00","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8959_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"964"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-09T22:56:57-07:00","id":1323381,"title":"","content":"Isn't there any charms to hide armour, or are they all at higher Essence?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/16927-illithid","name":"Illithid","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar16927_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1325"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-09T23:47:46-07:00","id":1323385,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Illithid</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1293395-ex-3-lunars-glorious-argent-beastiary-a-lunar-s-character-thread?p=1323381#post1323381\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Isn't there any charms to hide armour, or are they all at higher Essence?</div> </div> </div> </div>None, and I went looking specifically for this build. (Hope I didn\u2019t miss any!)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8959-prototype00","name":"prototype00","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8959_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"964"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-10T01:08:19-07:00","id":1323392,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Illithid</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1293395-ex-3-lunars-glorious-argent-beastiary-a-lunar-s-character-thread?p=1323381#post1323381\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Isn't there any charms to hide armour, or are they all at higher Essence?</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, <i>not exactly</i>.<br /> <br /> Many-Pockets Meditation allows the Lunar to elsewhere-banish any item light enough to hold or wear. Quicksilver Armor Approach allows the armor to be donned in one turn.<br /> <br /> But, you cannot hide your armor <i>and</i> wear it too.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/487-greyman","name":"Greyman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar487_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1308"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-11T07:51:17-07:00","id":1323681,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"font-size:16px\"><b>Kylina Sele</b> (Final Draft) <span style=\"font-size:12px\">Once more from the top. This one will be the cat's meow, promise.</span><br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\">Spirit Shape: Cat/Scarab<br /> Tell: Silent Movement OOO </span><br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><br /> <img src=\"https://images-wixmp-ed30a86b8c4ca887773594c2.wixmp.com/f/cdd9280a-59e1-4091-92de-01b9b84363c5/d8r51m6-bf8cb1e9-8dac-4040-8ef4-f0a25918c428.png?token=eyJ0eXAiOiJKV1QiLCJhbGciOiJIUzI1NiJ9..HyMtkWMAiXRZrYokhAGEKCKFRWmV1Wrd0pykz2ZwCEs\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/><br /> </div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\"><b>Attributes</b><br /> <br /> Physical (Primary</span></span><span style=\"font-size:16px\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">) (3bp spent)</span></span><br /> <br /> Strength OOOOO<br /> Dex OOOOO (Favored)<br /> Sta OOO<br /> <br /> Social (Secondary)<br /> <br /> Charisma OO<br /> Manipulation OOOOO (Favored)<br /> Appearance OOO (Favored)<br /> <br /> Mental (Tertiary)<br /> <br /> Perception OO<br /> Intelligence OOO<br /> Wits OOO (Favored)<br /> <br /> <b>Abilities (8bp spent)</b><br /> <br /> Athletics OO<br /> Awareness OOO<br /> Brawl OOOOO (Specialty: Claw)<br /> Dodge OOOOO (Specialty: Tiny/Miniscule Forms)<br /> Integrity O<br /> Larceny OOO<br /> Linguistics O<br /> Occult OOO<br /> Presence OOO<br /> Socialize OOO (Specialty: Cat Got your Tongue?)<br /> Stealth OOO (Specialty: Tiny/Miniscule Forms)<br /> <br /> <b>Merits (4 bp spent)</b><br /> <br /> Artifact (Belt of Shadow Walking) OOO<br /> Hearthstone (Stone of Resilient Bamboo) OO<br /> Heart's Blood O<br /> Stolen Faces O<br /> Silent Movement OOO (Tell)<br /> Latent: Underfoot Menace<br /> <br /> <b>Charms</b><br /> <br /> Excellencies: (Yes, she has Excellencies in all attributes. She is literally omni-capable. No, it wasn't easy, as you'll soon see)<br /> <br /> Strength<br /> Dexterity<br /> Stamina<br /> Charisma<br /> Manipulation<br /> Appearance<br /> Perception<br /> Intelligence<br /> Wits<br /> <br /> Universal:<br /> <br /> Quicksilver Second Face: Never be left without your battle form.<br /> <br /> Chimera Soul Expression: Kylina Sele is not merely a thorn in the side of the rich and cruel, she is an agent provocateur and a bringer of change, and so the Scarab, symbol of Death and Rebirth also becomes her. In battle, this gives her Unusual Hide OOOOO (as her skin takes on an almost onyx like hardness) and Mighty Thew O (as her compact form surges with strength). (Burrower OO would be perfect but I can't afford to take Unusual Hide OOOO can I?)<br /> <br /> Stamina:<br /> <br /> Impenetrable Beast Armor/Durant Quicksilver Adaptation: The wonder combination is the basis of Lunar Soak. In this case, we are hoping we don't get hit (9-10 Evasion), but if we do, this should take some of the edge off.<br /> <br /> So something I didn't realize, Soak enhancement isn't actually limited by your Excellency limit, its just that there are rules about how you can apply your Excellency, but it all stacks with Impenetrable Beast Armor.<br /> <br /> So Base 3 + Unusual Hide 5 + Impenetrable Beast Armor 3 (for 3 motes) + Stamina Excellency 4 (for 4 motes) + Resilient Bamboo Hearthstone 2 = 17 Ha! That's almost respectable! And of course you can pick up ISOB for another +6 if you know things are going to get dicey, bringing the total to 23, now that's decent Lunar Soak.<br /> <br /> Note: The Stamina Excellency you don't have to activate until after you see how many successes your opponent rolled.<br /> <br /> Dexterity:<br /> <br /> Agile Beast Defense: Our 1m workhorse will always give us +1 to Evasion and we can apply it after we see what our foe rolls (if it isn't 9, don't bother)<br /> <br /> Bending Before the Storm: Our Onslaught Negator.<br /> <br /> Charisma:<br /> <br /> Argent Songbird Voice: Our omni-applicable success-on-social actions generator.<br /> <br /> Debt of Borrowed Skin: Our altruistic method of stealing other people's faces. A thief with a heart of gold, indeed.<br /> <br /> Perception:<br /> <br /> Perceiving the Hidden World: Not only does this let us see immaterial, as a Cat we auto-detect out to Long Range!<br /> <br /> Spirit Rending Fury: For 1 mote per attack, this lets us attack with impunity with the Belt of Shadow Walking if the enemy can't strike Immaterial.<br /> <br /> Wits:<br /> <br /> Desert Basilisc Diadem: Gives us a handy slot for our Resilient Bamboo Hearthstone (hopefully the ST will allow it to either be Stable or Wyldborn) and is also the pre-req for the always great Radiant Basilic Jewel.<br /> <br /> Intelligence:<br /> <br /> Memory Drinking Meditation: If you ever replace someone and don't want their spouse to suspect, accept no substitutes. Also super good at collecting information on others (just steal the faces of those around them and reap the intel).<br /> <br /> Terrestrial Circle Sorcery: No need to belabour the usefulness here.<br /> <br /> Wood Dragon's Claw: A really key part of our combat - an artifact weapon on demand allows us to attack at a resting Withering Accuracy of 21 (!!!) (Dex 5 + Brawl 5 + Specialty 1 + Ambush Hunter 3 + Accuracy 5 + Stunt 2).<br /> <br /> Combined with Divine Predator Strike and Ferocious Biting Tooth (you'll need to buy these non-favored I'm afraid, but still not overly onerous), you are basically always adding 3 dice to your post-soak damage (you'll get 2 10s on 21 dice most of the time, statistically) and your overwhelming is going to be at least 4 so that's a 7 dice overwhelming damage even if their soak eats everything, which is nice.<br /> <br /> Appearance:<br /> <br /> Subtle Silver Declaration / Moons Hidden Face: Since our Mutations are now obvious, these are necessary investments to not reveal ourselves. Generally useful too for an infiltrator.<br /> <br /> So here are some numbers: (Not including stunting +2 dice)<br /> <br /> Withering Attack (Wood Dragon's Claw): 19 (+7 for 7m) / 15 damage (+5 for 5m)<br /> Decisive Attack (Wood Dragon's Claw): 14 (+7 for 7m)<br /> Soak (As Cat): 10 (+3 for 3m, +4 for 4m)<br /> Evasion: 8 (+1 for 1m, +2 for 4m)<br /> Parry: 6 (+1 for 1m, +4 for 8m)<br /> Guile: 6 (+5 for 10m)<br /> Resolve: 2 (+4 for 8m)<br /> <br /> Phew, I think thats mostly done, the obvious things to expand into with XP are the following:<br /> <br /> - Pick up Divine Predator Strike and Ferocious Biting Tooth, for low accuracy characters, these are white elephants, but for you the skys the limit. You will be rolling at least 2 10s and possibly/probably more on a regular basis with a resting accuracy of 21 (!!). That really boosts your post-soak damage.<br /> <br /> - Pick up ISOB, your emergency Soak puts you on par with legit Lunar Soakbeasts.<br /> <br /> - Pick up Radiant Basilisc Jewel - Your Free Greater Hearthstone awaits, lots of choices here.<br /> <br /> - Max your Appearance, why not? Just melt hearts wherever you go.<br /> <br /> I leave it to you, valued reader and fellow sojourner on this particular character's drafting to decide whether the character accomplishes what it sets out to.<br /> <br /> For me, as Death Kitty is, I am content.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8959-prototype00","name":"prototype00","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8959_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"964"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-11T20:28:57-07:00","id":1323840,"title":"","content":"A few thoughts:<ul><li>Latent Abilities only cost 3 bp, and you cost it as 4 bp under merits, so you have another bp to spend. Are Latents considered merits? I thought that you had to pay for them from your bp budget.</li> <li>Cats are considered to have Strength 1, so they can't perform feats of strength, so Mighty Thews is wasted in cat form.</li> </ul><br /> <br /> Here's another go at it.<br /> <br /> Death Kitty Revision<br /> <br /> Totem: Cat/Scarab<br /> <br /> Tell: Enhanced Sense (Smell)<br /> In the Ask the Devs thread, it was clarified that mutations can qualify you for Protean benefits as long as you aren\u2019t in base form. This is great for a lot of Perception charms.<br /> <br /> <b>Physical [Secondary] (3 bp spent):</b><br /> Strength 3<br /> Dexterity 5<br /> Stamina 3<br /> <b>Social [Primary]:</b><br /> Appearance 2<br /> Charisma 5<br /> Manipulation 5<br /> <b>Mental [Tertiary] </b><br /> Intelligence 3<br /> Perception 3 (Favoured)<br /> Wits 2<br /> <br /> <b>Merits:</b><br /> Enhanced Sense (Smell) 3<br /> Artifact 3 (Moonsilver Chainshirt) 3<br /> Hearthstone (Stone of Resilient Bamboo) 2<br /> Heart\u2019s Blood 1<br /> Stolen Faces 1<br /> Resources 1 (1 bp)<br /> <br /> <b>Bonus Points:</b><br /> Dexterity 4-5 (3 points)<br /> Dodge 3-5 (4 points)<br /> Brawl 3-5 (4 points)<br /> Latent Ability (Underfoot Menace) 3<br /> Merit (Resources 1) 1<br /> <br /> <b>Relevant Abilities:</b><br /> Brawl 5 (Claws)<br /> Dodge 5 (Tiny/Miniscule Forms)<br /> Stealth 3 (Tiny/Miniscule Forms)<br /> <br /> <b>Charms:</b><br /> <u>Excellencies:</u><br /> All of them<br /> <br /> <u>Universal:</u><br /> Quicksilver Second Face<br /> Chimera-Soul Expression (Unusual Hide 5, Antennae)<br /> <br /> <u>Appearance:</u><br /> Subtle Silver Declaration<br /> Moon\u2019s Hidden Face<br /> <br /> <u>Strength:</u><br /> Ferocious Biting Tooth<br /> Divine Predator\u2019s Strike<br /> <br /> <u>Stamina:</u><br /> Impenetrable Beast Armor<br /> Durant Quicksilver Adaptation<br /> <br /> <u>Dexterity:</u><br /> Agile Beast Defense<br /> Bending Before the Storm<br /> <br /> <u>Intelligence:</u><br /> Inevitable Genius Insight<br /> Memory-Drinking Meditation<br /> Terrestrial Circle Sorcery (Wood Dragon\u2019s Claw)<br /> <br /> <u>Wits:</u><br /> Squirrel\u2019s Cunning Technique<br /> Magpie\u2019s Nest Resourcefulness<br /> <br /> Relevant Numbers (Stunts not included):<br /> Withering Attack: 19 dice (+7 for 7m), 13 damage (+4 for 4m), Overwhelming 8ish<br /> Decisive Attack: 14 dice (+7 for 7m)<br /> Soak: 3 Stamina + 5 Armor + 5 Unusual Hide + 2 Hearthstone + 4 excellency = 19 soak<br /> <br /> While Impenetrable Beast Armor does add to soak, it has to be applied before the attack is rolled. Given how often attacks will miss, and that a great strength of Death Kitty is that she can increase her defense after she is hit until the attack misses, this is inefficient.<br /> 5m is gained per turn, and if 2m is spent on FBT, 2m on DPS, and 1m on Agile Beast Defense, then Death Kitty is mote neutral.<br /> She will most likely hit with a withering attack and successful dodge at least one attack on her so she will gain about (8 overwhelming dice/2) + 1i (Agile Beast Defense)= 5i per round.<br /> <br /> <b>Suggested Buys:</b><br /> <u>Post-hit Defense:</u><ul><li>Invulnerable Skin of Bronze</li> </ul><br /> Raise your soak by 6, your hardness to 6, and gain a disarming counterattack when hit.<ul><li>Immovable Aurochs Defense</li> </ul><br /> Have you ever tried to move a cat?<ul><li>Ox-Body Technique</li> </ul><br /> Taking health damage is inevitable.<br /> <br /> <u>Mobility:</u><ul><li>Graceful Crane Stance</li> </ul><br /> This might be necessary if you\u2019re running around while bronze.<ul><li>Instinct-Driven Beast Movement</li> </ul><br /> This is a prereq for some Dexterity subterfuge charms and also awards initiative.<ul><li>Shifting Octopus Trick</li> </ul><br /> This is a solid answer for being grappled.<br /> <u>Defense:</u><ul><li>Fleeting Gazelle Exercise</li> </ul><br /> Not only does this raise your Evasion for the rest of the scene, it also provides initiative.<br /> Cunning Prey Reversal<br /> It raises Evasion after you\u2019ve been hit and provides initiative.<br /> Flowing Body Evasion<br /> Technically the previous two charms have brought you to the dice cap, and this charm has to be declared before the attack roll. It\u2019s still a good answer to uncountable damage and a way to mitigate decisive damage.<br /> <br /> <u>Attack</u><ul><li>Sinuous Striking Grace</li> </ul><br /> Lunar Defense charms often rely on your attacker having lower initiative than you, so lower theirs before they can attack you.<br /> <u>Subterfuge:</u><ul><li>Many</li> </ul><br /> With both Tiny size and the Ambush Hunter ability, Death Kitty gains protean benefits from most charms in this tree. The craziest one is probably Shadow Talon Execution letting you Double 9s on a decisive attack roll.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/458-indivisible","name":"Indivisible","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"41"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-11T22:16:29-07:00","id":1323861,"title":"","content":"I think you have probably made a superior build but the beauty is apart from several key points, it\u2019s a pretty much a free build Chassis:<br /> <br /> - Caste Agnostic<br /> - Primary Attribute Agnostic (Secondary I would be physical, at least)<br /> - Ability Point agnostic, especially if you get Omni Excellency<br /> <br /> The Requirements Are:<br /> - Kitty Cat Shape (Spirit Shape if you want to Chimera)<br /> - The Underfoot Menace Latent<br /> - Wood Dragon\u2019s Claw<br /> - Max Dodge and Brawl, high Stealth<br /> - Some source of Soak would be nice (but not essential)<br /> <br /> And that\u2019s it, and in return you get a combat form that is nearly undetectable in Stealth, has better resting Accuracy than a Dawn Single Point Swordsman and Evasion on par with a Supernal Snake Martial Artist. <br /> <br /> On par with DBT I\u2019ll let you decide, it is a whole lot cheaper though.<br /> <br /> Oh yes, and killing Deebs as a Ragdoll Munchkin is never going to get old. Ha!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":8959,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8959-prototype00","user":"prototype00","date":". 07-12-2019, 02:02 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8959-prototype00","name":"prototype00","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8959_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"964"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-11T23:10:47-07:00","id":1323867,"title":"","content":"I do love how easy it is to bolt onto other characters. It's a way to be able to survive and contribute in combat while still focusing on other things. You don`t even need to max Brawl and Dodge at character creation, it`s just nice to do so.<br /> <br /> You know, if you're willing to wait for Stamina 3, Impenetrable Beast Armor, and Durant Quicksilver Adaptation, you could get away with Tertiary physical attributes.<br /> <br /> Strength 2+1 for 3bp<br /> Dexterity 5<br /> Stamina 1<br /> <br /> You could replace IMB and DQA with Invulnerable Skin of Bronze and wind up with comparable soak and higher hardness.<br /> <br /> So:<br /> 6 bp for an attribute dot and the latent skill<br /> 5 merit points for unusual hide or 1 charm for Chimera Soul Expression<br /> 4 Mental Attribute charms<br /> TCS for Wood Dragon's Claw<br /> 2 charms for FBT and DPS<br /> <br /> So like 3 charms and 6 bp. Most characters that will use this build will likely to social or mental focused, so the mental charms aren`t much of a tax.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/458-indivisible","name":"Indivisible","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"41"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-13T20:15:25-07:00","id":1324339,"title":"","content":"It occurs to me that Tail (OO) is a good mutation to take for the \u201cTell\u201d charm, as it allows you to Wood Dragon's Claw but still manipulate things like locks or whatnot.<br /> <br /> Tail + Unusual Hide is also shorthand for a Pestletail. Does it allow you to use it with Weapon Snatching Coils with the new Mutation understanding from Vance? Disarm to medium range (2 rounds of movement) is a neat trick.<br /> <br /> Note: If anyone wants to take the Ambidexterous Merit to offset the off-hand penalty of the Tail OO merit, it makes sense to take it as part of the Chimera 6 dots you get, as its very hard to find something good to fit in that one dot, and Ambidexterous fits the bill.<br /> <br /> (So Chimera is Unusual Hide OOOOO and Ambidexterous O).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":8959,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8959-prototype00","user":"prototype00","date":". 07-14-2019, 12:42 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8959-prototype00","name":"prototype00","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8959_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"964"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-14T10:56:14-07:00","id":1324522,"title":"","content":"We've been focusing on animal shapeshifting builds with good damage/soak/merits, for the sake of combining with high dex+brawl for something terrifying. I wanted to try something different - a minimal investment build that uses an animal form for nearly all it's stats.<br /> <br /> Changing Moon<br /> Spirit Shape: Tyrant Lizard<br /> Tell: Fangs<br /> <br /> Physical Tertiary<br /> Dex 3, Str 4, Sta 1<br /> Social Primary<br /> Cha 5*, Ma 2, App 5*<br /> Mental Secondary<br /> Perception 5*, Wits 3*, Intelligence 2<br /> <br /> Abilities<br /> Brawl 3, Presence 5, Integrity 3, Socialize 3, Awareness 3, Athletics 3, Linguistics 1, Performance 3, Stealth 3, War 3<br /> Specialties: Presence (Intimidation), Stealth (As tiny creature), Athletics (Showing Off)<br /> <br /> Merits<br /> Heart's Blood 2: River Dragon [I think the best aquatic legendary size thing?], some random utility forms (a few fish, birds, maybe a rat or cat, maybe a good all-around non-legendary combat form, I'd say a bear off the top of my head)<br /> Greater Manse (Rose of Millions - Major Tie (Self - Pride)) [Not sure what to put here, probably something to know how/whether to scare them]<br /> Stolen Faces 2: 5 random people, a successful bandit in the region [for the sake of people being scared of him]<br /> Something 1<br /> Latent Abilities: Predator's Menace<br /> <br /> Charms<br /> Non-attribute: Many-faced Moon Declaration<br /> Dex: Graceful Crane Stance, Instinct-Driven Beast Movement<br /> Str: Grizzly Bear Embrace, Towering Beast Form<br /> App: Glance Oration Technique, Argument-Eclipsing Shadow, Predator-and-Prey Mirror, Feral Smile Tactic, Subtle Silver Declaration,Changing Plumage Mastery<br /> Charisma: Argent Songbird's Voice, Poised Lion Attitude, Beast-King Dictates, Pack-Calling Cry<br /> <br /> BP Spent: 4 on presence, 3 on latents. Spend the rest on willpower or something. Or you can buy up dex/brawl to raise your cap.<br /> <br /> Combat:<br /> Round 1, turn into a tyrant lizard. Or Round 0, if you have time before a fight.<br /> You are now a tyrant lizard with excellencies (max 14 dice to attack, 7 parry, +4 damage, so not great), a cap on how much furious rampage can get you, 3 combat charms, and better intimidation.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23597-autxauty","name":"autXautY","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"286"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-14T18:38:18-07:00","id":1324593,"title":"","content":"So using the animal shape purely for combat and putting stats into everything else? I like it, I think it\u2019s one of the best use of Lunar animal forms (making a physically weak character that can turn into a powerhouse).<br /> <br /> A couple of things:<br /> - I think Accuracy and Damage is the name of the game here and the Great Cat\u2019s Claw Attack probably beats out anything the Bear can do? (Though it\u2019s close) Unless you are aiming for grapple? <br /> <br /> - If all you want is the Str Excellency, you could actually leave Str at 2 and just take charms and Totemic you way in with Sta for Legendary Sized shapes for more Soak on call.<br /> <br /> - Does Tell:Fangs actually help anything or is that just cosmetic?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8959-prototype00","name":"prototype00","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8959_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"964"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-14T18:59:52-07:00","id":1324596,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>prototype00</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1293395-ex-3-lunars-glorious-argent-beastiary-a-lunar-s-character-thread?p=1324593#post1324593\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So using the animal shape purely for combat and putting stats into everything else? I like it, I think it\u2019s one of the best use of Lunar animal forms (making a physically weak character that can turn into a powerhouse).<br /> <br /> A couple of things:<br /> - I think Accuracy and Damage is the name of the game here and the Great Cat\u2019s Claw Attack probably beats out anything the Bear can do? (Though it\u2019s close) Unless you are aiming for grapple?<br /> <br /> - If all you want is the Str Excellency, you could actually leave Str at 2 and just take charms and Totemic you way in with Sta for Legendary Sized shapes for more Soak on call.<br /> <br /> - Does Tell:Fangs actually help anything or is that just cosmetic?</div> </div> </div> </div> - I didn't look too closely at the backup form, great cat is likely the best.<br /> - I considered going totemic -&gt; stamina, and getting 1 stamina charm for the excellency (maybe ox-body? Legendary size likes lots of health levels). I mainly felt like a tyrant lizard will 9 times out of 10 have enough soak to reduce attacks to minimum damage, but fairly often have enough damage to not be at minimum damage themselves.<br /> - Fangs are just cosmetic. I wanted to write a tell and fangs seemed reasonable. Kind of liked the image of him trying to intimidate someone and them just sort-of noticing fangs in his smile.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23597-autxauty","name":"autXautY","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"286"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-14T21:54:45-07:00","id":1324633,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>autXautY</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1293395-ex-3-lunars-glorious-argent-beastiary-a-lunar-s-character-thread?p=1324596#post1324596\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> - I didn't look too closely at the backup form, great cat is likely the best.</div> </div> </div> </div>I was just thinking about it for \u201cinside\u201d when you can\u2019t go large. You know, instead of blowing points on a greater manse you could take the Wits charm Radiant Basilisc Jewel?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> - I considered going totemic -&gt; stamina, and getting 1 stamina charm for the excellency (maybe ox-body? Legendary size likes lots of health levels). I mainly felt like a tyrant lizard will 9 times out of 10 have enough soak to reduce attacks to minimum damage, but fairly often have enough damage to not be at minimum damage themselves. </div> </div> </div>Fair enough, I favour Str 3 for animal forms myself, as you get the excellency for most of your damage needs and some of the early star charms are nice.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> - Fangs are just cosmetic. I wanted to write a tell and fangs seemed reasonable. Kind of liked the image of him trying to intimidate someone and them just sort-of noticing fangs in his smile. </div> </div> </div>Also fair enough. I\u2019m fond of Tell mutation as your Superpower, but it\u2019s not for everyone, I understand.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8959-prototype00","name":"prototype00","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8959_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"964"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-25T19:47:13-07:00","id":1327521,"title":"","content":"So a small coda on Death Kitty as I like to keep all my noodling in one place.<br /> <br /> - Was going to make a full moon version of Death Kitty (Black Tom) but realized it\u2019s not enough changes for me to make another post, just:<br /> <br /> 1.)Avail yourself of all possible Soak Options (Sta 5 + Unusual Hide 5 + Artifact Light 5 + ISOB 6 + Bamboo Hearthstone 2) There, 23 Soak, no motes spent, no enemy can do more than overwhelming to you now.<br /> <br /> 2.) Max Stamina for above if you want, or don\u2019t, you still have 21 resting Soak.<br /> <br /> 3. Definitely invest in Divine Predator Strike. I know I\u2019ve said it\u2019s a gambling charm before, but with a 21 dice attack pool, you are going to roll at least one 10. Congrats, the Charm has paid for itself. More than likely you are going to roll 2-3 10s and potentially up to 4 10s which is massive value for the cost and a great way to boost damage.<br /> <br /> 4. Black Tom should keep the tail mutation and ambidextrous like I proposed. Then you totally get to Style on enemies with Weapon Snatching Coils.<br /> <br /> 5. Sneaky Edit: It\u2019s been pointed out to me on Discord by Drifting Soul that wearing a Frost Thorn Knuckle and merging with it with Last Warrior\u2019s Unity is also great value as it gives you a Thrown Weapon that Death Kitty can use out to Long Range without an Aim action (With Boulders as Pebbles Attitude) and Death Kitty is super accurate with it as, guess what, it also benefits from the 3 extra dice of Ambush Hunter. You can conceal the knuckles while in Stealth Kitty mode with Squirrel\u2019s Cunning Technique and nothing short of an Exalt with charms is going to see it.<br /> <br /> You probably can give up on the cute trick of Omni Excellency with this, but boy howdy is it a scary combatant.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":8959,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8959-prototype00","user":"prototype00","date":". 07-26-2019, 04:14 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8959-prototype00","name":"prototype00","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8959_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"964"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-25T19:51:54-07:00","id":1327522,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://m.youtube.com/watch?v=972UpK7sXok\" target=\"_blank\">How does Tom hold up against The Devil in a fight? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></a>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-25T21:02:38-07:00","id":1327530,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1293395-ex-3-lunars-glorious-argent-beastiary-a-lunar-s-character-thread?p=1327522#post1327522\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><a href=\"https://m.youtube.com/watch?v=972UpK7sXok\" target=\"_blank\">How does Tom hold up against The Devil in a fight? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></a></div> </div> </div> </div>Regular Combat: If Old Scratch can\u2019t beat his 10 EV, my money\u2019s on Black Tom.<br /> <br /> Shapeshifting Combat: Whoever pulls out that \u201cHope\u201d bullshit first wins I expect.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8959-prototype00","name":"prototype00","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8959_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"964"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-08-10T10:10:18-07:00","id":1330266,"title":"","content":"Have you looked at doing anything with Ant-and-Starfish trick? You can create non-legendary size animals from your Heart's Blood library, and while they can't use charms they *do* keep your health pool.<br /> <br /> Feel like you could get up to some shenanigans with once/scene abilities combined with continuously making/unmaking animals.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2154-cactuar","name":"Cactuar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2154_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"58"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-08-10T19:19:02-07:00","id":1330336,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cactuar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1293395-ex-3-lunars-glorious-argent-beastiary-a-lunar-s-character-thread?p=1330266#post1330266\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Have you looked at doing anything with Ant-and-Starfish trick? You can create non-legendary size animals from your Heart's Blood library, and while they can't use charms they *do* keep your health pool.<br /> <br /> Feel like you could get up to some shenanigans with once/scene abilities combined with continuously making/unmaking animals.</div> </div> </div> </div>Had a gander, the willpower cost is giving me pause on the continuously making/unmaking bit, really. Most people have 5, so doing this more than once is a pretty big opportunity cost.<br /> <br /> And it's Ess 3, where I haven't been doing most of my concepting, I must confess.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8959-prototype00","name":"prototype00","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8959_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"964"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-07T08:22:17-07:00","id":1334351,"title":"","content":"Are there any animals besides boars and bears that have Berserker?<br /> <br /> And which is the best animal for a berserker build?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-07T09:03:12-07:00","id":1334354,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1293395-ex-3-lunars-glorious-argent-beastiary-a-lunar-s-character-thread?p=1334351#post1334351\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Are there any animals besides boars and bears that have Berserker?<br /> <br /> And which is the best animal for a berserker build?</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't think there are any others in core or lunars.<br /> I'd probably say a hell boar is better than a bear, unless you like to grapple.<br /> Boars get bone-crunching bite, trample+Deathstomp (+5 decisive against prone, knock people prone with an attack after rushing them), +2 soak, a join-battle enhancing, and overwhelming 5.<br /> Bears get some grapple-enhancers, devour the weak (+5 decisive damage against a crashed enemy, 1/crash), +1 damage, and a lower-damage attack with 12 dice to hit. Also ferocious cub guardian, which if you need to defend other and can argue someone counts as either your young or your master is good.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23597-autxauty","name":"autXautY","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"286"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-07T09:50:46-07:00","id":1334358,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>autXautY</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1293395-ex-3-lunars-glorious-argent-beastiary-a-lunar-s-character-thread?p=1334354#post1334354\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I don't think there are any others in core or lunars.</div> </div> </div> </div>I searched and couldn't find any; I wondered if there were any in Hundred Devils. I don't think so though.<br /> <br /> Thanks for the advice. The boar does look better, though Ferocious Cub Guardian is interesting.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-29T16:08:14-07:00","id":1338525,"title":"","content":"So as an alternative to Falcon Style, I think Strix has some nice traits to enable fall damage abuse.<br /> <br /> First it doesn't have to use mutations to fly, so you can initiate grapples while flying without penalties. Which means you can Kraken-Arm Lash from medium range height without taking that -3 you would with the wings mutation.<br /> <br /> Secondly it has Eagle Wing Rush, which lets you rush from long range, combine this with Ferocious Hound Persuit you can move one range band instantly from long to medium on a rush, not counting as your move action.<br /> <br /> Third it can savage and drag a victim along with any movement action without taking Restrain.<br /> <br /> This lets you start a round from long range height, rush to medium thanks to Eagle Wing + Ferocious Hound, Kraken Arm Lash, withering savage to get your initiative back, reflexively move up to long and Release (reflexive) for long range fall damage shaving of ~10 HLs. Ready to repeat this all next round, starting and ending every round at long range which is a huge pain in the ass for anyone on the ground trying to fight back.<br /> <br /> If you decide to go in on a decisive savage you can also peck out peoples eyes with the predatory bird latent ability which is pretty neat.<br /> <br /> Ideally you want Extra Limbs mutation + Cunning Beast Warrior reflexes so you can rush without taking any penalty on the grapple attack or to your defense.<br /> <br /> A less costly version of this (both mote and intiative wise and for investment) is of course to just start at medium, pick up and drop the first guy from long, next round go down to medium and pick and drop there, next round pick and drop from long etc, only ending your turn and dropping at long range every other round.<br /> <br /> Edit: With Eagle Eye, Night Vision, and Swooping Descent this also gets even scarier on a dark night where strix lunar can re-establish stealth.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2579,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2579-limaxophobiac","user":"limaxophobiac","date":". 09-29-2019, 08:27 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2579-limaxophobiac","name":"limaxophobiac","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"294"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-30T09:27:04-07:00","id":1338637,"title":"","content":"Honestly, turning into a giant version of a bird of prey that grabs animals and flies off with them... does indeed seem like it ought to be a powerful choice if your strategy is to grab people and fly off with it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-30T16:53:21-07:00","id":1338710,"title":"","content":"Oh I've tried figuring out just silly you can get with Terrifying Dragon Roar + Predators Menace (since Vance said they were technically compatible) using appearance charms and oh boy.<br /> <br /> Myriad Graces Appeal (6 non-charm dice from appearance against base Resolve 5 opponents with Perfect Symmetry up) + Terrifying Bestial Visage (3 non-charm dice in predatory forms) really push it way over the top.<br /> <br /> It's possible at character creation (though not XP/BP efficient), on a one-point stunt as a changing moon, to make this intimidation roll with 33 dice, double 9s, and buy one extra success with WP*, for an average 20.8 successes with margin of success x2 initiative lost for all enemies.<br /> <br /> So while they might be read as compatible I'm starting to think they probably shouldn't be.<br /> <br /> *since you're an Apex Predator and are about to get showered in WP from crashes anyway","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2579,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2579-limaxophobiac","user":"limaxophobiac","date":". 09-30-2019, 07:56 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2579-limaxophobiac","name":"limaxophobiac","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"294"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-01T23:07:12-07:00","id":1338947,"title":"","content":"Ah, it\u2019s always a pleasant surprise when people take your build ideas further. <br /> <br /> I\u2019m currently digesting the implications and will comment more later.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8959-prototype00","name":"prototype00","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8959_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"964"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-07T05:36:01-08:00","id":1359456,"title":"","content":"Hmm, I'm feeling a bit inspired to go back and work on a build I had put down for a while.<br /> <br /> Which one? Why, glad you asked...<br /> <br /> <br /> <img src=\"https://i1.mangareader.net/sengoku-youko/27/sengoku-youko-1430120.jpg\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/><br /> <br /> Its the Tiger (Spirit Shape) Tiger Stylist of course! AKA how to add your Strength 4x to your damage for a +30 base damage attack.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":8959,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8959-prototype00","user":"prototype00","date":". 01-07-2020, 09:03 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8959-prototype00","name":"prototype00","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8959_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"964"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-07T07:02:07-08:00","id":1359475,"title":"","content":"Hmmm... Is it purely Tiger style+Lunar charms, or are there other MAs as well? Because there's a lot of styles with +damage charms right at the beginning.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-07T07:16:15-08:00","id":1359480,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1293395-ex-3-lunars-glorious-argent-beastiary-a-lunar-s-character-thread?p=1359475#post1359475\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hmmm... Is it purely Tiger style+Lunar charms, or are there other MAs as well? Because there's a lot of styles with +damage charms right at the beginning.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'll see what I can rustle up. The Core of the build is of course:<br /> <br /> - Max Str<br /> - Str Excellency<br /> - Deadly Claw Blow<br /> - Tiger Form<br /> - DBT<br /> <br /> The +30 base damage comes from that alone, really (and artifact tiger claws or whatnot).<br /> <br /> prototype00","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8959-prototype00","name":"prototype00","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8959_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"964"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-07T10:00:35-08:00","id":1359512,"title":"","content":"So if I'm reading this right, you're getting +5 withering damage from Strength, +10 from the razor claws, +5 more from DBT, and doubling up to 5 attack successes for pre-soak damage via Tiger form (effectively +5 dice if you roll well, which you should be using Deadly Claw Blow). So that's 20-25 presoak dice, plus your extra successes. I'm guessing the remaining +5 is stunting the Strength excellency to include another high attribute (Dex maybe, though Appearance would be amusing if you emphasize your dreadful mien as you tear your foes to shreds). Or is there another +5 I'm missing? I don't think the Strength Excellency can do that by itself without a stunt, since DBT is already providing the basic +Strength bonus to your Charm-dice limit.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2118-reminiscent-oasis","name":"Reminiscent Oasis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2118_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"158"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-07T10:50:58-08:00","id":1359526,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Reminiscent Oasis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1293395-ex-3-lunars-glorious-argent-beastiary-a-lunar-s-character-thread?p=1359512#post1359512\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So if I'm reading this right, you're getting +5 withering damage from Strength, +10 from the razor claws, +5 more from DBT, and doubling up to 5 attack successes for pre-soak damage via Tiger form (effectively +5 dice if you roll well, which you should be using Deadly Claw Blow). So that's 20-25 presoak dice, plus your extra successes. I'm guessing the remaining +5 is stunting the Strength excellency to include another high attribute (Dex maybe, though Appearance would be amusing if you emphasize your dreadful mien as you tear your foes to shreds). Or is there another +5 I'm missing? I don't think the Strength Excellency can do that by itself without a stunt, since DBT is already providing the basic +Strength bonus to your Charm-dice limit.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ah, but the beauty is that there is <i>no</i> Charm-dice limit for things that aren't Attribute+Ability, like Damage. You can pile on every single Charm and they'll all stack (just don't miss).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25764-vwllss-trnt-prncss","name":"vwllss trnt prncss","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"244"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-07T16:26:33-08:00","id":1359599,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Reminiscent Oasis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1293395-ex-3-lunars-glorious-argent-beastiary-a-lunar-s-character-thread?p=1359512#post1359512\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So if I'm reading this right, you're getting +5 withering damage from Strength, +10 from the razor claws, +5 more from DBT, and doubling up to 5 attack successes for pre-soak damage via Tiger form (effectively +5 dice if you roll well, which you should be using Deadly Claw Blow). So that's 20-25 presoak dice, plus your extra successes. I'm guessing the remaining +5 is stunting the Strength excellency to include another high attribute (Dex maybe, though Appearance would be amusing if you emphasize your dreadful mien as you tear your foes to shreds). Or is there another +5 I'm missing? I don't think the Strength Excellency can do that by itself without a stunt, since DBT is already providing the basic +Strength bonus to your Charm-dice limit.</div> </div> </div> </div>Revisiting my calculations you are indeed right. It seems to be only +25 pre other charms. +30 with the stunted Strength Excellency. If you are willing to dip White Reaper, it\u2019s an easy +35, +40 if you are Dex/Str focused and willing to dip snake.<br /> <br /> Deadly Claw blow also has some restrictions upon re-reading and razor claws might be a no go. I might have to find a way to route around that...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":8959,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8959-prototype00","user":"prototype00","date":". 01-07-2020, 08:36 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8959-prototype00","name":"prototype00","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8959_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"964"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-07T17:33:41-08:00","id":1359609,"title":"","content":"Here's an attempt at a death kitty sorcerer (that morphed into a raiton since flying at medium range and raining sorcery on people is hard to deal with. On the other hand, between control Death of Obsidian Butterflies and Underfoot Menace you can get near a free full excellency )<br /> <br /> Shadowed Wings<br /> No Moon Lunar - Raiton Totem<br /> Shapes - Raiton, Cat, Rat, Trout, Owl, Horse, Tiger, 5 insignificant humans<br /> <br /> Attributes:<br /> Dexterity 5 (F), Stamina 2, Strength 1<br /> Appearance 5 (F), Charisma 4, Manipulation 1<br /> Intelligence 5 (C), Perception 5 (C), Wits 2<br /> <br /> Willpower: 8<br /> <br /> Abilities:<br /> Dodge 5<br /> Occult 5<br /> Brawl 3<br /> Lore 3<br /> Medicine 3<br /> Presence 3<br /> Performance 3<br /> Socialize 3<br /> Stealth 3<br /> Linguistics 1<br /> <br /> Specialties: Dodge (As Tiny Creature), Occult (Sorcery), Presence (Being Spooky), Stealth (As Tiny Creature)<br /> <br /> Iodam<br /> <br /> Merits:<br /> Hearts Blood 1, Stolen Faces 1, Enhanced Sense (Scent) 3 [Tell], Contacts (Silver Pact) 3, Greenfriend 1, Ever-Blossoming Mastery 2<br /> <br /> Latent Abilities: Underfoot Menace<br /> <br /> Charms:<br /> Flesh-Sculpting Art<br /> Sharing Luna's Gifts<br /> Penumbra Witch Mastery<br /> Perceiving the Hidden World<br /> Terrestrial Circle Sorcery<br /> Root-Lore: Thousand Blossom Arts<br /> Control Death of Obsidian Butterflies<br /> Many-Faced Moon Transformation<br /> Feral Smile Tactic<br /> Subtle Silver Declaration<br /> Moon's Hidden Face<br /> Changing Plumage Mastery<br /> One of the Herd<br /> Agile Beast Defense<br /> Bending Before the Storm<br /> Demon of the First Circle<br /> Wood Dragon's Claw","signature":"","edited":{"userid":23597,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23597-autxauty","user":"autXautY","date":". 01-07-2020, 08:37 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23597-autxauty","name":"autXautY","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"286"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-07T17:38:04-08:00","id":1359610,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>autXautY</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1293395-ex-3-lunars-glorious-argent-beastiary-a-lunar-s-character-thread?p=1359609#post1359609\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Here's an attempt at a death kitty sorcerer (that morphed into a raiton since flying at medium range and raining sorcery on people is hard to deal with)<br /> <br /> Shadowed Wings<br /> No Moon Lunar - Raiton Totem<br /> Shapes - Raiton, Cat, Rat, Trout, Owl, Horse, Tiger, 5 insignificant humans<br /> <br /> Attributes:<br /> Dexterity 5 (F), Stamina 2, Strength 1<br /> Appearance 5 (F), Charisma 4, Manipulation 1<br /> Intelligence 5 (C), Perception 5 (C), Wits 2<br /> <br /> Willpower: 8<br /> <br /> Abilities:<br /> Dodge 5<br /> Occult 5<br /> Brawl 3<br /> Lore 3<br /> Medicine 3<br /> Presence 3<br /> Performance 3<br /> Socialize 3<br /> Stealth 3<br /> Linguistics 1<br /> <br /> Specialties: Dodge (As Tiny Creature), Occult (Sorcery), Presence (Being Spooky), Stealth (As Tiny Creature)<br /> <br /> Iodam<br /> <br /> Merits:<br /> Hearts Blood 1, Stolen Faces 1, Enhanced Sense (Scent) 3 [Tell], Contacts (Silver Pact) 3, Greenfriend 1, Ever-Blossoming Mastery 2<br /> <br /> Latent Abilities: Underfoot Menace<br /> <br /> Charms:<br /> Flesh-Sculpting Art<br /> Sharing Luna's Gifts<br /> Penumbra Witch Mastery<br /> Perceiving the Hidden World<br /> Terrestrial Circle Sorcery<br /> Root-Lore: Thousand Blossom Arts<br /> Control Death of Obsidian Butterflies<br /> Many-Faced Moon Transformation<br /> Feral Smile Tactic<br /> Subtle Silver Declaration<br /> Moon's Hidden Face<br /> Changing Plumage Mastery<br /> One of the Herd<br /> Agile Beast Defense<br /> Bending Before the Storm<br /> Demon of the First Circle<br /> Wood Dragon's Claw</div> </div> </div> </div>Hmm if you are willing to go chimera, you could have a flying Death Kitty. (I\u2019m assuming the Death kitty angle is for accuracy with spells and Evasion?)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8959-prototype00","name":"prototype00","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8959_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"964"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-07T17:48:02-08:00","id":1359613,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>prototype00</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1293395-ex-3-lunars-glorious-argent-beastiary-a-lunar-s-character-thread?p=1359610#post1359610\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Hmm if you are willing to go chimera, you could have a flying Death Kitty. (I\u2019m assuming the Death kitty angle is for accuracy with spells and Evasion?)</div> </div> </div> </div>Kitty is for accuracy and evasion (and stealth).<br /> <br /> Hmm. Winged Kitty could work well. I do like the sphinx aesthetic. It depends a lot on if shaping sorcery and aiming spells &quot;require any degree of finesse or precision&quot;<br /> <br /> I just remembered - I meant to have Spoke the Wooden Face in place of one of the spells, to keep in contact with other lunars who live far away.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":23597,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23597-autxauty","user":"autXautY","date":". 01-07-2020, 09:14 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23597-autxauty","name":"autXautY","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"286"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-12T16:58:46-08:00","id":1360608,"title":"","content":"So on the topic of Tiger- Tiger Stylist, the germ of the idea is that Lunar Exalted have a couple of withering damage enhancers and can get that number pretty high. <br /> <br /> Especially since withering damage isn\u2019t capped by dice pool.<br /> <br /> What else has withering damage enhancers...<br /> <br /> Oh yeah, literally the first charm of three or four martial arts!<br /> <br /> So here is the breakdown:<br /> <br /> Deadly Beastman Transformation:<br /> 5m 1wp (I\u2019m including the cost for assuming Hybrid Body Transformation) (Simple Activation)<br /> <br /> Strength Excellency<br /> 5m (for the whole stunted shebang)<br /> <br /> Tiger Form (Tiger)<br /> 10m (Simple Activation)<br /> <br /> Falling Scythe Flash (White Reaper)<br /> 5m<br /> <br /> Striking Cobra Technique (Snake)<br /> 3m<br /> <br /> Elegant Weapon Repertoire (Dreaming Pearl Courtesan)<br /> 3m<br /> <br /> Force of the Mountain (Earth Dragon, but get this when you are Ess 5 or something. Not worth it before then)<br /> 3m<br /> <br /> So to merge all the above into a straight up \u201cReturn of the Bad Touch Combo\u201d Attack, you\u2019ll have to use unarmed strike, so no artifact weapons but what you get is....<br /> <br /> A Total of 5 (Base Str) + 5 (Str Excellency) + 5 (Tiger Form if you roll 5 extra successes on the attack roll) + 5 (Falling Scythe Flash w/ 5 Str) + 5 (Striking Cobra Technique w/ 5 Dex) + 4 (Elegant Weapon Repertoire w/ Unarmed) + 5 (DBT) + 7 (Base Damage from Unarmed)= 41 Base damage! (Oh and you had to roll 5 extra successes to get the whole Tiger Form bonus off so it\u2019s necessarily 46, really)<br /> <br /> I mean it\u2019s not a sustainable technique and honestly two simple activations to get there is a real downer, but you can pare it down to just DBT + the supplemental stuff you get something that deals 36 base damage on a hit which, honestly, is impressive enough.<br /> <br /> Thoughts?<br /> <br /> Prototype00","signature":"","edited":{"userid":8959,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8959-prototype00","user":"prototype00","date":". 01-12-2020, 08:20 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8959-prototype00","name":"prototype00","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8959_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"964"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-13T04:05:55-08:00","id":1360667,"title":"","content":"&quot;Thoughts?&quot;<br /> <br /> Don't miss.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-13T04:15:09-08:00","id":1360670,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1293395-ex-3-lunars-glorious-argent-beastiary-a-lunar-s-character-thread?p=1360667#post1360667\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">&quot;Thoughts?&quot;<br /> <br /> Don't miss.</div> </div> </div> </div>I mean, some builds have sustain and some have burst (I've made mostly sustain up to now, it's nice to cut loose), its just the way of things. Its not onerous to get max accuracy (for a non artifact wielder) here 17 with stunting, at that point you're just trying to pick your moment for a &quot;probably gonna crash someone&quot; attack.<br /> <br /> I haven't seen anyone use/abuse the scaling withering damage Lunars are capable of, so it's in some ways a theoretical exercise too.<br /> <br /> prototype00<br /> <br /> Edit: There is nothing stopping you from only putting out 40%-50% of your damage most of the time. Say Elegant Repertoire and Striking Cobra, thats +9 raw damage for 6 motes (+21 raw damage total), so the value play is a more than viable proposition here as well.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":8959,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8959-prototype00","user":"prototype00","date":". 01-13-2020, 07:30 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8959-prototype00","name":"prototype00","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8959_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"964"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-13T19:25:09-08:00","id":1360800,"title":"","content":"Build report 1:<br /> <br /> I know I talked a big talk about cherry picking charms from Snake, White Reaper and DPC. But having to spend 12 (Tiger too) of your 28 ability dots on MA really puts a cramped on character building.<br /> <br /> It\u2019s like Martial Arts genius, awful at everything else, lol.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8959-prototype00","name":"prototype00","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8959_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"964"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-19T07:56:44-08:00","id":1361901,"title":"","content":"Hey Ho, Back to it again. Have been thinking about the Tiger-Tiger Stylist build in the last couple of days, but not going to commit anything to paper. Just using this thread as a notepad for collecting my thoughts, really, if folks don't mind.<br /> <br /> So we're all aware of the combining potential of Martial Arts (to wit, you can stack these effects from basically numerous different sources altogether in a way you couldn't with Melee and Brawl, say). It has always been my belief that the MA merit was a sunk cost that should be made good on, and thus dabblers in the Martial Arts always were getting the short end of the stick (by dabblers I mean people who pick up one MA as a secondary or tertiary combat ability, I mean I see the value for flavour, but... anyway, thats another thread).<br /> <br /> But what is a good practice I feel is to max out one style and then pick a couple of low hanging, synergistic fruits from other styles. Low hanging in this case still being expensive enough at 3 ability dots, but that's the price of doing business.<br /> <br /> Anyway, that's a bit of a look at my philosophy behind this build, but it's also by the by. Here I'm going to just list the &quot;low hanging fruits&quot; culled from the choicest of styles for my reference later on...<br /> <br /> (Note: For those of you just joining the broadcast, I'm merging together the withering boosters found in about 30% of all MAs with the Lunar Exalted's ability to boost withering via DBT and Str Excellency to reach some impressive base damage numbers, stick around, I find it's nice to get comments and learn from others)<br /> <br /> <u>Core MAs:</u><br /> <br /> <b>Snake</b><br /> <br /> Striking Cobra Technique / MA 3/ 3m:<br /> - For Dex 5 Exalts, this is a good, discounted deal, as long as you go first (higher init or other tricks like Sinuous Striking Grace for Lunars) - +5 Withering Damage (If you go first and Dex 5)<br /> <br /> <b>Tiger</b><br /> <br /> Overall review: TBH this style is not good to dip, because you need everything up to the Form Charm to work your damage Mojo. Good candidate for full investment and not dipping though.<br /> <br /> <b>White Reaper</b><br /> <br /> Falling Scythe Slash / MA 3 / 5m:<br /> - For Str 5 Exalts, this is about as good as the Lunar Str Excellency. No discount, but no conditions either. - +5 Withering damage (If Str 5)<br /> <br /> Revolving Crescent Defense / MA 3 / 4m 1i:<br /> - It's not exactly cheap, but this is a great Onslaught negator (because it actually gives you a bonus to your parry if you are suffering from an onslaught penalty) Certainly something for consideration (most other MAs don't have an onslaught negator this early)<br /> <br /> <b>Dreaming Pearl Courtesan</b><br /> <br /> Elegant Weapon Repertoire / MA 3 / 3m:<br /> - Unexpectedly DPC has something for this purpose in Elegant Weapon Repertoire, affordable but might not be as much damage as either WR or Snake if you are using Unarmed to deliver the blow. - +5 Withering damage (if artifact light weapon) or +4 Withering damage (if unarmed)<br /> <br /> <u>What Fire Has Wrought MAs:</u> Now for a Celestial, going whole hog on an Elemental Dragon style is... not to be recommended. The aura effects will never come into play. But... there are some unexpected gems here...<br /> <br /> <b>Earth Dragon Style </b><br /> <br /> Force of the Mountain / MA 3 / 3m:<br /> - Now I know what I said about Auras and it's still true. This is a high Essence purchase (for y'know theoretical games), where it becomes +5 withering damage for 3m, no strings attached. - + (Lower of Ess or Str) to withering damage<br /> <br /> <b>Wood Dragon Style</b><br /> <br /> Eyes of the Wood Dragon / MA 3 / 4m:<br /> - Not bad, not bad. If you have max Perception (a pretty nice stat for Lunars) this is a 1m discount on a full damage excellency. - + 5 Withering damage (if you have 5 Perception)<br /> <br /> <u>Fangs at the Gate MAs</u>: ...unfortunately out of all the styles there, nothing fits this specific purpose. But you do have:<br /> <br /> Deadly Beastman Transformation / 5m, 1wp (effectively)<br /> - Now the strength of DBT is undeniable, +5 Withering, +5 Soak, if 5 Str, but it is Simple Action activation unlike everything else on this list. Still, if you can buff up before combat, accept no substitutes.<br /> <br /> Strength Excellency / 5m for +5 Withering damage.<br /> - Basic bread and butter withering damage booster for Lunars (and only Lunars)<br /> <br /> Phew, so lets list the effects in terms of mote cost (to determine the sliding scale of what to use when).<br /> <br /> <b>Striking Cobra 3m / 5 damage (Dex)</b><br /> <b>Elegant Weapon Repertoire 3m / 4 damage (if unarmed) or 5 damage (if artifact)</b><br /> Force of the Mountain 3m / 1 damage (based on Ess until Ess 5)<br /> <b>Eyes of the Wood Dragon 4m / 5 damage (Per)</b><br /> <b>Falling Scythe Slash 5m / 5 damage (Str)<br /> Strength Excellency 5m / 5 damage</b><br /> DBT 5m 1wp / 5 damage (and other things if 5 Str)<br /> Tiger Form 10m / 5 damage (up to Str extra successes doubled)<br /> <br /> So for an unarmed Lunar MAist with 5 Str you could:<br /> <br /> Value Option (Striking Cobra and Elegant Weapon Repertoire): +7 (Unarmed) + 5 (Base Str) + 5 (Striking Cobra) + 4 (Elegant Weapon) = 21 base damage for 6m<br /> <br /> &quot;You're going down&quot; Option (as Value option + Eyes of the Wood Dragon) = 26 base damage for 10m<br /> <br /> &quot;All In&quot; (as &quot;You're going down&quot; + Falling Scythe Slash + Str Excellency) = 36 base damage for 20m<br /> <br /> And of course if you do have a round to prepare and can use DBT (or just devote round one to it) all the above values go up by +5.<br /> <br /> Okay, now to see what I can build around this...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":8959,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8959-prototype00","user":"prototype00","date":". 01-19-2020, 11:19 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8959-prototype00","name":"prototype00","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8959_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"964"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-19T08:34:21-08:00","id":1361902,"title":"","content":"How many attributes at 5 do you need for that? Str, Dex and Per?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-19T08:35:51-08:00","id":1361903,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1293395-ex-3-lunars-glorious-argent-beastiary-a-lunar-s-character-thread?p=1361902#post1361902\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How many attributes at 5 do you need for that? Str, Dex and Per?</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, more or less. Per can do double duty as JB attribute and is generally boss for Lunars so it's no big sacrifice when I was thinking about it, but I may of course be making too light of 3 attributes at 5.<br /> <br /> Edit: Having all the above charms is insane, btw, both in terms of ability cost and the number of charms you can get at chargen. I'd space out this progression over a couple of essence levels, maybe pick the cheaper options mote-wise first.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8959-prototype00","name":"prototype00","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8959_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"964"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-19T10:01:24-08:00","id":1361924,"title":"","content":"I don't think 3 Attributes at 5 is a big expense for Lunars, you can start with a load if you really want, and they are useful; if you're the kind of Lunar who wants to do this build, you'll want Str 5 and Dex 5 anyway. I was just checking.<br /> Whereas all those different MA styles is a serious cost.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-19T16:26:04-08:00","id":1362010,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1293395-ex-3-lunars-glorious-argent-beastiary-a-lunar-s-character-thread?p=1361924#post1361924\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't think 3 Attributes at 5 is a big expense for Lunars, you can start with a load if you really want, and they are useful; if you're the kind of Lunar who wants to do this build, you'll want Str 5 and Dex 5 anyway. I was just checking.<br /> Whereas all those different MA styles is a serious cost.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, completely agree. <br /> <br /> I\u2019m thinking of starting with... 3 at 3? Tiger, Snake and DPC. That should leave me with an... acceptable number of ability dots to play with and the rest of the MA dots hopefully can be picked up in play.<br /> <br /> Then next comes Wood Dragon (all the value options first) then White Reaper...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8959-prototype00","name":"prototype00","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8959_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"964"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-19T21:11:28-08:00","id":1362050,"title":"","content":"Of course the bugbear of this particular character concept is: Wouldn\u2019t Overwhelming 5 on a heavy artifact weapon do probably just as much damage with no more expenditure on a high soak foe?<br /> <br /> I mean realistically this character does better (more accurate and pips the damage), but it costs a fair amount of resources.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8959-prototype00","name":"prototype00","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8959_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"964"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-20T10:12:31-08:00","id":1362146,"title":"","content":"Hmmm... I guess that makes it an interesting trade-off. This character can throw out devastating attacks... for a short time.<br /> While Strength McBrawn the grand goremaul-wielding Full Moon can throw out good damage (but not amazing over a long time.<br /> <br /> Which... probably doesn't make much sense for a light vs heavy fighter, but nevermind.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-20T13:18:37-08:00","id":1362207,"title":"","content":"Fighting in horse form; yay or neigh?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-20T14:00:30-08:00","id":1362220,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1293395-ex-3-lunars-glorious-argent-beastiary-a-lunar-s-character-thread?p=1362207#post1362207\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Fighting in horse form; yay or neigh?</div> </div> </div> </div>If you get another Exalt to use Ride Charms on you, then yay all the way.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25285-epitome","name":"Epitome","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25285_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"754"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-20T14:06:59-08:00","id":1362221,"title":"","content":"The only other character with Ride charms rides her Dragon familiar, so I am thinking without Ride charms, but it's a very good point.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-20T14:07:55-08:00","id":1362223,"title":"","content":"I'd say neigh. Claw strider OTOH has some amazing bonuses if someone's riding you and you grab Quicksilver Steed Unity. Pack Hunting is bananas.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2579-limaxophobiac","name":"limaxophobiac","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"294"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-20T14:19:32-08:00","id":1362229,"title":"","content":"Why neigh? Just nothing useful? I remember horses have a great speed bonus, and some kind of prone-infliction. Don't remember much of the rest of their stats (no book right now). <br /> <br /> Can you remind me the basics of Quicksilver Steed Mastery?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-20T14:29:32-08:00","id":1362232,"title":"","content":"Horses are fast but thats about it. They have really bad soak (3), and the prone infliction only works against enemies 'smaller than human size' which really limits its usefullness. Other than that and swift-hooved they have no merits or special attacks.<br /> <br /> Elk OTOH are just as fast as horses, with 6 soak, also have swift-hooved, plus the Gore, Trample, and Horn Toss abilities that are actually usefull.<br /> <br /> Quicksilver Steed Unity is a 1m reflexive charm that lets you do your choice of a bunch of things either for your mount or your rider, including reflexively Defend Other, reflexively make a distract gambit (which even if distract gambits are usually pretty bad is a free extra attack for 1m which is probably worth it just for the unslaught), or increase the difficulty of an unhorse gambit.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2579,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2579-limaxophobiac","user":"limaxophobiac","date":". 01-20-2020, 05:32 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2579-limaxophobiac","name":"limaxophobiac","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"294"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-20T17:08:31-08:00","id":1362276,"title":"","content":"Does speed do anything for a lunar that isn't being ridden? I don't see any rule saying it gets added to your movement pool. I guess you can use a horse's 12 die combat movement, but if you have good stats of your own it's only a small boost, and probably not worth the poor soak, and mediocre damage. I guess it's good to have if you have Quicksilver Second form in case you need it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23597-autxauty","name":"autXautY","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"286"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-20T17:26:52-08:00","id":1362282,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1293395-ex-3-lunars-glorious-argent-beastiary-a-lunar-s-character-thread?p=1362146#post1362146\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hmmm... I guess that makes it an interesting trade-off. This character can throw out devastating attacks... for a short time.<br /> While Strength McBrawn the grand goremaul-wielding Full Moon can throw out good damage (but not amazing over a long time.<br /> <br /> Which... probably doesn't make much sense for a light vs heavy fighter, but nevermind.</div> </div> </div> </div>If I actually were to play this character I\u2019d just go for the value option most of the time. Accurate 21-26 (w/DBT) raw damage attacks for 6m are nice.<br /> <br /> And y\u2019know when you need 10+ raw damage post soak to crash a legendary sized foe...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":8959,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8959-prototype00","user":"prototype00","date":". 01-20-2020, 08:36 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8959-prototype00","name":"prototype00","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8959_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"964"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-20T17:28:52-08:00","id":1362283,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>autXautY</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1293395-ex-3-lunars-glorious-argent-beastiary-a-lunar-s-character-thread?p=1362276#post1362276\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Does speed do anything for a lunar that isn't being ridden? I don't see any rule saying it gets added to your movement pool. I guess you can use a horse's 12 die combat movement, but if you have good stats of your own it's only a small boost, and probably not worth the poor soak, and mediocre damage. I guess it's good to have if you have Quicksilver Second form in case you need it.</div> </div> </div> </div>I seem to recall asking this to Vance. <br /> <br /> If Horse native pool&gt; yours, use that. Speed bonus is already included.<br /> <br /> If your native pool &gt; Horse, use yours and add the Speed Bonus. It counts as charm dice as per the rules.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8959-prototype00","name":"prototype00","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8959_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"964"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-20T19:14:09-08:00","id":1362316,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>prototype00</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1293395-ex-3-lunars-glorious-argent-beastiary-a-lunar-s-character-thread?p=1362283#post1362283\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I seem to recall asking this to Vance.<br /> <br /> If Horse native pool&gt; yours, use that. Speed bonus is already included.<br /> <br /> If your native pool &gt; Horse, use yours and add the Speed Bonus. It counts as charm dice as per the rules.</div> </div> </div> </div>Which results in weird stuff when your pool if larger than (native pool - speed bonus) of a creature, but smaller than native pool itself.<br /> <br /> Fe.x. if you have a 10 dice pool yourself you would have 12 dice as a horse (12 dice native, +4 speed bonus), but 14 dice as an elk (9 dice native, also +4 speed bonus), so turning into the animal that is natively the slower one makes you faster.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2579,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2579-limaxophobiac","user":"limaxophobiac","date":". 01-21-2020, 12:19 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2579-limaxophobiac","name":"limaxophobiac","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"294"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-20T22:43:38-08:00","id":1362345,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>limaxophobiac</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1293395-ex-3-lunars-glorious-argent-beastiary-a-lunar-s-character-thread?p=1362316#post1362316\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Which results in weird stuff when your pool if larger than (native pool - speed bonus) of a creature, but smaller than native pool itself.<br /> <br /> Fe.x. if you have a 10 dice pool yourself you would have 12 dice as a horse (12 dice native, +4 speed bonus), but 14 dice as an elk (9 dice native, also +4 speed bonus), so turning into the animal that is natively the slower one makes you faster.</div> </div> </div> </div>It also results in the absolute nonsense that a Lunar horse is slower than a Lunar on a totally normal horse.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25764-vwllss-trnt-prncss","name":"vwllss trnt prncss","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"244"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-21T05:30:52-08:00","id":1362378,"title":"","content":"That's a general issue with Lunars; a Lunar tyrant lizard is probably significantly worse at attacking and has far worse health than a regular Tyrant Lizard, except when throwing down a combo.<br /> I understand it from a balance perspective, but it can be weird.<br /> <br /> Anyway, sounds like a horse-totem Lunar should fight in Centaur form then. That's a bit of a pity, but doesn't surprise me.<br /> Are there any Protean charms that at least let you get something good out of the horse's speed? I'm sure I recall something like that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-21T06:54:12-08:00","id":1362388,"title":"","content":"I'm trying to think if it's even possible for a Lunar to have as high a base pool as a horse, to get that free 4 dice (obviously you could also have a Dex+Athletics pool of 8 or lower).<br /> I guess maybe if you had Dex 5, Athletics 5, a specialty in &quot;being a horse&quot; and the Fleet of Foot merit? I can't think how else.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-21T07:06:18-08:00","id":1362390,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>limaxophobiac</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1293395-ex-3-lunars-glorious-argent-beastiary-a-lunar-s-character-thread?p=1362316#post1362316\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Which results in weird stuff when your pool if larger than (native pool - speed bonus) of a creature, but smaller than native pool itself.<br /> <br /> Fe.x. if you have a 10 dice pool yourself you would have 12 dice as a horse (12 dice native, +4 speed bonus), but 14 dice as an elk (9 dice native, also +4 speed bonus), so turning into the animal that is natively the slower one makes you faster.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sounds like an oversight to me. I can't think of any reason, balance or otherwise, why you couldn't get the speed bonus the moment you beat the creature's native dice. So if the Lunar has 9 dice just give them 13 as a horse, 4 of which are Charm dice.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25285-epitome","name":"Epitome","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25285_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"754"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-21T10:26:29-08:00","id":1362446,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epitome</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1293395-ex-3-lunars-glorious-argent-beastiary-a-lunar-s-character-thread?p=1362390#post1362390\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Sounds like an oversight to me. I can't think of any reason, balance or otherwise, why you couldn't get the speed bonus the moment you beat the creature's native dice. So if the Lunar has 9 dice just give them 13 as a horse, 4 of which are Charm dice.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Yeah. 'Whichever is higher of animals pool or your pool + speed bonus, counting everything over your pool as charm dice' would be very simple and straightforward.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2579-limaxophobiac","name":"limaxophobiac","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"294"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-23T02:41:12-08:00","id":1362828,"title":"","content":"This thread is quite long now, with a lot of stuff going on... Would anyone be willing to make a kind of &quot;top 10&quot; animal forms for Lunars? Including choices for different tactics (grappling, soak, poison, fear, ambush, Legendary Size, etc).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":2402,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","user":"The Wizard of Oz","date":". 01-23-2020, 06:43 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-23T04:19:56-08:00","id":1362843,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1293395-ex-3-lunars-glorious-argent-beastiary-a-lunar-s-character-thread?p=1362828#post1362828\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This thread is quite long now, with a lot of stuff going on... Would anyone be willing to make a kind of &quot;top 10&quot; animal forms for Lunars? Including choices for different tactics (grappling, soak, poison, fear, ambush, Legendary Size, etc).</div> </div> </div> </div>I humbly leave this for someone else to create as I don\u2019t have the full beastiary in front of me (waiting for the collected HDNP).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8959-prototype00","name":"prototype00","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8959_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"964"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-23T06:15:16-08:00","id":1362864,"title":"","content":"Do you have any of them?<br /> <br /> I made a list the other day. HDNP's releases so far include:<br /> <br /> Strix<br /> Elephant/Mammoth<br /> Metagalapan Riding Hawk (and Roc, which is an upgraded version)<br /> Armoured Kraken<br /> Giant Constrictor<br /> Bat<br /> Sky Titan<br /> Eight-Tailed Molehound<br /> Aurochs<br /> Austrech<br /> Forest Strider (giant stick insect)<br /> Northern Ursidae (it's an aquatic bear)<br /> <br /> The Kraken is the best form for Naval Combat. Because it has good stats, grappling powers, and... essentially is one of only two animals that can do Naval Combat at all.<br /> <br /> The Elephant is a very strong form. It has good stats, can gore (add extra successes on decisive if you do no other actions), and has Trample, which IIRC there are a fair few Protean charms for. But I imagine that the Tyrant Lizard (gated behind the same charm) is a bit better? Elephants can spend a wp to flurry a withering and decisive attack against different targets, which combo'd with the Lunar charm for ignoring flurry penalties might be good.<br /> <br /> The Sky Titan is the fastest form for long travel (80 miles an hour for up to 10 days), and its Legendary Size, and has some powers for resetting initiative to higher levels. But the stats aren't as good as land-dwelling Legendary Size creatures.<br /> <br /> For the non-Legendary Size creatures, I'm not sure.<br /> The Aurochs doesn't have brilliant stats (Soak 7, Damage 15, not terrible or amazing). But it has a lot of abilities: Gore, Deadly Charge, Horn Toss, Trample, Sturdy as Stone. As I said, I think there's some Trample Protean effects, but I'm not very familiar with them. Maybe it can be made good with Protean charms?<br /> The Northern Ursidae are pretty much the same as bears except without the Grapple abilities. So still a berzerker, but not the best berzerker. However, they have this ability which looks really good to me, if you combo it with intimidation charms and that Latent where people lose initiative when you intimidate them?<br /> &quot;Roaring Charge (Latent): After moving at least one<br /> range band toward a target on the ursidae\u2019s current<br /> turn, roll Intimidate against the target\u2019s Resolve as a<br /> miscellaneous action. If successful, the enemy reflexively<br /> flees one range band in the opposite direction,<br /> and the bear or its rider receives one automatic<br /> success on the next attack roll against anyone who<br /> witnessed the charge.&quot;<br /> As it's a miscallaneous action, I guess it can be flurried with an attack?<br /> <br /> The others are all meh. Not necessarily bad, but they're no Moose.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-23T09:46:58-08:00","id":1362904,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1293395-ex-3-lunars-glorious-argent-beastiary-a-lunar-s-character-thread?p=1362828#post1362828\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This thread is quite long now, with a lot of stuff going on... Would anyone be willing to make a kind of &quot;top 10&quot; animal forms for Lunars? Including choices for different tactics (grappling, soak, poison, fear, ambush, Legendary Size, etc).</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I don't own all the HDNPs but I'll make an attempt, splitting legendary size and the rest because the mote/wp investment and practical problems of being huge means they have to be a lot better than non-Legendary size animals to be worth it. Also I'll need a break in between.<br /> <br /> In general by my judgement powerfull special ablities and merits &gt;&gt; big dicepools. This is assuming you get brawl 5 dex 5 and a specialty. If you don't max your combat dicepools animals with big pools like Elephants get more interesting.<br /> <br /> Legendary Size:<br /> <br /> 1. Tyrant Lizard, for many reasons. Best ledendary size grappler. IMO the strongest form there is.<br /> <br /> -Deadly Thrash is bananas. Deadly thrash lets you get around one of the core mechanics of the 3e combat system; making decisive attacks normally leaves you vulnerable to initiative shift and you have to make withering attacks to work up the initiative for another decisive. Then it also doubles your initiative for damage. Like either one of those would be great getting both is nuts.<br /> <br /> (Look at the tiger-style E3 charm Prey-Maiming Frenzy, at 8m 1wp. While they're a bit different with one enhancing a savaging and the other a slam, Deadly Thrash is pretty clearly superior, while being free as long as you're in tyrant lizard form.)<br /> <br /> As long as no one crashes you and you keep landing your grapples and spend a couple motes on the control roll, you could just keep Deadly Thrashing every round for ~20 decisive damage against anything that isn't legendary size (or one of the ~10 or so solar brawl grapplers in creation).<br /> <br /> -Apex Predator. Most animals like f.ex. Elephants have to spend WP for their best attacks. Tyrant Lizards OTOH actually gain WP when they use their big attacks<br /> <br /> -Terrifying Dragon Roar: I already made a post on how stupid this gets if you can stack it with predators menace. If you (sanely) rule that you can't stack them it still automatically defeats any number of mortals who automatically flee with no chance of resistance.<br /> <br /> -Furius Rampage: 3 auto successes on attacks against crashed enemies really is quite a lot. Very likely to be active after you use Dragon Roar and/or Predators Menace.<br /> <br /> 2. Sky Tyrant. High mobility with ability to attack at short range. Bad soak/hardness for legendary size but you can get around that. Overall a weaker but more mobile (and stylish) alternative to T-Rex.<br /> <br /> -Spine-Shattering Emperors Beak: Can attack from short range and reset at 6, or make withering attacks that hit as hard as a hippos from the same range.<br /> <br /> -Clamp Down: Resetting at higher initiative is as previously noted quite good. But it's no Deadly Thrash.<br /> <br /> -Horizon Sweeping Wingspan: The basic damage of wings is only 14 but lunars have great withering boosters and when you're hitting multiple people with one attack its worth stacking them up. Since the option to flurry it with a decisive doesn't say anything about not taking flurry penalties its probably not worth the WP unless you take extra limb mutations and the charm that reduces flurry penalties.<br /> <br /> -Fearsome Display: If you buy predators menace its pretty much Terrifying Dragon Roar, and unlike TDR you don't need to spend 6xp for a latent limited to one animal.<br /> <br /> 3. Siege Lizard. Tough, hits hard. Access to a really good solar charm at reduced cost.<br /> <br /> -Spiked Tail Slam: It's Heaven Thunder Hammer, a notorious solar charm at 7m, for 2i (ok also a defense penalty but you'll find some way around it). At E2+ with Octopus and Spider Barrage it really gets crazy when you HTH 3-5 times in one round for 8m, 1wp, 6i-10i. At E3+ with Running Through the Herd you could juggle some sucker over 4-5 range bands with repeated hits.<br /> <br /> -Death Stomp: If you only want to HTH the first of your Octopus and Spider Barrage attacks, you can do the rest of them with this against your now prone opponent for +5 damage on each attack. Lunars also have some decent charms to prone people with like Tiger Claw Swat.<br /> <br /> Edit: I missremembered the cost of smashing attacks, its 2i not 1i.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2579,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2579-limaxophobiac","user":"limaxophobiac","date":". 01-24-2020, 04:48 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2579-limaxophobiac","name":"limaxophobiac","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"294"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-23T10:10:43-08:00","id":1362908,"title":"","content":"Thanks!<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> At E3+ with Thousand Claw Affliction you could juggle some sucker over 4-5 range bands with repeated hits. </div> </div> </div> Oh man, didn't think of that, but yeah.<br /> <br /> Is the Siege Lizard an Anklosaur? I think they look pretty cool.<br /> <br /> The Sky Tyrant I think is pretty fun, but... I'll be honest, I think it looks kind of stupid. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> That's just personal taste.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-23T10:53:51-08:00","id":1362914,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1293395-ex-3-lunars-glorious-argent-beastiary-a-lunar-s-character-thread?p=1362908#post1362908\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Thanks!<br /> <br /> Oh man, didn't think of that, but yeah.<br /> <br /> Is the Siege Lizard an Anklosaur? I think they look pretty cool.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm pretty sure they're Stegosaurs.<br /> <br /> Shieldback Lizard in Lunars is an Anklosaur.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1293395-ex-3-lunars-glorious-argent-beastiary-a-lunar-s-character-thread?p=1362908#post1362908\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Thanks!<br /> <br /> The Sky Tyrant I think is pretty fun, but... I'll be honest, I think it looks kind of stupid. <br /></div> </div> </div> </div>I'm not a huge fan of the illustration but I'd just use some other drawing of a Quetzalcoatlus which is what they're based of and imagine some hard scales on it.<br /> <br /> I'll finish my top 10 tomorrow because I'm tired and the site is loading painfully slow right now.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2579-limaxophobiac","name":"limaxophobiac","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"294"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-23T12:43:52-08:00","id":1362936,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1293395-ex-3-lunars-glorious-argent-beastiary-a-lunar-s-character-thread?p=1362864#post1362864\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Do you have any of them?<br /> <br /> I made a list the other day. HDNP's releases so far include:<br /> <br /> Strix<br /> Elephant/Mammoth<br /> Metagalapan Riding Hawk (and Roc, which is an upgraded version)<br /> Armoured Kraken<br /> Giant Constrictor<br /> Bat<br /> Sky Titan<br /> Eight-Tailed Molehound<br /> Aurochs<br /> Austrech<br /> Forest Strider (giant stick insect)<br /> Northern Ursidae (it's an aquatic bear)<br /> <br /> The Kraken is the best form for Naval Combat. Because it has good stats, grappling powers, and... essentially is one of only two animals that can do Naval Combat at all.<br /> <br /> The Elephant is a very strong form. It has good stats, can gore (add extra successes on decisive if you do no other actions), and has Trample, which IIRC there are a fair few Protean charms for. But I imagine that the Tyrant Lizard (gated behind the same charm) is a bit better? Elephants can spend a wp to flurry a withering and decisive attack against different targets, which combo'd with the Lunar charm for ignoring flurry penalties might be good.<br /> <br /> The Sky Titan is the fastest form for long travel (80 miles an hour for up to 10 days), and its Legendary Size, and has some powers for resetting initiative to higher levels. But the stats aren't as good as land-dwelling Legendary Size creatures.<br /> <br /> For the non-Legendary Size creatures, I'm not sure.<br /> The Aurochs doesn't have brilliant stats (Soak 7, Damage 15, not terrible or amazing). But it has a lot of abilities: Gore, Deadly Charge, Horn Toss, Trample, Sturdy as Stone. As I said, I think there's some Trample Protean effects, but I'm not very familiar with them. Maybe it can be made good with Protean charms?<br /> The Northern Ursidae are pretty much the same as bears except without the Grapple abilities. So still a berzerker, but not the best berzerker. However, they have this ability which looks really good to me, if you combo it with intimidation charms and that Latent where people lose initiative when you intimidate them?<br /> &quot;Roaring Charge (Latent): After moving at least one<br /> range band toward a target on the ursidae\u2019s current<br /> turn, roll Intimidate against the target\u2019s Resolve as a<br /> miscellaneous action. If successful, the enemy reflexively<br /> flees one range band in the opposite direction,<br /> and the bear or its rider receives one automatic<br /> success on the next attack roll against anyone who<br /> witnessed the charge.&quot;<br /> As it's a miscallaneous action, I guess it can be flurried with an attack?<br /> <br /> The others are all meh. Not necessarily bad, but they're no Moose.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Lol, not a one. I'm patient I am, but that also makes me useless for this.<br /> <br /> &quot;Roaring Charge (Latent): After moving at least one<br /> range band toward a target on the ursidae\u2019s current<br /> turn, roll Intimidate against the target\u2019s Resolve as a<br /> miscellaneous action. If successful, the enemy reflexively<br /> flees one range band in the opposite direction,<br /> and the bear or its rider receives one automatic<br /> success on the next attack roll against anyone who<br /> witnessed the charge.&quot;<br /> As it's a miscallaneous action, I guess it can be flurried with an attack?<br /> <br /> As to this, I can tell you that you are... probably still better off getting the Predator's Menace Latent. This one has wording that specifically affects one target (I mean, it can be flurried with a decisive, sure) but the Predator's Menace can affect everyone you are fighting with (thanks to Lunar multi-target social interaction charms) and crash them.<br /> <br /> prototype00","signature":"","edited":{"userid":8959,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8959-prototype00","user":"prototype00","date":". 01-23-2020, 03:50 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8959-prototype00","name":"prototype00","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8959_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"964"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-23T14:29:17-08:00","id":1362954,"title":"","content":"Ah, good point. I was thinking about specific animals intimidation powers, but I guess you can just use Predator's Menace on a normal intimidation, roll against all enemies, and ignore the -3 penalty with Argent Muse.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>limaxophobiac</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1293395-ex-3-lunars-glorious-argent-beastiary-a-lunar-s-character-thread?p=1362914#post1362914\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I'm pretty sure they're Stegosaurs.<br /> <br /> Shieldback Lizard in Lunars is an Anklosaur.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ah, you're right. Hmmm... Shieldback Lizards have slightly higher damage, but it's probably not as good as Heaven Thunder Hammer, and their soak isn't as good.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <br /> I'll finish my top 10 tomorrow because I'm tired and the site is loading painfully slow right now. </div> </div> </div>No worries, no rush.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-23T17:45:48-08:00","id":1362979,"title":"","content":"Ok continuing with non-legendary size because I don't think the other LS animals measure up to those first 3, except Kraken for underwater and naval combat but that's going to be pretty niche in most campaigns. Also an honorable mention to walruses for non legendary-size aquatic forms but again that's kinda niche.<br /> <br /> 4. Hippopotamus: Offensive powerhouse. Amazing persistent withering and decisive attack bonuses.<br /> <br /> -Downsides: Not the best creature for Predators Menace since they don't get the protean bonus for Terrifying Bestial Visage. Might be nerfed when Lunars is actually released.<br /> <br /> -Crushing Bite: Because 19L wasn't nearly enough, lets ignore 4 + margin of success soak on top of that. Unlike piercing attacks not limited to soak from armor so the bite is practically just 23L and double extra successes for damage against mid-high soak enemies.<br /> <br /> -Bone-Crunching Bite: Anyone you bite is cursed with scene-long suck unless they can ignore crippling penalties. Wonky interaction with the fact that hippos can grapple since its based on margin of success. Having a crippling attack also gives you the protean effect of Limb-Maiming Flourish (E2 lunar decisive damage adder), which means you get the WP you spend on it back if incapacitate your foe.<br /> <br /> 5. Pestletail: The tankiest of tanks, high soak and reduce min damage by 1. If it wasn't for the defensive benefits of legendary size itself it would be tankier than any of the legendary size animals with its latents. One of the best forms for a combat sorceror.<br /> <br /> -Downside are it's best abilities are Latent so you're going to have to spend some xp and you can't use Predators Menace since it has no intimidation pool.<br /> <br /> -Hardened Shell Superiority: This right here is what it's all about. Like 3-4 permanent solar charms worth of effect for 6xp; does everything Searing Quicksilver Flight + Force-Stealing Feint does while working with either parry or evasion, plus it also works when an attack hits you but fails to deal damage, plus an extra 4 initiative if its a decisive attack.<br /> <br /> -Bony Shell: If you're a sorceror and aquire the natural shield mutation, this + Shadow-Hands Invocation lets you flurry Full Defense + Shape Sorcery with no defense penalty and no initiative cost for 2m/round and give you Soak/Hardness: 21/14 in addition to the normal +2 defense. Combined with Ferocious Guardian Beast Stance* you make yourself and your ward a nightmare to attack.<br /> <br /> -Smashing Tail Hammer: It's Heaven Thunder Hammer again, but this time it costs xp to learn and WP to use so its down from amazing to pretty good.<br /> <br /> -Claw Stomp: Like Death Stomp this is amazing if you can prone someone and then throw an Octopus-and-Spider Barrage at them.<br /> <br /> *This and War Lion Stance seem to me sometimes underrated charms, they're not bad if you're all combat badasses; they let you keep eachother safe when you go all-out offensive incurring defense penalties and resetting to base initiative. Also for Lunars it significantly improves your penalty negators.<br /> <br /> 6. Cats: Tiny ninja warriors. Can be ninja sorcerors if you want them to be since the attack bonus as-written works with spells that make attack rolls.<br /> <br /> -Downsides: You have to rely on your own strength, stamina, and artifacts for damage and soak/hardness. The aesthetic might get old after a fight or two (IMO aesthetically it works better if you go for combat sorcery but obviously tastes differ).<br /> <br /> -Underfoot Menace + Tiny Creature: This is why you're a cat. +2 evasion +3 attack against anything larger than you are. Persistently for the 4m commitment of shapeshanging.<br /> <br /> -Tiny-Creature + Ambush Hunter: A lot of lunar stealth charms have protean bonuses for being an Ambush Hunter. A few other stealth and defensive Dex charms have protean effects for being TIny. Cat's are the only tiny ambush hunters.<br /> <br /> 7. Strix: The flying grappler. I did a big writeup on them earlier in this thread so I'll try to keep things short.<br /> <br /> -Downsides: Non-functional indoors. Have to get your soak somewhere else because these guys only get 3.<br /> <br /> -The ability to Kraken-Arm Lash from Medium height, flying up to Long and carrying your victim while at the same time making a savaging attack and then dropping them is a very cost-effective way to deal a lot of decisive damage.<br /> <br /> -While doing the above you stay quite safe from most enemies on the ground since even if they've learned archery they still can only attack you every other round unless they have some charm that gets around the aim requirement.<br /> <br /> -You get some abilities that make you even scarrier at night when you can grapple from stealth.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2579,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2579-limaxophobiac","user":"limaxophobiac","date":". 01-23-2020, 09:05 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2579-limaxophobiac","name":"limaxophobiac","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"294"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-23T20:02:49-08:00","id":1362994,"title":"","content":"The Mote Efficiency of Kitty Cat combat would make Angels weep.<br /> <br /> Since they are the only Tiny Creature on the list so far, I think I\u2019m safe in also pointing out they have an inherent ability to EAT SUCCESSES on perception rolls to spot them (two).<br /> <br /> So yes, +4m commitment for +2 EV, +3 to hit and effectively +4 Stealth.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":8959,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8959-prototype00","user":"prototype00","date":". 01-23-2020, 11:11 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8959-prototype00","name":"prototype00","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8959_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"964"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-23T20:56:12-08:00","id":1363004,"title":"","content":"8. Hellboar. The berserker. Decent but not as good as Hippo or Pestletai as a primary combat form, but it's great to slip into with Quicksilver Second Face at the same time as you activate Relentless Lunar Fury when someone puts you down to your -2 or -4 health levels.<br /> <br /> -Downsides: Mediocre withering damage and soak.<br /> <br /> -Berserker: Lunars can have a lot of -2 or -4 health levels with their ox-body* and when you're at those health levels this is a ton of free dice.<br /> <br /> *Side note ox-body for lunars is a better purchase than it is for solars since 1. lunars have an easier time getting Sta 5 and it gives them 4 health levels if they do, and 2. lunar charms are generally weaker than solar charms so the opportunity cost is lower.<br /> <br /> -Death stomp: Again lunars have some decent ways to prone people and if you also have berserker active you can roll an Octopus-and-Spider Barrage with a lot of free attack and damage dice on a prone opponent with this.<br /> <br /> -Bone Crunching BIte: Same as for HIppos except Hellboars can't grapple.<br /> <br /> 9. Chimeric Spidersquid: The poison assassin.<br /> <br /> -Downsides: Need use tiny-octopus as base spirit shape and take the chimeric charm for Extra Limbs and Enhanced Toxin mutations and pick up Shifting Breath Inversion to move at full speed on land with no penalties. Like a cat it needs last-warriors unity for withering attacks (and even then some might rule those weapons should do less damage when you're tiny anyway) and soak, also aesthetically its an aquired taste.<br /> <br /> -Poison: With Enhanced Toxin mutation and Mamba-and-Cobra the octopus poison is doing 4i Aggravated with a 6+essence+(10s on attack and damage roll) duration and -1 penalty for 3m 2i. The penalty is low but other than that it's a hell of a poison.<br /> <br /> -Stealth: With Skulking Rat Spirit, tiny size, and the Camouflage merit spidersquid rolls stealth with double 9s, rerolling 1s and 2s, and -2 successes on enemy rolls to notice it. That's more than a little stealthy.<br /> <br /> 10. Death Moa: Situational death machine. Again like Hellboar not the greatest main combat form, but in the right situation it's amazing to slip into with Quicksilver Second Face. That situation is when you want to finish of a crashed enemy. Once you get to E3 and can take Constant Quicksilver Rearrangement situational forms like this will really shine.<br /> <br /> -Downside: Mediocre withering damage and low soak.<br /> <br /> -Blade-Beak Frenzy + Furious Rampage: Against enemies in initiative crash Death Moas get 2 auto successes on attacks, plus extra successes and double 10s to damage on decisive attacks. Like all decisive boosting merits/abilities this gets nutty with Octopus-and-Spider Barrage.<br /> <br /> -Lunging Beak: Can make peck attacks and grapple from short range.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2579,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2579-limaxophobiac","user":"limaxophobiac","date":". 01-23-2020, 11:59 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2579-limaxophobiac","name":"limaxophobiac","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"294"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-23T21:05:47-08:00","id":1363007,"title":"","content":"Note: Tiny Creatures still use the same damage calculations as full sized creatures (Asked the devs.) but miniscule creatures can\u2019t do decisive damage even with spells against larger foes.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8959-prototype00","name":"prototype00","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8959_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"964"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-23T21:58:30-08:00","id":1363013,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>prototype00</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1293395-ex-3-lunars-glorious-argent-beastiary-a-lunar-s-character-thread?p=1362994#post1362994\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Mote Efficiency of Kitty Cat combat would make Angels weep.<br /> <br /> Since they are the only Tiny Creature on the list so far, I think I\u2019m safe in also pointing out they have an inherent ability to EAT SUCCESSES on perception rolls to spot them (two).<br /> <br /> So yes, +4m commitment for +2 EV, +3 to hit and effectively +4 Stealth.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's even better than +4 Stealth, since eating those successes dramatically increases the botch chance of anyone trying to find you. <br /> I was mathing out the traditional &quot;Housecat versus Commoner&quot; fight and the poor shmuck had a whopping 17% chance to botch his Perception roll even if he spent a WP.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25764-vwllss-trnt-prncss","name":"vwllss trnt prncss","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"244"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-24T15:27:51-08:00","id":1363206,"title":"","content":"Great stuff, Limaxaphobic, thanks!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-24T20:54:19-08:00","id":1363244,"title":"","content":"Thanks. I actually enjoyed writing it up. The ordering on the list is hardly definite and TBH the poison build is there because it's different and it's the highest damage poison build. Poison damage is really just too slow for exalted combat so even at 4 aggravated with a 8-10 duration it's just not all that effective.<br /> <br /> Actually I'll throw in a bit here about walruses which are actually quite amazing in their element and should probably have been on the list instead.<br /> <br /> 11. The mighty Walrus. Best non-legendary size aquatic combat form, not even that bad on land.<br /> <br /> -Downsided: Soak/Hardness 10/4 isn't great compared to what the best land-dweller can throw around.<br /> <br /> -Aquatic Grace: The great kitty-cats of the sea. +2 evasion and double 9s on all movement underwater. If this was on land they'd be up there with the hippos and pestletails no question.<br /> <br /> -Impenetrable Blubber: -1 min withering damage aint bad if you can raise your soak a bit over 10.<br /> <br /> -Impale: Withering tusk attacks ignore 4 soak, seemingly from any source including stamina. Given that very few combatants have less than 4 soak they might as well just have made the tusks 18L and saved some word count.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2579,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2579-limaxophobiac","user":"limaxophobiac","date":". 01-25-2020, 12:01 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2579-limaxophobiac","name":"limaxophobiac","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"294"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-24T21:26:53-08:00","id":1363248,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>limaxophobiac</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1293395-ex-3-lunars-glorious-argent-beastiary-a-lunar-s-character-thread?p=1363244#post1363244\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Poison damage is really just too slow for exalted combat so even at 4 aggravated with a 8-10 duration it's just not all that effective.</div> </div> </div> </div>I\u2019ll have you know that if not for poison coursing through his veins during a fight with a fae cataphract, Knight Raiton almost certainly wouldn\u2019t have been knocked out.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-26T08:47:32-08:00","id":1363453,"title":"","content":"Anyone have commendations for the &quot;familiar 3&quot; rank animals you can get with Heart's Blood 2+, if the Lunar doesn't have Towering Beast Form?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2118-reminiscent-oasis","name":"Reminiscent Oasis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2118_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"158"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-26T09:13:18-08:00","id":1363456,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Reminiscent Oasis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1293395-ex-3-lunars-glorious-argent-beastiary-a-lunar-s-character-thread?p=1363453#post1363453\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Anyone have commendations for the &quot;familiar 3&quot; rank animals you can get with Heart's Blood 2+, if the Lunar doesn't have Towering Beast Form?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> It's definitely a tricky question! Given that great cats are canonically examples of a 2-dot familiar, it's tricky to find creatures that have better stats that aren't Legendary Size. Given that Lunars can take the form of mutated animals, you might end up having to draw from that well a fair bit - claim that you went into the Bordermarches and Sacred Hunted a tiger that was perpetually on fire or something. That said, there's a couple of creatures in the books that I'd peg as 3-dot Familiars without being Legendary Size.<ul><li>The pestletail doesn't have the dice pools for combat that a great cat does, but its damage is <i>very</i> nice, and its Smashing Tail Hammer latent ability is enough by itself to push it up to 3-dot Familiar for me.</li> <li>A hippopotamus, for similar reasons to the pestletail: high damage if it lands a hit, and an impressive natural ability in Bone-Crunching Bite.</li> <li>Northern ursidae (from Hundred Devils Night Parade) strike me as 3-dot familiars, since they're both very impressive bears <i>and</i> can swim underwater indefinitely.</li> </ul>Those are all I can find that I'd personally rate as 3-dot Familiars, though.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Interested in chatting with other Exalted fans online? Join us on the <a href=\"https://discord.gg/kGsyF5jhdy\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted Discord server</a>!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1533-kelly-pedersen","name":"Kelly Pedersen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1533_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"929"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-26T09:16:49-08:00","id":1363457,"title":"","content":"I suggested Pegasus to one of my PCs (ie a mutated horse with wings).<br /> <br /> Tbh though, my advice to someone without Mountainous Spirit Expression, or a plan to get it later, is to either a)take more 2-dot familiars, or b)don't buy 3 dots in Heart's Blood.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-26T09:24:03-08:00","id":1363461,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kelly Pedersen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1293395-ex-3-lunars-glorious-argent-beastiary-a-lunar-s-character-thread?p=1363456#post1363456\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> It's definitely a tricky question! Given that great cats are canonically examples of a 2-dot familiar, it's tricky to find creatures that have better stats that aren't Legendary Size. Given that Lunars can take the form of mutated animals, you might end up having to draw from that well a fair bit - claim that you went into the Bordermarches and Sacred Hunted a tiger that was perpetually on fire or something. That said, there's a couple of creatures in the books that I'd peg as 3-dot Familiars without being Legendary Size.<ul><li>The pestletail doesn't have the dice pools for combat that a great cat does, but its damage is <i>very</i> nice, and its Smashing Tail Hammer latent ability is enough by itself to push it up to 3-dot Familiar for me.</li> <li>A hippopotamus, for similar reasons to the pestletail: high damage if it lands a hit, and an impressive natural ability in Bone-Crunching Bite.</li> <li>Northern ursidae (from Hundred Devils Night Parade) strike me as 3-dot familiars, since they're both very impressive bears <i>and</i> can swim underwater indefinitely.</li> </ul>Those are all I can find that I'd personally rate as 3-dot Familiars, though.</div> </div> </div> </div>Just to note Kelly, all the animals you have mentioned are Familiar 2 creatures by word of Dev. <br /> <br /> It\u2019s been confirmed that to be Familiar 3, you either need Legendary Size or be a Familiar 2 creature with a magical ability.<br /> <br /> Familiar 1 creatures are anything you expect a Disney Princess to be cavorting with.<br /> <br /> To answer the OP: For Lunar Shapechange there is nothing canonical for a 3 dot. I\u2019d go with what Wizard says (forgive me it\u2019s early)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":8959,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8959-prototype00","user":"prototype00","date":". 01-26-2020, 12:54 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8959-prototype00","name":"prototype00","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8959_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"964"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-26T23:46:00-08:00","id":1363565,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>prototype00</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1293395-ex-3-lunars-glorious-argent-beastiary-a-lunar-s-character-thread?p=1363461#post1363461\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Familiar 1 creatures are anything you expect a Disney Princess to be cavorting with.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, except Jasmine. She's rocking Familiar 2.<br /> <br /> Thanks for the suggestions, everyone. I think we'll be going with the mutant variants of Familiar 2 animals for our game to help the players with high Heart's Blood but only Strength 2-3.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2118-reminiscent-oasis","name":"Reminiscent Oasis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2118_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"158"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-29T07:52:07-08:00","id":1363965,"title":"","content":"How do you guys rate the Armoured Terror for underwater combat? (Vs Kraken, hippo, river dragon, etc, I guess)<br /> <br /> It looks like it's got good damage (17+crushing bite) and soak (17, impenetrable armour).<br /> <br /> (Anyone know what animal it actually is?)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-29T08:43:22-08:00","id":1363969,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1293395-ex-3-lunars-glorious-argent-beastiary-a-lunar-s-character-thread?p=1363965#post1363965\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">(Anyone know what animal it actually is?)</div> </div> </div> </div>It's <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Dunkleosteus\" target=\"_blank\">Dunkleosteus</a>. (I don't have enough experience with underwater combat to really answer the rest of your question.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Interested in chatting with other Exalted fans online? Join us on the <a href=\"https://discord.gg/kGsyF5jhdy\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted Discord server</a>!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1533-kelly-pedersen","name":"Kelly Pedersen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1533_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"929"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-29T09:32:53-08:00","id":1363978,"title":"","content":"That's a pretty dangerous looking fish!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-07T08:21:26-08:00","id":1366027,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"font-size:14px\"><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The white speckled owl flew silently over the snow-capped peaks into the serene valley of Skandhar-Bhal, unerringly towards the cupola of the sacred stupa of Moon-that Fell.<br /> <br /> Vanamaithri winced from their lingering injury as they looked up, having sensed the eddy in the constant breezes that swept the valley.<br /> <br /> &quot;You could have warned me, Elder. It will take a season for the meadow to come back into flower.&quot; they said, favoring their broken ribs and looking at the great lashing gash that rent the field of wilted silver-bells carpeting the approach to the Chamber of Luna's Presence.<br /> <br /> &quot;She's a strange one.&quot; Vanamaithri continued, indicating a gently snoring mound of white fur and rippling muscle behind them. &quot;Every strike a killing blow, but not an ounce of aggression, all with a smile untrammeled by hate. Where did you dig her up?&quot;<br /> <br /> The owl alighted on a prayer flagstaff and regarded her in amusement.<br /> <br /> Then with a quicksilver unfolding, Lillith the Reaper-in-White spoke.<br /> <br /> <i>Once there was a maiden...<br /> who acknowledged a fickle master...<br /> &quot;I will teach you upon my return&quot;, they said...<br /> So she resolved to sleep until that day...<br /> Until an age had past and the master remembered themself,<br /> and dreamt of Great Yas once more. </i><br /> <br /> Vanamaithri was momentarily speechless, &quot;This child... &quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;waited three thousand five hundred years, yes.&quot; finished Lillith ruefully. </div> </div> </div><br /> <b>G'intora na Yas</b><br /> <br /> <img src=\"https://www.dropbox.com/s/h6qauupa9aycsn5/1420861211634.jpg?raw=1\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/></span><br /> <br /> So here she is, in all her glory. I do always like to include a bit of a narrative interlude. (Some liberties taken vis a vis Vanamaithri's current Essence and Charms)<br /> <br /> <b>Caste</b>: Full Moon<br /> <br /> <b>Concept</b>: Tiger-Tiger Stylist<br /> <br /> <b>Spirit Shape</b>: White Tiger / Mantis Shrimp<br /> <br /> <b>Tell</b>: Three pupils in each eye (Triple Polycoria)<br /> <br /> <u><b>Attributes</b></u><br /> <br /> Physical (Primary)<br /> Strength OOOOO<br /> Dexterity OOOOO (Caste)<br /> Stamina OOOOO (Caste) (9 bp spent)<br /> <br /> Social (Tertiary)<br /> Charisma OOOOO (Favored)<br /> Manipulation O<br /> Appearance OO<br /> <br /> Mental (Secondary)<br /> Perception OOOOO (Favored)<br /> Intelligence OO<br /> Wits OOO<br /> <br /> <u><b>Abilities</b></u><br /> <br /> MA: Tiger OOOOO (4 bp spent) (Specialty: Unarmed)<br /> MA: Dreaming Pearl Courtesan OOO<br /> MA: Snake OOO<br /> Athletics OOO (Specialty: Closing for the kill)<br /> Awareness OOO (Specialty: Eye of the Tiger)<br /> Presence OOO (Specialty: Untrammeled Smile)<br /> Dodge OO<br /> Socialize OO<br /> Integrity OO<br /> Resistance O<br /> Stealth O<br /> Linguistics O<br /> Brawl O<br /> <br /> <b><u>Merits</u></b><br /> <br /> Martial Arts OOOO<br /> Artifact (Moonsilver Silken Armor) OOOO<br /> Artifact (Yasal Crystal) OO<br /> Language (Old Realm)<br /> Hearthstone (Stone of Resilient Bamboo) OO (2 bp spent)<br /> Hearthstone (Gem of Crushing Might)<br /> (In Hybrid Body Transformation)<br /> - Unusual Hide OOOOO<br /> - Claw OOOO<br /> - Enhanced Sense (Sight) OOO<br /> <br /> <u><b>Charms</b></u><br /> <br /> <b>Tiger Style</b><br /> Crimson Leaping Cat Technique<br /> <br /> <b>Snake Style</b><br /> Striking Cobra Technique<br /> <br /> <b>Dreaming Pearl Courtesan</b><br /> Elegant Weapon Repertoire<br /> <br /> <b>Universal</b><br /> Hybrid Body Transformation<br /> Chimera Soul Expression<br /> <br /> <b>Strength</b><br /> Strength Excellency<br /> Deadly Beastman Transformation<br /> <br /> <b>Dexterity</b><br /> Dexterity Excellency<br /> Sinuous Striking Grace<br /> <br /> <b>Stamina</b><br /> Stamina Excellency<br /> Ox Body Technique<br /> Bear Sleep Technique<br /> <br /> <b>Charisma</b><br /> Charisma Excellency<br /> Arrogant Lion Bearing<br /> <br /> <b>Appearance</b><br /> Appearance Excellency<br /> Subtle Silver Declaration<br /> Moon's Hidden Face<br /> <br /> <b>Perception</b><br /> Perception Excellency<br /> Unwavering Predator's Eye<br /> <br /> <b>Wits</b><br /> Wits Excellency<br /> Desert Basilic Diadem<br /> Radiant Basilisc Jewel<br /> <br /> Phew, I think I'll pause there for the moment and go into how everything works together in the next post.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":8959,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8959-prototype00","user":"prototype00","date":". 02-07-2020, 12:00 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8959-prototype00","name":"prototype00","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8959_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"964"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-07T10:55:16-08:00","id":1366067,"title":"","content":"I asked you guys before for a &quot;top 10&quot; of animal forms, and you gave me:<br /> Tyrant Lizard<br /> Sky Tyrant<br /> Seige Lizard<br /> Hippo<br /> Pestletail<br /> Cat<br /> Strix<br /> Hellboar<br /> Chimeric Spidersquid<br /> Death Moa<br /> Walrus<br /> <br /> Besides of course the spidersquid, what mutations do you think would go great on each if these if you're playing a Chimera?<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-07T13:56:56-08:00","id":1366105,"title":"","content":"Unusual Hide is good for everything obviously (though of the above list Cat and Strix want it the most), as are four dot medium natural weapon like some horns or antlers for +1 brawl parry (though cats defend with evasion).<br /> <br /> For a pestletail maybe moose/elk for some big medium antlers with natural shield so you can flurry full defense without the flurry defense penalty or initiative cost.<br /> <br /> Vance has said Deadly Weaponry mutation can be applied to any natural weapon in the final product so that will be good for any animal. You could make your Hippo tusks piercing or chopping weapons on top of crushing bite for complete overkill withering attacks. Or make your Pestletail or Siege Lizard tail-slam Flexible to dunk on some Crane stylists.<br /> <br /> Imposing Features and/or Frighting Voice works well for any predatory form thats going to use Predators Menace and instill ties of fear to itself. So Sky Tyrant/Tyrant Lizard/Hellboar could use it.<br /> <br /> Chameleon is good for kitty to be even stealthier.<br /> <br /> Extra Limbs is good for anything that might want to flurry.<br /> <br /> Tempered By the Elements if an animal is chimeric with an animal native to a different environment is going to be really good if you find yourself in that environment a lot.<br /> <br /> Fast Reflexes if a nice merit that works as a mutation for some animals but requires you to start combat in your spirit shape which works fine for kitty but less so for spirit shapes that are inconvenient to stay most of the time.<br /> <br /> Centaur is a really good mutation but it's going to be a stretch to justify on anything but say a Gorilla.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2579,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2579-limaxophobiac","user":"limaxophobiac","date":". 02-08-2020, 05:14 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2579-limaxophobiac","name":"limaxophobiac","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"294"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-07T17:24:57-08:00","id":1366172,"title":"","content":"Its a trick I pulled for the build I just posted but Enhanced Senses (X) OOO gives you two extra dots to every Perception based roll using (X) sense.<br /> <br /> You can make Join Battle a Perception Based roll with the charm Unwavering Predator's eye. So if you can stunt it so that your keen eyesight gives you the edge when violence starts, its an automatic 2 free dice on every join battle. (More bang for your buck than the similarly priced Danger Awareness merit from the Ex3 core)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":8959,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8959-prototype00","user":"prototype00","date":". 02-08-2020, 12:25 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8959-prototype00","name":"prototype00","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8959_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"964"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-07T19:40:57-08:00","id":1366213,"title":"","content":"So continuing on for G'intora na Yas, the derived Statistics (pre-stunt)!<br /> <br /> <b>Defenses:</b><br /> Parry: 6 (7 in HBT due to Medium weapon Claw, which she can be in all the time due to Moon's Hidden Face, 6 in DBT)<br /> Evasion: 4<br /> Soak: 12 (17 in HBT, 22 in DBT) (5 Stamina + 2 Stone of Resilient Bamboo + 5 Silken Armor + 5 Unusual Hide in HBT + 5 Strength in DBT)<br /> Resolve: 4 (5 if social partner has Resolve &lt;5)<br /> Guile: 2<br /> Health Levels: 0, 3x(-1), 3x(-2), 3x(-4), Inc<br /> <br /> <b>Movement</b>:<br /> Rush: 9<br /> Disengage: 7<br /> <br /> <b>Offense</b>:<br /> Join Battle: 9 (11 if it can be stunted that keen eyesight contributes)<br /> Unarmed Attack: Accuracy +15, Base Damage +12, Overwhelming 1 (Bashing, Brawl, Grapple, Natural)<br /> Claw: Accuracy +13, Base Damage +14, Overwhelming 1 (Bashing, Brawl, Grapple, Natural)<br /> <br /> <b>General</b>:<br /> Essence: Personal (16/16), Peripheral (32/38), 6 committed (4 Silken Armor +1 Stone of Resilient Bamboo +1 Gem of Crushing Might)<br /> Willpower: 5<br /> <br /> <b>Intimacies</b>:<br /> Defining Tie: Martial Arts (Deep and Abiding Passion)<br /> Defining Principle: I will seek the guidance of my learned Silver Pact Elders and treasure their advice. (This was from her duel with Vanamaithri's Crane Style)<br /> Defining Principle: I cannot hate anyone who fights me with their whole soul!<br /> Major Tie: Luna (Gratitude and Reverence)<br /> Major Tie: The Slumbering Populace of the city in the Deep Wyld, Lost Yasal. (Protective Steadfastness)<br /> Major Tie: Lilith (Immense Respect and Admiration)<br /> Major Principle: The Strong defend the Weak.<br /> Minor Tie: Dragonblooded (Ambivalent Affection *The Royal Line of Yasal was historically Earth Aspected, as were both of her parents, doesn't change the fact that they are currently trying to kill her*)<br /> Minor Tie: The First Age (Nostalgic Longing)<br /> Minor Principle: I hate being called and treated as a Princess, even though that is technically what I am.<br /> <br /> All right I think that just about rounds her out. G'intora na Yas is a frightening combatant who is always at least in HBT (she can hide all her mutations with Moon's Hidden Face and just look like a, admittedly physically perfect, normal young adult), and who hits like a truck even at this stage with not even half of the martial arts charms that contribute to big withering damage.<br /> <br /> Her maximum withering damage output in DBT is: 12 (Base) + 5 (DBT) + 5 (Str Excellency) + 4 (DPC) + 5 (Snake) = 31 base withering damage for 11 motes expended<br /> <br /> In the short term she should pick up 3 points of MA: Wood Dragon so she can get Eyes of the Wood dragon and add her 5 perception onto the above,as well as rounding out her soak suite in Stamina and pick up the counterattack charm Coiled Serpent Strikes in Dexterity, so when she gets a massive bank of initiative with the above, she can turn around on the same turn and deal it back as a massive Decisive counterattack if anyone misses her.<br /> <br /> Of course she isn't completely optimized, I did make some concessions to backstory (Yasal Crystal) but overall, decently pleased. Simple concept, well executed.<br /> <br /> Also reasonably pleased that my basic guiding principle of Shonen Manga Heroine worked out quite well as a backbone to build her up.<br /> <br /> Anything I should have done differently?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":8959,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8959-prototype00","user":"prototype00","date":". 02-07-2020, 11:13 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8959-prototype00","name":"prototype00","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8959_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"964"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-08T06:42:52-08:00","id":1366309,"title":"","content":"Silent Movement is also good for making things even stealthier.<br /> <br /> Wings are fairly useful (and good for sorcerer-kitties to escape melee attacks. Also fly to medium range to escape ranged attacks, since sorcery skips aiming)<br /> <br /> Venomous and Poisonous blood might be good for combat","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23597-autxauty","name":"autXautY","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"286"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-11T08:35:51-08:00","id":1366987,"title":"","content":"Owls. Not the best stealth form, as they lack Tiny, but they've got great vision and they're good stealth-flyers.<br /> <br /> What Chimera mutations, if any, would be useful on them? I think Silent Movement probably doesn't fit, because, well, they kind of already have that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-11T08:55:12-08:00","id":1366993,"title":"","content":"If you are going for really, really big owls, then Constrictor obviously, so you can grab and go (and drop a deeb from 10 storeys up).<br /> <br /> prototype00","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8959-prototype00","name":"prototype00","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8959_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"964"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-11T09:03:46-08:00","id":1366996,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1293395-ex-3-lunars-glorious-argent-beastiary-a-lunar-s-character-thread?p=1366987#post1366987\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Owls. Not the best stealth form, as they lack Tiny, but they've got great vision and they're good stealth-flyers.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'd argue that <i>some</i> owls would have Tiny.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-11T09:09:26-08:00","id":1366997,"title":"","content":"Just a regular owl I'm afraid.<br /> <br /> I'm thinking Chameleon (for stealth), maybe Extra Limbs for some rush/disengage/attack stuff, combo'd with Wing-Rushing Strike? (And then peck out their eyes!) I know you can't flurry attacks and stealth (I have a feeling there might be a Lunar charm that gets around that). Maybe Natural Missile so you can attack from the air, since you're flying? There's probably other ways to do that though.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-11T09:10:42-08:00","id":1366998,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1293395-ex-3-lunars-glorious-argent-beastiary-a-lunar-s-character-thread?p=1366996#post1366996\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'd argue that <i>some</i> owls would have Tiny.</div> </div> </div> </div>I agree, but not the one I've got.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-18T14:11:06-07:00","id":1375482,"title":"","content":"Any great Chimaera combos for a DBT build?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-18T14:37:52-07:00","id":1375489,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1293395-ex-3-lunars-glorious-argent-beastiary-a-lunar-s-character-thread?p=1375482#post1375482\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Any great Chimaera combos for a DBT build?</div> </div> </div> </div>I saw a build for a Bird/Snake/Centaur hybrid Falcon Stylist. Every round it would try to grapple someone move up and drop them for falling damage. I can't seem to find it atm though.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25732-wrecksalot","name":"wrecksalot","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-18T14:57:27-07:00","id":1375495,"title":"","content":"Can't you only have 2 shapes?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-18T17:26:07-07:00","id":1375518,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1293395-ex-3-lunars-glorious-argent-beastiary-a-lunar-s-character-thread?p=1375495#post1375495\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Can't you only have 2 shapes?</div> </div> </div> </div>That was one of mine actually. It was just giant constrictor and hawk, Quetzalcoatl basically (the centaur I tacked on for the more dragon-y feel, it can be taken out).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8959-prototype00","name":"prototype00","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8959_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"964"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-20T16:23:06-07:00","id":1375872,"title":"","content":"Just a thought, using Chimera-Soul Expression to make your spirit shape a fusion of poisonous snake and a Crown-Of-Thorns starfish, and then using Mountainous Spirit Expression/Undaunted Behemoth Avatar to make it huge and scary, and you've got yourself a passable Orochi.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>She/Her pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12975-zealot_vedas","name":"Zealot_Vedas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12975_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"85"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-15T16:39:18-07:00","id":1381795,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>prototype00</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1293395-ex-3-lunars-glorious-argent-beastiary-a-lunar-s-character-thread?p=1327530#post1327530\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Regular Combat: If Old Scratch can\u2019t beat his 10 EV, my money\u2019s on Black Tom.<br /> <br /> Shapeshifting Combat: Whoever pulls out that \u201cHope\u201d bullshit first wins I expect.</div> </div> </div> </div>Overlooked this initially.<br /> <br /> Just to clarify: Morpheus saying &quot;I am hope&quot; was not bullshit. Choronzon, <i>as a demon</i>, has to acknowledge that <i>the whole model of Hell</i> presented is built on the foundation of hope. Hell would not be torment, if there were no Heaven to dream of. And every demon, from the least to the greatest, dreams of improving their lot in life (generally at the expense of others, yes, but...). <i>As a demon</i>, Choronzon <b>cannot</b> crush hope.<br /> <br /> \u200bAnd who better to drive that point home than the Endless embodiment of Dream?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-15T23:51:28-07:00","id":1381866,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1293395-ex-3-lunars-glorious-argent-beastiary-a-lunar-s-character-thread?p=1381795#post1381795\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Overlooked this initially.<br /> <br /> Just to clarify: Morpheus saying &quot;I am hope&quot; was not bullshit. Choronzon, <i>as a demon</i>, has to acknowledge that <i>the whole model of Hell</i> presented is built on the foundation of hope. Hell would not be torment, if there were no Heaven to dream of. And every demon, from the least to the greatest, dreams of improving their lot in life (generally at the expense of others, yes, but...). <i>As a demon</i>, Choronzon <b>cannot</b> crush hope.<br /> <br /> \u200bAnd who better to drive that point home than the Endless embodiment of Dream?</div> </div> </div> </div>I was being ironic in a (possibly mis-pitched) genre savvy fashion.<br /> <br /> Ah, the many (little and totally inconsequential) internet deaths I die for self-aware humour.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8959-prototype00","name":"prototype00","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8959_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"964"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-14T21:24:45-07:00","id":1388555,"title":"","content":"Inspired by Tegama I've been considering how to build a Lunar Single-Point Stylist.<br /> <br /> First holy crap the damage potential. If you get Str 5 Dex 5 and decide to go for Deadly Beastman and activate Liquid Steel Flow your reaper daiklave is swinging for 27 dice twice per round.<br /> <br /> Second no mastery is not a complete disaster, what hurts is really the double 9s on Fatal Stroke Flash and the success on Liquid Steel Flow. If someone manages to crash your sword through your ridiculous lunar soak instead of crashing you then form has pretty much paid for itself already. Also not having Mastery means your second pool doesn't reset to base with Blinding Nova Flare, which is actually a bonus.<br /> <br /> Third think I overlooked Wasp Sting Blur as just the price to pay to get to Octopus-and-Spider when I read the KS document, I think I missed that it also works for withering attacks that crash your target and not just on decisives. A Single-Point Stylist could use it for a withering against an enemy at low initiative and then Shining Starfall Execution/Fatal Sword Flash on the follow-up attack for a full damage decisive that doesn't reset you to base. Just don't miss.<br /> <br /> Fourth Gathering Light Concentration is actually kind of decent for lunars if you're at low initiative where Bending Before the Storm can fail you.<br /> <br /> Fifth the Fatal Stroke Flash + Behemoth's Footprint Thread combo might be impractical nonsense when there's anyone around that you don't want to die, but when you absolutely need to blow up everyone right now it's glorious.<br /> <br /> Sixth once you get to Fivefold Transcendent Insight (with Red-Visions Realized the commitment pays for itself on your Join-Battle Roll), it gives you another 6 motes of discount on excellency + Unwaverign Predator + Wolfs Eye to enhance your Join Battle for the sword, with a stunt and an MA speciality in the sword you're wielding that averages to your sword starting at 13i with 1 mote spend to enhance the roll.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2579,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2579-limaxophobiac","user":"limaxophobiac","date":". 05-15-2020, 12:26 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2579-limaxophobiac","name":"limaxophobiac","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"294"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-19T14:16:12-07:00","id":1390059,"title":"","content":"Is this also the right place to discuss not completely optimized builds? Either flavorful builds, builds designed for some kind of fun factor, or builds operating under a weird restriction?<br /> <br /> For the third one, I was wondering what's the most viable starting build you could make for an ordinary campaign using only Charms from a single Attribute? After a quick look I selected Dexterity and came up with this - you end up being basically a ni