":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25834-habitableexoplanet","name":"habitableexoplanet","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"296"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-29T23:03:02-07:00","id":1392763,"title":"","content":"Hi there folks! Got a couple questions about death kitty. How does the shadow walking belt work with the cat spirit shape? I thought it was sent to elsewhere? And are you stunting to get more evasion using your charms and whatnot since the bonus from tiny creature counts as a bonus from charm dice according to page 132 of Fangs at the Gate. Thanks!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24445-arkayriel","name":"Arkayriel","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"122"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-29T23:26:19-07:00","id":1392766,"title":"","content":"Okay, so reading the book again I'm guessing the idea is that the belt is something you could use in cat form? I guess I can see that though isn't a cat wearing a belt a little odd? Is that really inconspicuous? Or would it draw unwanted attention from those you can't afford to?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24445-arkayriel","name":"Arkayriel","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"122"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-29T23:30:24-07:00","id":1392767,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Arkayriel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1293395-ex-3-lunars-glorious-argent-beastiary-a-lunar-s-character-thread?p=1392766#post1392766\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Okay, so reading the book again I'm guessing the idea is that the belt is something you could use in cat form? I guess I can see that though isn't a cat wearing a belt a little odd? Is that really inconspicuous? Or would it draw unwanted attention from those you can't afford to?</div> </div> </div> </div>I &quot;ruled of cool&quot; in my head to be a collar when a cat. But yes, a cat can wear a belt.<br /> <br /> And to be obvious you have to <b><i>see </i></b>the cat which is not particularly easy under any circumstances. (Cat could also have long hair I guess, which could hide the belt if it's a small silk number.)<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> And are you stunting to get more evasion using your charms and whatnot since the bonus from tiny creature counts as a bonus from charm dice according to page 132 of Fangs at the Gate. Thanks! </div> </div> </div>Its Charm dice, yes. Just think of it as getting 4 free charm dice for your character at all time for free, just like your accuracy bonus.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":8959,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8959-prototype00","user":"prototype00","date":". 05-30-2020, 02:44 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8959-prototype00","name":"prototype00","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8959_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"964"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-29T23:43:57-07:00","id":1392768,"title":"","content":"Ok yeah, I can see that, thanks. And the evasion? Are stunting to add the bonus from charms because you should be tapped out from the tiny creature bonus right? Ah I see you already answered that thanks again.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":24445,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24445-arkayriel","user":"Arkayriel","date":". 05-30-2020, 02:53 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24445-arkayriel","name":"Arkayriel","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"122"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-30T03:40:56-07:00","id":1392778,"title":"","content":"So just a rough calculation:<br /> <br /> Base Dodge: 5 (Dex) + 5 (Dodge) + 1 (Specialty) = 6 Dodge DV. Then you add on Tiny Creature bonus (which is considered 4 charm dice) = 8 Dodge DV. Then you can add on Agile Beast Defense if needed for 1 mote (Considered 2 charm dice) = 9 Dodge DV.<br /> <br /> Then finally you can stunt your defense to be an impossible to hit kitty for 10 Dodge DV (which is not considered charm dice). So in total you have for 1m expenditure a constant 9-10 Dodge DV (Considered to be 6 charm dice, which is still within the charm cap if I don't get my math wrong).<br /> <br /> prototype00","signature":"","edited":{"userid":8959,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8959-prototype00","user":"prototype00","date":". 05-30-2020, 08:12 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8959-prototype00","name":"prototype00","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8959_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"964"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-30T07:26:49-07:00","id":1392803,"title":"","content":"Well your cap from attribute is +2 when dex alone( 5 divided by 2 round down). So you have to stunt first then use agile beast defense, but sure same dif in the end. Except of course you're going from 8 to 10 without the possibilty of stopping at 9, but...who cares? No reason I know of to settle for less when it's as little effort as just putting forth some effort. Oh and while I'm at it, I believe you said don't worry about raising it unless they hit 9? Implying that your 8 evasion can't be hit with 8 successes( is that even how you spell that word? looks weird)? If so I believe that's wrong, that's why drifting leaf illusion exists in solar dodge after all.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":24445,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24445-arkayriel","user":"Arkayriel","date":". 05-30-2020, 10:41 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24445-arkayriel","name":"Arkayriel","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"122"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-30T07:40:42-07:00","id":1392804,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Arkayriel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1293395-ex-3-lunars-glorious-argent-beastiary-a-lunar-s-character-thread?p=1392803#post1392803\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well your cap from attribute is +2 when dex alone( 5 divided by 2 round down). So you have to stunt first then use agile beast defense, but sure same dif in the end. Except of course you're going from 8 to 10 without the possibilty of stopping at 9, but...who cares? No reason I know of to settle for less when it's as little effort as just putting forth some effort.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, just say that your keen eyesight sees the exact path of the blow or that your dizzying intellect is constantly calculating four moves ahead and no foe can keep up.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8959-prototype00","name":"prototype00","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8959_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"964"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-30T07:56:10-07:00","id":1392805,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Arkayriel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1293395-ex-3-lunars-glorious-argent-beastiary-a-lunar-s-character-thread?p=1392803#post1392803\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Oh and while I'm at it, I believe you said don't worry about raising it unless they hit 9? Implying that your 8 evasion can't be hit with 8 successes( is that even how you spell that word? looks weird)? If so I believe that's wrong, that's why drifting leaf illusion exists in solar dodge after all.</div> </div> </div> </div>Its actually base 9 EV if you stunt it. So I'm assuming Death Kitty runs around with 9 EV all the time, because its just a simple stunt to get that.<br /> <br /> So if they hit 9, just use Agile Beast after you see the result to boost it to 10 (you need either higher Initiative, or they need to roll a 1, but the thing is if they have enough dice to roll 9 successes, they probably rolled at least one 1 too, so why not) since you are a Tiny Creature and you get the Protean benefit.<br /> <br /> So one mote potentially for defense and then toss everything else from mote drip into to hit for a constant 9 EV (boostable to 10) and 25 accuracy for 5 mote expenditure per turn.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":8959,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8959-prototype00","user":"prototype00","date":". 05-30-2020, 11:03 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8959-prototype00","name":"prototype00","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8959_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"964"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-30T13:21:23-07:00","id":1392890,"title":"","content":"Oh yes, it's quite good. I always knew cats were evil in the bestest of ways.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24445-arkayriel","name":"Arkayriel","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"122"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-30T13:21:23-07:00","id":1392891,"title":"","content":"Oh yes, it's quite good. I always knew cats were evil in the bestest of ways.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24445-arkayriel","name":"Arkayriel","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"122"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-31T02:27:33-07:00","id":1393042,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Arkayriel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1293395-ex-3-lunars-glorious-argent-beastiary-a-lunar-s-character-thread?p=1392891#post1392891\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Oh yes, it's quite good. I always knew cats were evil in the bestest of ways.</div> </div> </div> </div>Cats in all RPGs = Unexpectedly Powerful and Deadly<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8959-prototype00","name":"prototype00","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8959_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"964"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-07T19:15:25-07:00","id":1394933,"title":"","content":"Hmm, since the book is out officially-ish and some charms got nerfed/buffed, I might make a second pass through some of my builds and think about what changes I would make. <br /> <br /> Hopefully it helps other players with their own inspirations and you wont run into as many unexpected walls.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8959-prototype00","name":"prototype00","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8959_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"964"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-25T02:20:29-07:00","id":1398742,"title":"","content":"As an example of how a build can develop over the course of a game here's my approx 150xp Full Moon from Wizard of Oz's 3rd ed Lunar game. Focuses primarily on strength-based fighting with a huge soak as backup and a final trump card of Mountainous Spirit expression if needed (yes I know as written its not that great, I just like the idea of a 20 ft tall angry walrus man smashing things).<br /> <br /> He's an icewalker from the coastal regions north of the Haslanti League who was exalted while trying to prevent the destruction of his village at the hands of dragon blooded led mercenaries. Defeated and left for dead, he was rescued by a group of silver pact lunars, tattooed, and spent ten years searching for the ones who wrecked his home before being sent to join the rest of the party at the court of a northern king. His moonsilver and ivory Grimcleaver incorporates the shattered pieces of his broken tusk into its blade, although it has yet to awaken any evocations due to only being forged a few years ago.<br /> <br /> <br /> Name \u2013 Olaf Keelbreaker, The Steel Iceberg<br /> Caste \u2013 Full Moon<br /> Spirit Shape \u2013 Walrus<br /> Tell \u2013 Broken tusk/teeth and large scar on left side of the mouth<br /> Limit Trigger - <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman, Times New Roman, serif\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">The Lunar destroys, abandons, or sacrifices something precious or valuable to her</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <u>Attributes</u> <br /> STR (C) \u2013 5<br /> DEX \u2013 2 <br /> STA (C) \u2013 5<br /> CHA (F) - 4<br /> MAN - 3<br /> APP - 1<br /> PER - 3<br /> INT - 2<br /> WITS (F) \u2013 5<br /> <br /> <br /> <u>Abilities</u> <br /> Athletics \u2013 4 (Swimming)<br /> Awareness \u2013 4<br /> Brawl - 4<br /> Melee \u2013 5 (Axes)<br /> Craft \u2013 Shipbuilding \u2013 1 (Northern longboats)<br /> Ivory Carving - 2<br /> Integrity - 2<br /> Resistance - 4<br /> Presence - 2<br /> Socialise - 2<br /> Sail \u2013 3 (Northern Longboats)<br /> Stealth \u2013 2<br /> Thrown \u2013 2<br /> Survival \u2013 4 (Tundra)<br /> <br /> <u>Merits</u> <br /> Language \u2013 2 (Sky Tounge, Riverspeak, 4 local tongues)<br /> Artifact \u2013 3 (Grand Grimcleaver)<br /> Hearts Blood \u2013 1 (Raven, Arctic Wolf, Arctic Fox, Pine Marten, Snowy Owl, Wandering Tern)<br /> Resources \u2013 1 (Silver armlets and torcs, silver coins)<br /> Quick Reflexes (3) [+ 1 to join battle]<br /> <br /> <u>Charms</u> <u>Universal</u><br /> Hybrid Body Transformation (Walrus Head and hide \u2013 Huge, Deadly Weapons (Tusk, + Piercing), Fangs (Tusk)<br /> Deadly Beastman Transformation<ul><li>+ 5 dice on Withering damage, feats of strength and movement actions</li> <li>+ 5 nat soak</li> <li>may attempt up to str 10 feats of strength</li> <li>-1 Def</li> <li>lose benefits of resonance</li> </ul><br /> <br /> <br /> <u>Charisma</u><br /> Argent Songbird Voice<br /> <br /> <u>Dexterity</u><br /> Finding The Needles Eye<br /> Sinuous Striking Grace<br /> <br /> <u>Perception</u><br /> Perceiving the Hidden World<br /> Spirit Rending Fury<br /> <br /> <u>Stamina</u><br /> Steel Paw Style<br /> Ox-body Technique x 2 (4 -2s, 4 -4s]<br /> Impenetrable Beast Armour<br /> Durant Quicksilver Adaption<br /> Bear Sleep Technique<br /> Halting The Scarlet Flow<br /> Invulnerable Moonsilver Carapace <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman, Times New Roman, serif\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><i>(+11 soak, 10 Hardness, \u22122 mobility). Its soak can\u2019t be reduced below (Stamina) by effects that ignore armored soak, like Piercing attacks.</i></span></span></span><br /> <br /> <u>Strength</u><br /> Deadly Claw Blow<br /> Ferocious Biting Tooth<br /> Divine Predator Strike<br /> Ox-Dragon Smash<br /> Angry Rhino Charge<br /> Unstoppable Beast Force Blow<br /> Mighty Ram Smash<br /> World Shaking Slam<br /> Towering Beast Form<br /> Mountainous Spirit Expression<br /> Terrifying Ogre Alteration \u2013 level 4 tough hide (+4 nat soak in DBT)<br /> <br /> <u>Wits</u><br /> Squirrels Cunning Technique<br /> Many Pockets Meditation<br /> <br /> <br /> Essence \u2013 2 Personal - 17 Periphiral - 42<br /> Resolve - 4<br /> Guile - 2<br /> Parry \u2013 5 (6 with Axes)<br /> Evasion - 1<br /> <br /> Health levels<br /> 0 \u2013 1 -<br /> -1 \u2013 2 -<br /> -2 \u2013 6 -<br /> -4 \u2013 5 -<br /> Incap<br /> <br /> <u>Gear</u> Vengeance Fang - Moonsilver Grand Grimcleaver (Acc +1, DAM +14, Def 0, Overwhelm 5, Attune 5)<br /> Tags \u2013 Lethal, Melee, Chopping, Reaching, Two Handed<br /> 2 x Hatchet<br /> Melee - (Acc +2, DAM 9, Def +1, Overwhelm 1)<br /> Thrown \u2013 (Acc +4/+3, DAM 9, Overwhelm 1)<br /> Buff jacket<br /> Sealskin clothing<br /> <br /> Permanent Crippling Injury - Blinded Left Eye<br /> <br /> <br /> I would be interested to see how people think he compares to some of the other builds in the thread since I wasnt really focused on optimising him at all, I just had some ideas I wanted to try out and certain charms I wanted to take.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26249-keelbreaker","name":"Keelbreaker","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26249_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-26T09:38:30-07:00","id":1399087,"title":"","content":"Hmm, in terms of power/coolness, I rank my builds in the following order (I know, I know they're all my babies, but you gotta be brutally honest with yourself when the time comes), ascending.<br /> <br /> 4. Gintora Na'Yas Tiger Tiger Stylist<br /> 3. Aguile Ophidian, Gravity Destroyer<br /> 2. The Knight of Bone and Ivory<br /> 1. Death Kitty<br /> <br /> Not any slight on the way your character developed, I'd probably put him somewhere in the middle there in terms of his raw power. (Which is pretty good, considering these are probably some of the best builds I have come up with for Lunars so far).<br /> <br /> prototype00<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8959-prototype00","name":"prototype00","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8959_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"964"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-28T10:55:43-07:00","id":1399621,"title":"","content":"So what sort of things would you change/modify if you were going for a similar concept?<br /> <br /> Because I would be interested to see what someone elses take on the same idea would be.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26249-keelbreaker","name":"Keelbreaker","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26249_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-28T19:40:01-07:00","id":1399719,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Keelbreaker</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1293395-ex-3-lunars-glorious-argent-beastiary-a-lunar-s-character-thread?p=1399621#post1399621\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So what sort of things would you change/modify if you were going for a similar concept?<br /> <br /> Because I would be interested to see what someone elses take on the same idea would be.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'd consider looking for ways to get light/medium artifact weapon stats that work with steel paw style or deadly claw blow. It's not a huge thing, but I'd worry that the current build has exceptional withering damage (I think 24 base), but merely good withering accuracy (looks like 12 base). It may be that natural weapons+brawl is helping there, but it doesn't look like you have access to artifact quality natural weapons, and don't have maxed-out brawl like you do melee. OTOH, your stats are good enough that your accuracy isn't bad, and sacrificing damage would be a drawback.<br /> <br /> The splitting of combat style (having dots in melee, brawl and thrown, having an artifact weapon and a hybrid body transformation that grants natural weapons) is spend resources on a fair amount of stuff that doesn't aid your primary combat style. OTOH, it does help you if you end up in a situation where melee isn't ideal. I think lunars don't have any great charms for dealing with being disarmed or at a range as a Melee user, so grabbing a few dots is possibly an efficient way to deal with that.<br /> <br /> This thread, and my thoughts, have focused more on optimizing shapeshifting than charms, and I think Lunar charms have less overpowering effects than solars and less useless-seeming effects than Dragonblooded, but it looks like you have most of my favorite strength and stamina combat charms. Little in the way of social and utility charms, but a few.<br /> <br /> In general &quot;Deadly Beastman Transformation, Strength 5, Stamina 5, either Dex 5 or the dex replacement charms, artifact weapon and armor or charms that grant these, attack ability 5+specialty, defense ability 5+ specialty&quot; is a very strong starting point for basically any charms to be added to. I'm always tempted to use a martial art on these characters, since it isn't competing with native melee charms or animal form, but there aren't any martial arts that seem like a great fit for the character.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23597-autxauty","name":"autXautY","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"286"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-28T21:42:13-07:00","id":1399730,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>autXautY</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1293395-ex-3-lunars-glorious-argent-beastiary-a-lunar-s-character-thread?p=1399719#post1399719\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The splitting of combat style (having dots in melee, brawl and thrown, having an artifact weapon and a hybrid body transformation that grants natural weapons) is spend resources on a fair amount of stuff that doesn't aid your primary combat style. OTOH, it does help you if you end up in a situation where melee isn't ideal. I think lunars don't have any great charms for dealing with being disarmed or at a range as a Melee user, so grabbing a few dots is possibly an efficient way to deal with that.</div> </div> </div> </div>He had thrown from the start just because it fits his background as an icewalker, but having the ranged option is nice too even though he probably won't hit with it due to god awful dice pools. As for the Brawl that's pretty much exactly why I took it, he didn't originally have it but got grappled into submission by one of the other PCs and thought &quot;hmmm, maybe I should actually learn how to fight without my axe just in case&quot;<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>autXautY</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1293395-ex-3-lunars-glorious-argent-beastiary-a-lunar-s-character-thread?p=1399719#post1399719\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In general &quot;Deadly Beastman Transformation, Strength 5, Stamina 5, either Dex 5 or the dex replacement charms, artifact weapon and armor or charms that grant these, attack ability 5+specialty, defense ability 5+ specialty&quot; is a very strong starting point for basically any charms to be added to. I'm always tempted to use a martial art on these characters since it isn't competing with native melee charms or animal form, but there aren't any martial arts that seem like a great fit for the character.</div> </div> </div> </div>I can't find anything even remotely appropriate aside from maybe White Reaper, and that wouldn't work with his Grimcleaver. Given its made in part of his own flesh and blood and he has a specific intimacy towards using it I doubt he would ever give it up just to learn a new fighting style. Although one amusing thing I was considering is to buy Beast-Form Empowerment and add that new 'wield two-handed weapons one-handed' merit as part of the additional mutation package because again giant walrus men waving multiple oversized weapons around is very funny to me.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26249-keelbreaker","name":"Keelbreaker","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26249_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-29T07:21:49-07:00","id":1399815,"title":"","content":"As Olaf stands now with Manipulation 3 Socialize 2 you should have Guile 3 reather than 2.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Keelbreaker</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1293395-ex-3-lunars-glorious-argent-beastiary-a-lunar-s-character-thread?p=1399621#post1399621\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So what sort of things would you change/modify if you were going for a similar concept?<br /> <br /> Because I would be interested to see what someone elses take on the same idea would be.</div> </div> </div> </div>Since he already has Cha 4 changing him to Cha 5 Man 2 Per(F) 5 Wits 3 and grabbing Arrogant Lion Bearing (use Cha for resolve) and Unwavering Predators Eye (Per for join-battle) could be a thing if you're not super interested in any more Cache charms than you already have, (walruses migrate <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Walrus#Migration\" target=\"_blank\">https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Walrus#Migration</a> so you can grab the navigation charms as Per with totemic).<br /> <br /> You could drop thrown or stealth from 2 to 1 to increase socialize to 3 to keep Guile at 3.<br /> <br /> Beast-Form Empowerement or Chimera-Soul Expression are strictly superior to Terrifying Ogre Alteration (6 dots of mutations vs 4, whenever you are in Hybrid Body vs only when you are also in DBT). and would let you get Unusual Hide 5 and Carapace if you droped the piercing of the tusks.<br /> <br /> With how many -2 and -4 HLs you have Relentless Lunar Fury would also be nice to have to still be a functional combatant at lower HLs, if you later adder Pain Tolerance with lunar xp you'd never take more than a -1 wound penalty.<br /> <br /> That's 3 new charms so I'd drop all of Impenetrable Beast Armour, Durant Quicksilver Adaption, and Invulnerable Moonsilver Carapace, because they are not really very good charms. If you wanted to go Deadly Beastman + Mountainous Spirit + Invulnerable Moonsilver Carapace you'd be down 30 motes and 3wp before the fight even starts.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2579,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2579-limaxophobiac","user":"limaxophobiac","date":". 06-29-2020, 03:48 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2579-limaxophobiac","name":"limaxophobiac","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"294"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-06T22:18:18-07:00","id":1401432,"title":"","content":"With their anima having been clarified to apply to normal attack rolls, No-Moon shapeshifting sorcerers are no joke in a fight.<br /> <br /> I was making a character and with a fairly low investment in actual combat charms and abilities you're a serious combatant.<br /> <br /> With a core of:<br /> _______<br /> <br /> Dex 5<br /> <br /> Athletics 3 (Specialty: Animal Forms)<br /> Brawl 5 (Specialty: Natural Weapons),<br /> Hearts Blood 1<br /> Medium Natural Weapon (Tell) 4<br /> <br /> and<br /> <br /> Quicksilver Second Face<br /> Finding the Needle's Eye<br /> Ox-Body Technique<br /> <br /> any 4 mental charms (you're a no-moon you were 100% getting this anyway)<br /> Terrestrial Circle Sorcery (ISoB control)<br /> _______<br /> <br /> You get parry 7, with -2 to enemy attack rolls at iconic (RAW only solar/DB archers and lunars can get around this penalty, plus potential enemies that dont rely on sight)<br /> <br /> Turning into a Hippo with ISoB you have:<br /> <br /> Combat Movement: 12 dice (from +3 Hippo speed bonus)<br /> <br /> Soak/Hardness: 19/6 + essence<br /> <br /> Hippo Bite 12 dice (19 Damage, Min 5, ignore 4 + extra success soak, inflict [extra success] crippling penalty with decisive attacks)<br /> _______<br /> <br /> All this for 4 commited motes, reflexive or day-long effects, which is amazingly mote and action efficient compared to what you have to commit to artifact weapons and spend to activate MA forms which require far more chargen/xp investment to access<br /> <br /> With combat competency so easily taken care of you can dive into all the mysticism, knowledge, scrutiny charms and non-combat spells you want while still kicking butt in a fight.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2579,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2579-limaxophobiac","user":"limaxophobiac","date":". 08-06-2020, 05:57 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2579-limaxophobiac","name":"limaxophobiac","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"294"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-07T00:09:07-07:00","id":1401440,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>limaxophobiac</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1293395-ex-3-lunars-glorious-argent-beastiary-a-lunar-s-character-thread?p=1401432#post1401432\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">With their anima having been clarified to apply to normal attack rolls, No-Moon shapeshifting sorcerers are no joke in a fight.<br /> <br /> I was making a character and with a fairly low investment in actual combat charms and abilities you're a serious combatant.<br /> <br /> With a core of:<br /> _______<br /> <br /> Dex 5<br /> <br /> Athletics 3 (Specialty: Animal Forms)<br /> Brawl 5 (Specialty: Natural Weapons),<br /> Hearts Blood 1<br /> Medium Natural Weapon (Tell) 4<br /> <br /> and<br /> <br /> Quicksilver Second Face<br /> Finding the Needle's Eye<br /> Ox-Body Technique<br /> <br /> any 4 mental charms (you're a no-moon you were 100% getting this anyway)<br /> Terrestrial Circle Sorcery (ISoB control)<br /> _______<br /> <br /> You get parry 7, with -2 to enemy attack rolls at iconic (RAW only solar archers and lunars can get around this penalty, plus potential enemies that dont rely on sight)<br /> <br /> Turning into a Hippo with ISoB you have:<br /> <br /> Combat Movement: 12 dice (from +3 Hippo speed bonus)<br /> <br /> Soak/Hardness: 19/6 + essence<br /> <br /> Hippo Bite 12 dice (19 Damage, Min 5, ignore 4 + extra success soak, inflict [extra success] crippling penalty with decisive attacks)<br /> _______<br /> <br /> All this for 4 commited motes, reflexive or day-long effects, which is amazingly mote and action efficient compared to what you have to commit to artifact weapons and spend to activate MA forms which require far more chargen/xp investment to access<br /> <br /> With combat competency so easily taken care of you can dive into all the mysticism, knowledge, scrutiny charms and non-combat spells you want while still kicking butt in a fight.</div> </div> </div> </div>A perfect illustration of the minimum required for what I am terming &quot;Lunar Battlesuit&quot;, lol. I should probably just make a post: &quot;Want your Lunar to hang with Combat Specialists in combat, no matter what their primary focus is? This is the minimum requirement.&quot;<br /> <br /> And then keep it to about 1/3-1/4 of chargen resources.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8959-prototype00","name":"prototype00","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8959_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"964"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-10T06:21:10-07:00","id":1402056,"title":"","content":"So I assume you're getting the medium natural weapon as a tell, so you'll have +1 parry in hippo form (or rather, any form), right?<br /> <br /> Like, I'm reading this thread as an interested party, but I tend to play with STs that react a bit allergic to obvious cheese, like super-powerful mutations tied to your tell that don't &quot;fit&quot; the character and are there for mechanical purposes only, pretty much. So I tend to try and imagine how such builds work without.<br /> <br /> \u200bSame with <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8959-prototype00\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar8959_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"8959\" data-vbnamecard=\"8959\">prototype00</a> 's Death Kitty, which had Wood Dragon's Claw, which I assume is so you have access to your brawl pool + the accuracy from light artifact, right?<br /> I like to be inspired, but I also need to tone your builds down, they're too optimized and will get me slapped by my ST <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/903-cheshire-cat","name":"Cheshire Cat","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar903_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"502"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-10T07:37:59-07:00","id":1402065,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cheshire Cat</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1293395-ex-3-lunars-glorious-argent-beastiary-a-lunar-s-character-thread?p=1402056#post1402056\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So I assume you're getting the medium natural weapon as a tell, so you'll have +1 parry in hippo form (or rather, any form), right?</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah. F.ex. some big horns or antlers from your spirit-shape no matter what form you take.<br /> <br /> In a game where other people aren't optimising it should perfectly fine without the +1 parry and you free up 4 extra merit-dots and you can use shapeshifting for disguises a lot easier.<br /> <br /> Animal forms and sorcery are both low barrier of entry high pay-off abilities that work great together and shape-shifting sorceror is a solid thematic archetype. Even without hippos and the ISoB control bonus both being on the overtuned end it would still be a strong flexible combo..","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2579,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2579-limaxophobiac","user":"limaxophobiac","date":". 07-10-2020, 11:13 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2579-limaxophobiac","name":"limaxophobiac","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"294"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-10T08:13:20-07:00","id":1402070,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cheshire Cat</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1293395-ex-3-lunars-glorious-argent-beastiary-a-lunar-s-character-thread?p=1402056#post1402056\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So I assume you're getting the medium natural weapon as a tell, so you'll have +1 parry in hippo form (or rather, any form), right?<br /> <br /> Like, I'm reading this thread as an interested party, but I tend to play with STs that react a bit allergic to obvious cheese, like super-powerful mutations tied to your tell that don't &quot;fit&quot; the character and are there for mechanical purposes only, pretty much. So I tend to try and imagine how such builds work without.<br /> <br /> \u200bSame with <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8959-prototype00\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar8959_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"8959\" data-vbnamecard=\"8959\">prototype00</a> 's Death Kitty, which had Wood Dragon's Claw, which I assume is so you have access to your brawl pool + the accuracy from light artifact, right?<br /> I like to be inspired, but I also need to tone your builds down, they're too optimized and will get me slapped by my ST <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>Wood Dragon's Claw is for the Accuracy and a lesser extent the damage, yes. Without it, Death Kitty is kind of meh, so I wouldn't recommend it for STs who might be averse.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8959-prototype00","name":"prototype00","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8959_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"964"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-10T09:20:37-07:00","id":1402077,"title":"","content":"Stalking Shadow Hunter + Last Warrior's Unity (+ Underfoot Menace) can also give you cats with dex+brawl+accuracy to hit, and look much more like an intended reading of the rules to me - Last Warrior's Unity seems unambiguously intended to allow animal forms to make use of dex+brawl+accuracy to hit.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23597-autxauty","name":"autXautY","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"286"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-10T09:22:02-07:00","id":1402078,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>autXautY</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1293395-ex-3-lunars-glorious-argent-beastiary-a-lunar-s-character-thread?p=1402077#post1402077\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Stalking Shadow Hunter + Last Warrior's Unity (+ Underfoot Menace) can also give you cats with dex+brawl+accuracy to hit, and look much more like an intended reading of the rules to me - Last Warrior's Unity seems unambiguously intended to allow animal forms to make use of dex+brawl+accuracy to hit.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, but the damage nerf to Last Warrior's Unity is extremely gnarly in cat form. I also couldn't in good conscience recommend that either.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8959-prototype00","name":"prototype00","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8959_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"964"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-10T09:36:53-07:00","id":1402083,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>prototype00</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1293395-ex-3-lunars-glorious-argent-beastiary-a-lunar-s-character-thread?p=1402078#post1402078\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Yeah, but the damage nerf to Last Warrior's Unity is extremely gnarly in cat form. I also couldn't in good conscience recommend that either.</div> </div> </div> </div>I was thinking that stalking shadow hunter + underfoot menace deals with that. SSH doesn't specify it must be a cat's natural weapon. It describes the effect as &quot;<span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">it uses the higher of the two damage ratings for its attacks.&quot;, which is different from how LWU describes the damage reduction, but it feels like a really forced interpretation that &quot;you deal 15 damage against tiny creatures, and 10 against smaller&quot; isn't two different damage ratings for this attack,</span></span>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23597-autxauty","name":"autXautY","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"286"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-10T13:57:19-07:00","id":1402113,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Keelbreaker</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1293395-ex-3-lunars-glorious-argent-beastiary-a-lunar-s-character-thread?p=1398742#post1398742\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Awareness \u2013 4<br /> <br /> Quick Reflexes (3) [+ 1 to join battle]<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>The Quick Reflexes merit is a gotcha I don't agree with, it is an objectively poor choice that actively tries to mislead the players. <br /> <br /> You know you can take awareness 5 for 2 bonus points, and have +1 to Join Battle and also every awareness roll, for one less bp than the merit? Or you can have the 'initiative' specialty for one bp, that does the same thing but for 2 bps less?<br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1524-pcontop","name":"pcontop","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1524_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"278"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-10T15:31:29-07:00","id":1402130,"title":"","content":"Merits like that are because you've got spare merit dots and don't know what to spend them on.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-10T16:18:04-07:00","id":1402137,"title":"","content":"So Last Warrior's Unity + Moonsilver Smashfist or Tiger Claws or whatever?<br /> <br /> Edit: I mean sure, Stalking Shadow Hunter using normal reasoning seems to tell you to use the damage values for same-size enemies, but actually RAW it just says &quot;use the higher of the two ratings&quot;, apparently referring to the cat's natural attacks, which your LWU-empowered artifact wouldn't be. So again you're a bit at the mercy of your ST.<br /> But even aside, I wouldn't really want to drop a willpower just to cheese my attack roll, and you can't use your hands if you keep if committed indefinitely, so... Meh?<br /> At the whole I kind of dislike the aesthetic of upgrading your kitty form with sorcerous or artifact claws, because then you're not really a cat anymore... But that's just personal taste.<br /> Even if you don't though, you can do brawl 5, dex 5, specialty, so you get a pool of 11, which is higher than the cat's, so withering 11+1, at least you get the 12, and Ambush Hunter tunes that up to a 15, which is almost as good as the 16 which is the maximum you could've had as a human with a light artifact weapon.<br /> <br /> (Though I get the appeal of cheesing your way to 11 pool + 5 accuracy + 3 Ambush Hunter for a total whopping 19 without having spent a single mote, it is VERY appealing)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":903,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/903-cheshire-cat","user":"Cheshire Cat","date":". 07-10-2020, 07:25 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/903-cheshire-cat","name":"Cheshire Cat","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar903_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"502"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-10T16:26:06-07:00","id":1402139,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1293395-ex-3-lunars-glorious-argent-beastiary-a-lunar-s-character-thread?p=1402130#post1402130\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Merits like that are because you've got spare merit dots and don't know what to spend them on.</div> </div> </div> </div>Also, as a cap breaker, right?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/903-cheshire-cat","name":"Cheshire Cat","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar903_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"502"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-10T18:34:51-07:00","id":1402158,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cheshire Cat</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1293395-ex-3-lunars-glorious-argent-beastiary-a-lunar-s-character-thread?p=1402137#post1402137\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So Last Warrior's Unity + Moonsilver Smashfist or Tiger Claws or whatever?<br /> <br /> Edit: I mean sure, Stalking Shadow Hunter using normal reasoning seems to tell you to use the damage values for same-size enemies, but actually RAW it just says &quot;use the higher of the two ratings&quot;, apparently referring to the cat's natural attacks, which your LWU-empowered artifact wouldn't be. So again you're a bit at the mercy of your ST.<br /> But even aside, I wouldn't really want to drop a willpower just to cheese my attack roll, and you can't use your hands if you keep if committed indefinitely, so... Meh?<br /> At the whole I kind of dislike the aesthetic of upgrading your kitty form with sorcerous or artifact claws, because then you're not really a cat anymore... But that's just personal taste.<br /> Even if you don't though, you can do brawl 5, dex 5, specialty, so you get a pool of 11, which is higher than the cat's, so withering 11+1, at least you get the 12, and Ambush Hunter tunes that up to a 15, which is almost as good as the 16 which is the maximum you could've had as a human with a light artifact weapon.<br /> <br /> (Though I get the appeal of cheesing your way to 11 pool + 5 accuracy + 3 Ambush Hunter for a total whopping 19 without having spent a single mote, it is VERY appealing)</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, I agree that the reading of the Stalking Shadow Hunter merit that way is a bit prone to fall afoul of any ST who has actually read the rules. Personally I prefer to depend on the established-to-work via word of Vance method of Wood Dragon's Claw, which gives you full accuracy and damage, guaranteed (heck you could be practically impossible to hit if you went with a No Moon Death kitty with that penalty to visual attack rolls they can get).<br /> <br /> As to the aesthetic aversion thing, that is something I unfortunately can't help with.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8959-prototype00","name":"prototype00","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8959_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"964"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-10T18:41:41-07:00","id":1402162,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>prototype00</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1293395-ex-3-lunars-glorious-argent-beastiary-a-lunar-s-character-thread?p=1402158#post1402158\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As to the aesthetic aversion thing, that is something I unfortunately can't help with.</div> </div> </div> </div>You could always go for an even more sorcerer death kitty route, who launches Deaths of Obsidian Butterflies from medium range, forcing his enemies to spend a turn aiming for every attack they make, on top of the -2 penalty and +2 defense, with essence+3 free dice to the attack from Ambush Predator+control bonus. That doesn't rely on any transformations.<br /> <br /> Unless you go for the flying death kitty, so you can avoid melee combatants.<br /> <br /> With Perfected Hybrid Interaction, or a combination of 2 cat forms, one of whom is mutated (possibly because it's a chimera), at least you can turn the wings on and off.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23597-autxauty","name":"autXautY","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"286"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-11T02:25:56-07:00","id":1402204,"title":"","content":"Can you actually just shape sorcery in animal form? You can, right?<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8959-prototype00\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar8959_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"8959\" data-vbnamecard=\"8959\">prototype00</a> ah right, I half-remember Vance saying that. So at least there's a Dev ruling on it.<br /> <br /> ty guys for your replies, I'm thinking out loud mostly on how you can make builds work in a more straight-forward way <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/903-cheshire-cat","name":"Cheshire Cat","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar903_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"502"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-01-16T21:37:11-08:00","id":1432463,"title":"","content":"I was looking throught the books for MA that can be competitive with animal forms and I think I found something (other than Single-Point being Single-Point).<br /> <br /> So Full Defense as an action has this funny thing where even though a lot of abilties and shield-tag weapons interact with it, it's not an action taken with any particular ability or a particular weapon, so when anything lets you take a full defense action that full defense action applies to defenses with all your abilities no matter the source effect that let you take a full defense. Which is what lets the lunar Crane sorceror flurry full defense with shape sorcery and get counterattacks despite the shield-tag weapon from natural shield mutation not being a crane-compatible weapon.<br /> <br /> So when Flowing Water Defense (from Water Dragon) lets you flurry an attack with full defense while ignoring the defense penalty, and you're a lunar who can sprout Extra Limbs for only a -1 penalty on your flurried attacks, and get Natural Armor to have decent soak despite being unarmored for Crane Style, you can make regular attacks on your turn in crane-form and keep your counterattacks.<br /> <br /> As a lunar you also have acces to Many-Armed Warriors Panopoly which lets you attune Razor Claws + Hooked Daiklave at reasonable cost (7m).<br /> <br /> So if you set it all up you're running around with 4 arms, one pair with Razor Claws and the other pair with your Hooked Daiklave, Crane Form active and using Flowing Water Defense + Golden Tiger Stance every turn, you're sitting at parry 12 (7 base, 1 crane, 2 full defense, 1 GTS, 1 stunt) with no onslaught from successfull parries, and -2 to attacks against you if you're no-moon, while making attacks as normal + counter attacking every attack against you for 7m 2i per round.<br /> <br /> All in all this is pretty mote-hungry, but it should also be inititive-positive with all the withering attacks you get to make which means you can throw in Theft-of-Essense Method whenever you crash someone with your Razor Claws to get some motes back.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2579,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2579-limaxophobiac","user":"limaxophobiac","date":". 01-17-2021, 12:45 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2579-limaxophobiac","name":"limaxophobiac","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"294"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-01-17T22:53:58-08:00","id":1432581,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>limaxophobiac</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1293395-ex-3-lunars-glorious-argent-beastiary-a-lunar-s-character-thread?p=1432463#post1432463\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I was looking throught the books for MA that can be competitive with animal forms and I think I found something (other than Single-Point being Single-Point).<br /> <br /> So Full Defense as an action has this funny thing where even though a lot of abilties and shield-tag weapons interact with it, it's not an action taken with any particular ability or a particular weapon, so when anything lets you take a full defense action that full defense action applies to defenses with all your abilities no matter the source effect that let you take a full defense. Which is what lets the lunar Crane sorceror flurry full defense with shape sorcery and get counterattacks despite the shield-tag weapon from natural shield mutation not being a crane-compatible weapon.<br /> <br /> So when Flowing Water Defense (from Water Dragon) lets you flurry an attack with full defense while ignoring the defense penalty, and you're a lunar who can sprout Extra Limbs for only a -1 penalty on your flurried attacks, and get Natural Armor to have decent soak despite being unarmored for Crane Style, you can make regular attacks on your turn in crane-form and keep your counterattacks.<br /> <br /> As a lunar you also have acces to Many-Armed Warriors Panopoly which lets you attune Razor Claws + Hooked Daiklave at reasonable cost (7m).<br /> <br /> So if you set it all up you're running around with 4 arms, one pair with Razor Claws and the other pair with your Hooked Daiklave, Crane Form active and using Flowing Water Defense + Golden Tiger Stance every turn, you're sitting at parry 12 (7 base, 1 crane, 2 full defense, 1 GTS, 1 stunt) with no onslaught from successfull parries, and -2 to attacks against you if you're no-moon, while making attacks as normal + counter attacking every attack against you for 7m 2i per round.<br /> <br /> All in all this is pretty mote-hungry, but it should also be inititive-positive with all the withering attacks you get to make which means you can throw in Theft-of-Essense Method whenever you crash someone with your Razor Claws to get some motes back.</div> </div> </div> </div>Hmm, I wonder what Spirit Shape you\u2019d want for this? Some kind of insect, maybe?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8959-prototype00","name":"prototype00","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8959_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"964"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-01-17T23:00:25-08:00","id":1432582,"title":"","content":"I'm trying really hard to avoid building a naval destroyer Lunar (Armoured Kraken totem). Not because it is unviable, but because I want to save it until I see the ship combat rules in play first.<br /> <br /> Anyone else have similar ideas?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Thoughts ripple out, birthing others","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1624-falleneco","name":"FallenEco","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1624_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1927"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-01-18T11:02:16-08:00","id":1432615,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>pcontop</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1293395-ex-3-lunars-glorious-argent-beastiary-a-lunar-s-character-thread?p=1402113#post1402113\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The Quick Reflexes merit is a gotcha I don't agree with, it is an objectively poor choice that actively tries to mislead the players. <br /> <br /> You know you can take awareness 5 for 2 bonus points, and have +1 to Join Battle and also every awareness roll, for one less bp than the merit? Or you can have the 'initiative' specialty for one bp, that does the same thing but for 2 bps less?<br /> <br /></div> </div> </div> </div>As I recall, Quick Reflexes is specifically costed the way it is to be the 12th die of Join Battle. That is, it was expected that you would have Wits 5, Awareness 5, and a Join Battle specialty before Quick Reflexes was worth it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1424-ghanjrho","name":"GhanjRho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1424_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"126"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-01-18T13:47:43-08:00","id":1432626,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>FallenEco</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1293395-ex-3-lunars-glorious-argent-beastiary-a-lunar-s-character-thread?p=1432582#post1432582\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm trying really hard to avoid building a naval destroyer Lunar (Armoured Kraken totem). Not because it is unviable, but because I want to save it until I see the ship combat rules in play first.<br /> <br /> Anyone else have similar ideas?</div> </div> </div> </div>I have (the idea was a pirate-queen who keeps hoards from ships she sinks at the bottom of the ocean), but the naval combat rules being what they are (in short; the number of successes on the maneuver roll is the only thing that really matters, and lunars have no charms to cap-break sailing charms) keeps the idea from being all that attractive to invest in.<br /> <br /> It's good flavour thought and you'll still beat all mortal and most DB captains with just Wits 5 Sail 3, so as long as you don't over-invest in it it's a nice trick to have in your kit.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2579-limaxophobiac","name":"limaxophobiac","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"294"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-01-21T08:15:59-08:00","id":1432914,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>GhanjRho</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1293395-ex-3-lunars-glorious-argent-beastiary-a-lunar-s-character-thread?p=1432615#post1432615\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> As I recall, Quick Reflexes is specifically costed the way it is to be the 12th die of Join Battle. That is, it was expected that you would have Wits 5, Awareness 5, and a Join Battle specialty before Quick Reflexes was worth it.</div> </div> </div> </div>And yet, so many NPCs made by this same company, and that have nowhere near 'peak-initiative', have this abomination of a merit. And note, the merit does not have those requirements you mentioned, because nobody would buy it (which would, ironically, be a good thing). This is a very bad design, and it shows, because it is a trap that is so easy to fall.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1524-pcontop","name":"pcontop","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1524_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"278"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-01-21T18:42:22-08:00","id":1432991,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>pcontop</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1293395-ex-3-lunars-glorious-argent-beastiary-a-lunar-s-character-thread?p=1432914#post1432914\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And yet, so many NPCs made by this same company, and that have nowhere near 'peak-initiative', have this abomination of a merit.</div> </div> </div> </div>NPCs don't have to follow character creation rules.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-01-22T05:55:26-08:00","id":1433043,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1293395-ex-3-lunars-glorious-argent-beastiary-a-lunar-s-character-thread?p=1432991#post1432991\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">NPCs don't have to follow character creation rules.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> That's not the point I was making - this merits misleads players and even professionals to believe they are getting anything meaningful buying it. It is a trap.<br /> <br /> Imagine I made a three-dot merit called 'weapon mastery', but that gave one dice to attacks in just one type of weapon. It has a cool name, a player who wants to be a good swordsman would take it - but it is a sham.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1524-pcontop","name":"pcontop","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1524_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"278"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-01-22T09:25:53-08:00","id":1433059,"title":"","content":"On the contrary that weapon master merit would be overpowered. Any non-charm bonus you can stack on top of what would otherwise be your cap is worth its weight in gold if you're already at the intended cap. There's a 2-dot hearthstone (Jewel of Swift-Strike) which only gives a rather situational +1 non-charm to attacks and it's easily one of the best 2-dot hearthstones.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2579-limaxophobiac","name":"limaxophobiac","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"294"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-01-22T14:34:39-08:00","id":1433101,"title":"","content":"I also spotted a fun little thing I hadn't thought about before; since Fivefold Transcendent Insight applies to all perception charms, it reduces Demon-Drinking Fang to 1m for +5 Aggravated Decisive damage against spirits and Fey (if you have Per 5). Combine with Octopus-and-Spider Barrage for a real God-blender (at E3 thats +20 aggravated decisive damage for 4m).<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>prototype00</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1293395-ex-3-lunars-glorious-argent-beastiary-a-lunar-s-character-thread?p=1432581#post1432581\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Hmm, I wonder what Spirit Shape you\u2019d want for this? Some kind of insect, maybe?</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah pretty much any insect or arachnid would work for natural armor and extra arms. I was tempted to say Mantis and also dip into Mantis style but the combination of Mantis + Crane isn't so hot without the Mastery on Iron-Arm Block.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2579,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2579-limaxophobiac","user":"limaxophobiac","date":". 01-23-2021, 08:53 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2579-limaxophobiac","name":"limaxophobiac","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"294"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-05T23:23:43-07:00","id":1447697,"title":"","content":"Hello all, I am sorry if this is necromancy but I was wondering if anyone has worked out a large crab lunar combat character?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1635-citadel97501","name":"Citadel97501","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"544"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-06T08:47:27-07:00","id":1447718,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Citadel97501</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1293395-ex-3-lunars-glorious-argent-beastiary-a-lunar-s-character-thread?p=1447697#post1447697\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hello all, I am sorry if this is necromancy but I was wondering if anyone has worked out a large crab lunar combat character?</div> </div> </div> </div>This is not... hard? Especially with the massive buff to Carapace, you can easily walk around with &quot;Only Exalts need apply&quot; levels of Soak. Then just rock up with the biggest meanest grimcleaver you have and Ma Ha Suchi's your uncle.<br /> <br /> Did you want it to have any cute tricks? Any obscure corner cases of the rules you'd like to exploit? Those I admittedly have some faculty with.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":8959,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8959-prototype00","user":"prototype00","date":". 05-06-2021, 11:54 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8959-prototype00","name":"prototype00","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8959_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"964"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-06T22:40:52-07:00","id":1447767,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>prototype00</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1293395-ex-3-lunars-glorious-argent-beastiary-a-lunar-s-character-thread?p=1447718#post1447718\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This is not... hard? Especially with the massive buff to Carapace, you can easily walk around with &quot;Only Exalts need apply&quot; levels of Soak. Then just rock up with the biggest meanest grimcleaver you have and Ma Ha Suchi's your uncle.<br /> <br /> Did you want it to have any cute tricks? Any obscure corner cases of the rules you'd like to exploit? Those I admittedly have some faculty with.</div> </div> </div> </div>I specifically was thinking for an animal form of a Large Crab as the combat form?<br /> <br /> So a crab is only really beneficial for super armor characters? There isn't a grapple build there even with the Grasping Claws for bonus damage?<br /> -How are you getting carapace on the crab all I can see is the Tell, or Chimera-Soul Expression? Or are you suggesting that we &quot;simply&quot; use a very powerful shape IE a Super Armored large crab shape that starts with Carapace 2 and Unusual Hide 5? This would give you a base armor of 18/5 with a Mobility penalty of 1, + any moon silver armor your wearing so capping out at about 29 armor not counting excellencies? Lets say you toss on Legendary Size and now you are basically immune from crash as I can't think of much that can do 39+ withering damage in one shot.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1635-citadel97501","name":"Citadel97501","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"544"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-06T23:04:53-07:00","id":1447769,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Citadel97501</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1293395-ex-3-lunars-glorious-argent-beastiary-a-lunar-s-character-thread?p=1447767#post1447767\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I specifically was thinking for an animal form of a Large Crab as the combat form?<br /> <br /> So a crab is only really beneficial for super armor characters? There isn't a grapple build there even with the Grasping Claws for bonus damage?<br /> -How are you getting carapace on the crab all I can see is the Tell, or Chimera-Soul Expression? Or are you suggesting that we &quot;simply&quot; use a very powerful shape IE a Super Armored large crab shape that starts with Carapace 2 and Unusual Hide 5? This would give you a base armor of 18/5 with a Mobility penalty of 1, + any moon silver armor your wearing so capping out at about 29 armor not counting excellencies? Lets say you toss on Legendary Size and now you are basically immune from crash as I can't think of much that can do 39+ withering damage in one shot.</div> </div> </div> </div>Okay, that\u2019s different. You\u2019re wanting an actual crab shape not a puissant HBT/DBT crab person.<br /> <br /> I gotta break it to you now, the extant crabs in the book are not the greatest, but I\u2019ll do what I can.<br /> <br /> 1. You can Chimera Soul on 6 points of mutations to your crab body, so that\u2019s Carapace 00 and Unusual Hide 0000. You can have Unusual hide 0 as a Tell mutation, but it\u2019s only two points more of Soak. So this gives you 10 Armored soak (that stacks with armor) if you take the whole shebang. Large crabs natively have a Soak of 8, so that\u2019s 18. If you were wearing Moonsilver Artifact armor, you have a base of around 28. (This is more than probably overkill)<br /> <br /> *Maui Impression* You\u2019re Welcome.<br /> <br /> 2.The Grapple side, there are a bunch of charms that enhance grapple, but I\u2019ll let you sort them out. If you just want to *win grapple* all the time, I\u2019d advise you be Crabzilla and take the Ess 2 charm Mountainous Spirit Expression which makes you Legendary size and you can auto win grapples against anything that isn\u2019t Solar Supernal Brawl, another Lunar running the same suite or a Warstrider. (And even then good odds)<br /> <br /> *Maui Encore* You\u2019re welcome again.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":8959,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8959-prototype00","user":"prototype00","date":". 05-07-2021, 02:26 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8959-prototype00","name":"prototype00","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8959_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"964"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-06T23:29:15-07:00","id":1447773,"title":"","content":"Thanks, I was also noting that there are some charms that just seem great for the Iron Skull Devil? Basically Relentless Monster Pursuit makes this disgusting with free initiative whenever you move to the guy you just smashed a zone? Here is 3 free initiative you can use to smash the guy again, &amp; again, or maybe even better just keep tossing him like a ragdoll gaining more and more initiative each time.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1635-citadel97501","name":"Citadel97501","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"544"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-07T00:11:32-07:00","id":1447777,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Citadel97501</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1293395-ex-3-lunars-glorious-argent-beastiary-a-lunar-s-character-thread?p=1447773#post1447773\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Thanks, I was also noting that there are some charms that just seem great for the Iron Skull Devil? Basically Relentless Monster Pursuit makes this disgusting with free initiative whenever you move to the guy you just smashed a zone? Here is 3 free initiative you can use to smash the guy again, &amp; again, or maybe even better just keep tossing him like a ragdoll gaining more and more initiative each time.</div> </div> </div> </div>It\u2019s cool, but seems a bit win more to me, you\u2019re already making Decisives against the guy to get him in that position, I\u2019d personally rather concentrate on the abilities that get you into that position.<br /> <br /> And aside from this neat trick, Iron Skull Devils really don\u2019t have much else going for them (poor soak, not top tier damage, etc). <br /> <br /> It\u2019s fine I suppose, not all Lunar have to be hippos.<br /> <br /> Edit: Nothing prevents you from resetting to base after Decisives with this animal, btw, so you\u2019re doing the punting trick once and then probably building up initiative again.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8959-prototype00","name":"prototype00","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8959_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"964"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-07T05:36:34-07:00","id":1447797,"title":"","content":"True, what got my attention is your resetting to base then closing for 3 more likely triggering it again...6 initiative, and a charm sounds like plenty to trigger 3+ decisive damage.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1635-citadel97501","name":"Citadel97501","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"544"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-04T06:48:48-07:00","id":1466638,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>prototype00</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1293395-ex-3-lunars-glorious-argent-beastiary-a-lunar-s-character-thread?p=1447777#post1447777\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Edit: Nothing prevents you from resetting to base after Decisives with this animal, btw, so you\u2019re doing the punting trick once and then probably building up initiative again.</div> </div> </div> </div>Hi <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8959-prototype00\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar8959_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"8959\" data-vbnamecard=\"8959\">prototype00</a> (and anyone else who is willing to think along!)<br /> <br /> I stalked the forums for a few days to find interesting (lunar) builds and saw a few of yours that roused my interest.<br /> <br /> Mostly the killer kitty variants and the maiden of the black claw spoke to me.<br /> <br /> <br /> I am now building a Lunar Changing Moon that tries to be a hybrid of those two builds themes(but there are some nonbo's since m.a. cannot be used by the housecat)<br /> <br /> So the goal of the build is to:<br /> <br /> (at CC)Be social fighter/assassin.<br /> (at CC)Leverage human shapes for their ties<br /> <br /> Later I'd like to invest in:<br /> (future): Increase guile and stealth (Dex and Man charms)<br /> (future): increase/manipulate join battle (perception charms)<br /> (future): get instill love rolls upon being intention read<br /> (future) Copies and fakes (dex swarm and app mirror charms)<br /> (futrure) project blame (and anima) on other characters (man charms)<br /> (future) Make hunts of animals useful through poisons (stam poison charms)<br /> (future): get wood dragons claw if ST allows for it to be used in Cat shape and with WVS charms).(perhaps get the invocations of spring razor as suggested in the black claw maiden build).<br /> (future) Build out to full WVS and BCS (and maybe laughing monster style, M.A.'s are so expensive though).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_description\">Code:</div> <pre class=\"bbcode_code notranslate\" style=\"max-height:calc(30 * 1.4rem + 2 * var(--bbcode-padding) + var(--h-scrollbar-allowance));\">&lt;spoiler&gt; Name: Alryss(a) Concept: Social Assassin Spirit Shape: Housecat (or butterfly, I'm tempted to get the butterfly if i'd also get the fluttering wings poison effect AND if somehow housecat does not bring enough utility with my build) Anima banner: Mothra wings (google mothra wings gif) &#91;B&#93;Attributes&#91;/B&#93; str 1 X dex 5 stam 2 cha 2 X man 5 X app 5 X per 2 int 3 wits 3 The idea is to max dex man app to get as high m.a. pools with guile bonusses appearance for the resolve penalty. Stam at 2 is to get closer to the poison charms requisites, favoured perception for later buying it up and getting charms. Wits only at 3 because Open palm caress kind of makes having amazing JB rolls a nonbo. &#91;B&#93;Abilities:&#91;/B&#93; I'm really struggling to get all the points i'd want. Ath 1 Aware 1 brawl 1 (I know, this is atrocious for fighting in animal (including cat) shape. But I really do not know where to take points away to have this higher, also i'm focussing on battling in human shape so there's that too). dodge 3 Integrity 1 Investig 1 Larceny 3 Presence 3 Resistance 1 Socialize 5 Stealth 3 M.A. (BCS) 5 M.A. (WVS) 5 The 1's are hygiene abilities, the 3 are the important abilities with the 5's being abilities that either give guile or open up the m.a. charms. &#91;B&#93;Merits&#91;/B&#93;: Tell: Unusual Hide 5, Imposing Features 2, pheromones 1 (love, humans). This represents beautiful fur that also smells amazing and is very strong (not sure how to represent the unusual hide 5, maybe it's made of white glass or porcelin or something.) The idea here is to enhance my social combat in all (human) shapes. I'm not just in someone's shape, i'm the slightly more awesome version. Mentor (for the m.a.'s) 1 Martial Artists 4 &#91;B&#93;Charms:&#91;/B&#93; Black Claw Style up to form charm (4) White Claw Style up to Alehouse Memory Stance (3) Subtle Silver Delcaration and Moon's hidden face (to hide the mutations when not in use) Memory Drinking Meditation (get info with shapes) Agile Beast Defense and Bending before the storm (additional defense package, also prerequisites for cunning anglerfish decoy, which i'd like to pick up early). Skulking Rat Spirit: extra bonusses to stealth, both good for cat form stealthing and WVS, also prereq for cunning anglerfish decoy). Many Faced Moon Transformation: to aid with disguising, maybe to help hide mutations when in use (like imposing features, i'd like to have the manes be just extremely beautiful hair in human shapes). Nest Raiding Slyness (I'm between this and heart rending alure for my non-lethal shape taking. This one seems easier to satisfy early on and also can take animal shapes easier then the other one). I will start out with just my human shape and my spirit shape (cat) because I think the journey of getting more shapes is more interesting than already having the full package. &lt;/spoiler&gt;</pre> </div>Questions:<br /> <br /> 1 Any suggestions to increase the build at CC, also are there any tricks I missed for a social assassin?<br /> <br /> 2 I do not have game experience with 3rd edition yet so I'm not sure if i'm going over dice-caps or if there are other things that are nonbo-ing tremendously.<br /> - One thing I feel is I'm extremely invested in defence but that's partly also because I want to get to cunning anglerfish decoy. I could drop the dex package in favour of the manipulation line that leads up to cunning anglerfish decoy, but the dex package works in animals shapes and seems really good so I would only do that if the BCS and WVS package makes the dex package useless.<br /> <br /> 3 I could not get to terrestial circle sorcery with my charms (four mental charms, I took a lot of perc charms initially, but it does not do so much at CC). This means I will not have wood dragon claw<br /> at the beginning. Are there alternative packages for offence that would work in human shapes as well as animal shapes and work with the m.a. styles?<br /> <br /> 4 one route I could see is to drop the mutation package and the hide mutations charm package. I could still get to Essential Mirror Nature through manipulation charms (which would incidentily avoid shifting penumbra stance, which i find lacking). Not sure if this is smart since unusual hide is going to be our main source of soak in the early game and the social mutations are nice bonuses. It does open up 5 points of merits, 3bp's and two charms (although I guess I might want subtle silver declaration at some point anyway?). I could take artefact armour but it conflicts with my m.a.'s and silk armor is not moonsilver.<br /> <br /> 5 one other thing i'm worried about is that i'll be quite combat focussed at cc and it will take me a while to get more utility charms up and running (but all of those will make my combat suite better simultaniously).<br /> <br /> 6 the housecat package is limited by my lack of points to get brawl to 5, and also I'm not sure if getting it will make it useless to go human shapes + m.a.. What I mean is, it's kinda either cat shape or m.a. and human shape and it seems hard to find things that help both. I do like the cat shape a lot for cuddling up to people and sneaking around so I'll want it anyway. <br /> <br /> Any advice anyone can share is more than welcome.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27166-reficulris","name":"Reficulris","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-21T08:50:47-07:00","id":1509195,"title":"","content":"Just going to throw this here, since I didn't find an answer after reading Fangs at the Gate and search through forums doesn't yield results. Also don't want to make new thread just for this and since this thread goes close enough...<br /> <br /> Anyone got an idea WHAT is Amatha Kinslayer's Spirit shape?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11221-turtleking","name":"Turtleking","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-09-18T21:40:43-07:00","id":1522775,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Turtleking</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1293395-ex-3-lunars-glorious-argent-beastiary-a-lunar-s-character-thread?p=1509195#post1509195\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Just going to throw this here, since I didn't find an answer after reading Fangs at the Gate and search through forums doesn't yield results. Also don't want to make new thread just for this and since this thread goes close enough...<br /> <br /> Anyone got an idea WHAT is Amatha Kinslayer's Spirit shape?</div> </div> </div> </div>There was a character in one of my Exalted games who had Amatha's backstory almost exactly, and her Spirit Shape was a hyena, so that's what I've gone with. I've just retconned later appearances of that character to be that she's actually Amatha Kinslayer, having used one of her many aliases when she met the original party.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr />&quot;The true object of all human life is play. Earth is a task garden; heaven is a playground.&quot; -G.K. Chesterton","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/53-blackwingedheaven","name":"blackwingedheaven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar53_3.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"351"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-08T11:58:24-08:00","id":1532248,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>prototype00</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1293395-ex-3-lunars-glorious-argent-beastiary-a-lunar-s-character-thread?p=1432581#post1432581\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Hmm, I wonder what Spirit Shape you\u2019d want for this? Some kind of insect, maybe?</div> </div> </div> </div>The Giant Centipede should fit perfectly.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>When will you rage?","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1405-anteros","name":"Anteros","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1405_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"661"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}